window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD && window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD("0056", [{"word":"intellectually","ipa_uk":"/ˌɪntəˈlektʃuəli/","ipa_us":"/ˌɪntəˈlektʃuəli/","definition_zh":"智力上；在认知层面；理智地；以显得有学识的方式","definition_en":"in a way that involves or relates to the intellect; mentally, by reasoning rather than feeling, or in a manner that shows knowledge and thought","core_image":"书房里一盏亮着的台灯：头脑像灯一样把看不清的问题照亮","scene":"论文研讨会上，教授指着投影上的数据说，这项发现在认知层面很重要，但还需要实验验证。The result is intellectually important, but it still needs experimental work.","sceneCN":"这里 intellectually 是「在智力、认知层面上」（第 1 个义项：与思考、理解有关）；句意：这项结果在认知层面很重要，但仍需要实验验证。","pos":[{"tag":"adv.","zh":"智力上；在思维层面（修饰形容词或动词，说明判断所依据的层面）"},{"tag":"adv.","zh":"理智地；显得有学识地（修饰行为方式，与情绪化、随意相对）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"intellectually demanding","zh":"对智力要求很高的"},{"phrase":"intellectually stimulating","zh":"令人思维活跃的；启发智力的"},{"phrase":"intellectually curious","zh":"求知欲强的；爱动脑筋的"},{"phrase":"intellectually honest","zh":"思想上诚实的；不回避反证的"},{"phrase":"intellectually disabled","zh":"智力上有障碍的"},{"phrase":"intellectually rigorous","zh":"思维严谨的"}],"forms":[{"label":"副词原级","form":"intellectually"},{"label":"比较级（少见，用于对比程度）","form":"more intellectually"},{"label":"最高级（少见，用于对比程度）","form":"most intellectually"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"intellectual","pos":"adj./n.","zh":"智力的；知识分子"},{"word":"intellect","pos":"n.","zh":"智力；才智"},{"word":"intelligence","pos":"n.","zh":"智力；理解力；情报"},{"word":"intelligent","pos":"adj.","zh":"聪明的；有理解力的"},{"word":"intelligible","pos":"adj.","zh":"可理解的；明白易懂的"},{"word":"intellectualism","pos":"n.","zh":"智性主义；重理智的倾向"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"In terms of mental capacity","titleCN":"在智力、认知能力层面","definition":"with respect to the mind and its ability to understand, reason, and learn","definitionCN":"就头脑及其理解、推理与学习的能力而言","example":"The puzzle is intellectually demanding but not physically tiring.","exampleCN":"这个谜题对智力要求很高，但体力上并不累。","why":"Intellectually is the adverb of intellectual, from Latin intellectualis, from intellectus, the past participle of intelligere 'to understand'. The -ly adverb names the domain in which something is judged, so the word answers the question 'on what level?' — the level of the mind.","whyCN":"intellectually 是 intellectual 的副词，后者源自拉丁语 intellectualis，而 intellectualis 又来自 intelligere“理解”的过去分词 intellectus。-ly 副词命名判断所处的领域，所以这个词回答的是“在哪一层面上”——头脑的层面。"},{"no":"02","title":"By reasoning, not by feeling","titleCN":"凭理性而非情感","definition":"in a way that appeals to logic and evidence rather than to emotion or instinct","definitionCN":"诉诸逻辑与证据，而不是情绪或本能","example":"She approached the dispute intellectually, listing facts before feelings.","exampleCN":"她以理性的方式处理争执，先摆事实，再谈感受。","why":"Latin intelligere joins inter- 'between' and legere 'to pick, choose': understanding is picking out what lies between things. That image of selection is why the adverb can contrast with emotion — reasoning selects, feeling does not.","whyCN":"拉丁语 intelligere 由 inter-“在……之间”和 legere“挑选、选择”组成：理解就是从诸多事物之间挑出关键。正是这种“挑选”的意象，使这个副词能与情感相对——推理在挑选，情绪则不。"},{"no":"03","title":"In a learned or thoughtful manner","titleCN":"以有学识、有思想的方式","definition":"in a manner that shows knowledge, cultivation, and serious thought","definitionCN":"表现出知识修养与认真思考的方式","example":"The interview was conducted intellectually, with references to primary sources.","exampleCN":"这场访谈进行得很有学识，援引了原始文献。","why":"The adjective intellectual in English since the fourteenth century named both the faculty and the person who cultivates it. The adverb inherits this social meaning: doing something intellectually signals membership in a world of books and argument.","whyCN":"intellectual 自 14 世纪起在英语中既指心智能力，也指修养这种能力的人。副词继承了这个社会含义：以 intellectually 行事，等于表明自己属于读书与论辩的世界。"},{"no":"04","title":"Relating to academic work","titleCN":"在学术研究层面","definition":"with respect to scholarship, research, or formal study rather than practical application","definitionCN":"就学术、研究或正规学习而言，而非实际应用","example":"The project is intellectually valuable even though it has no commercial use yet.","exampleCN":"这个项目即使尚无商业用途，在学术上仍有价值。","why":"Universities separated the intellectual life from manual and commercial life, and the adverb became a way to mark that separation. 'Intellectually valuable' means valuable to knowledge itself, not to a market.","whyCN":"大学把智识生活与手工、商业生活区分开来，这个副词于是成为标记这种区分的手段。intellectually valuable 意为“对知识本身有价值”，而不是对市场有价值。"},{"no":"05","title":"In abstract rather than practical terms","titleCN":"从抽象思考而非实操角度","definition":"in terms of ideas and theory rather than hands-on practice","definitionCN":"就观念与理论而言，而不是动手实践","example":"He understood the machine intellectually but could not repair it.","exampleCN":"他在道理上懂这台机器，却不会修。","why":"This sense draws the same line as sense 4, but inside one person: knowledge may exist in the head without reaching the hands. The adverb marks that gap, which is why it often appears in sentences of contrast.","whyCN":"这个义项与第 4 个义项划的是同一条线，只是落在一个人身上：知识停在头脑里，没有到手上去。副词标记的正是这道缝隙，因此常出现在对比句里。"},{"no":"06","title":"As mental stimulation","titleCN":"作为精神上的启发","definition":"as a source of mental interest, challenge, or enjoyment","definitionCN":"作为思维趣味、挑战或愉悦的来源","example":"The seminar was intellectually refreshing after a week of routine work.","exampleCN":"在经历了整周例行工作后，这场研讨会在思维上令人耳目一新。","why":"English often pairs the adverb with adjectives of pleasure — stimulating, satisfying, rewarding — because the intellect is treated as a faculty that can be fed or starved. The adverb then names the kind of pleasure involved.","whyCN":"英语常把这个副词与表示愉悦的形容词搭配——stimulating、satisfying、rewarding——因为智力被当作一种可以被喂养或挨饿的能力。副词于是命名了愉悦的种类。"},{"no":"07","title":"Through the intellect in philosophy","titleCN":"哲学上通过理智认识","definition":"by means of the intellect, as opposed to the senses or the will, in philosophical usage","definitionCN":"哲学用语中，凭借理智而非感官或意志去认识","example":"Aquinas held that some truths are grasped intellectually rather than through images.","exampleCN":"阿奎那认为有些真理是靠理智而非靠形象把握的。","why":"Medieval scholastics distinguished intellectus, the faculty of immediate understanding, from ratio, step-by-step reasoning. The English adverb preserves this technical contrast, so 'intellectually' can mean 'by intellectual intuition', not merely 'by thinking'.","whyCN":"中世纪经院哲学把 intellectus（直接理解的能力）与 ratio（逐步推理）区分开来。英语副词保留了这个术语性对立，因此 intellectually 可以指“靠智性直观”，而不只是“靠思考”。"},{"no":"08","title":"In terms of mental development","titleCN":"在智力发展意义上","definition":"with regard to the growth or training of the mind, especially in education","definitionCN":"就心智的成长或训练而言，尤用于教育","example":"Children benefit intellectually from reading aloud with an adult.","exampleCN":"儿童与成人一起朗读，在智力发展上受益匪浅。","why":"Nineteenth-century educational writing turned the adjective into a measure of growth: a child is 'intellectually ready' for a task. The adverb here shifts from describing a level to describing a trajectory — the mind moving forward.","whyCN":"19 世纪的教育写作把这个形容词变成衡量成长的尺度：一个孩子在智力上“准备好”做某项任务。这里的副词从描述水平转为描述轨迹——心智在向前走。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Intellectually is a transparent English adverb: intellectual plus -ly. Intellectual goes back through Latin intellectualis to intellectus, the noun of intelligere 'to understand', built on inter- 'between' and legere 'to pick, choose'.","cn":"intellectually 是透明的英语副词：intellectual 加 -ly。intellectual 经拉丁语 intellectualis 上溯至 intellectus，即 intelligere“理解”的名词，由 inter-“在……之间”与 legere“挑选、选择”构成。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Latin legere meant 'to pick out, gather, read', and inter- meant 'between'. Intelligere therefore pictured understanding as picking the right item out of what lies between many things. Its noun intellectus named both the faculty and its act.","cn":"拉丁语 legere 意为“挑出、收集、阅读”，inter- 意为“在……之间”。因此 intelligere 把理解描绘成从众多事物之间挑出正确的那一项。其名词 intellectus 既指这种能力，也指它的活动。"},{"era":"LATIN / MEDIEVAL","en":"Intellectualis 'of the understanding' was used by medieval scholastics to mark the intellectual virtues, distinct from moral ones. The word entered Old French as intellectuel and then English in the fourteenth century.","cn":"intellectualis“属于理解的”被中世纪经院学者用来标记智性德性，以区别于道德德性。该词经古法语 intellectuel 于 14 世纪进入英语。"},{"era":"14C. ENGLISH","en":"English intellectual first appears as an adjective meaning 'grasped by the intellect', and soon also as a noun for a person devoted to learning. The -ly adverb is formed on the adjective in the usual English way.","cn":"英语 intellectual 最早作为形容词出现，义为“凭理智把握的”，很快又作名词指致力于学问的人。-ly 副词按英语常规由该形容词构成。"},{"era":"17C–18C.","en":"Enlightenment writing made the adverb a standard label for the life of reason: 'intellectually convinced', 'intellectually honest'. The contrast with emotion and with manual labour was fixed in this period.","cn":"启蒙运动的写作使这个副词成为理性生活的标准标签：intellectually convinced、intellectually honest。与情感、与体力劳动的对立在这一时期固定下来。"},{"era":"19C. EDUCATION","en":"Educational and psychological texts extended the adverb to development, producing phrases such as 'intellectually ready' and 'intellectually gifted'. The word became part of the vocabulary of assessment.","cn":"教育与心理学文本把这个副词扩展到发展领域，产生了 intellectually ready、intellectually gifted 等说法。该词成为评估用语的一部分。"},{"era":"20C.–PRESENT","en":"Modern usage keeps both the everyday sense 'mentally' and the formal sense 'by reasoning'. The phrase 'intellectually disabled' shows how neutral technical language absorbed the older adjective.","cn":"现代用法同时保留日常义“在头脑上”和正式义“凭推理”。intellectually disabled 这一说法显示了中性的技术语言如何吸收了这个旧形容词。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates words built on the same Latin verb intelligere but with different formations; the near-meaning group separates adverbs of mental activity.","cn":"形近组区分建立在同一拉丁动词 intelligere 之上但构词方式不同的词；近义组区分表示心智活动的副词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"intelligent","ipa":"/ɪnˈtelɪdʒənt/","tag":"same verb, present-participle formation","definition":"having good mental ability. It comes from intelligens, the present participle of intelligere, so it describes a person's capacity rather than an academic domain.","definitionCN":"具有良好心智能力的。它来自 intelligere 的现在分词 intelligens，因此描述人的能力，而不是学术领域。"},{"word":"intelligible","ipa":"/ɪnˈtelɪdʒəbl/","tag":"same verb, -ible formation","definition":"able to be understood. Latin intelligibilis named what the intellect can grasp; it describes clarity of content, not the act of using the mind.","definitionCN":"可被理解的。拉丁语 intelligibilis 指理智能够把握的东西，它描述内容的清晰，而不是运用心智的行为。"},{"word":"intellectualism","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈlektʃuəlɪzəm/","tag":"same root, abstract noun","definition":"the tendency to rely on reasoning or to prize intellectual pursuits. It names a doctrine, not a level at which something is judged.","definitionCN":"倚重推理或推崇智识追求的倾向。它命名一种主张，而不是判断所处层面。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"mentally","ipa":"/ˈmentəli/","tag":"neutral","definition":"in the mind. It is the plain neutral adverb, from Latin mens 'mind'; intellectually is more formal and usually implies cultivated reasoning.","definitionCN":"在头脑中。它是最朴素的中性副词，来自拉丁语 mens“心智”；intellectually 更正式，通常暗示受过训练的推理。"},{"word":"rationally","ipa":"/ˈræʃənəli/","tag":"method","definition":"by logical reasoning. It stresses the correctness of the method, while intellectually stresses the faculty that is being used.","definitionCN":"以合乎逻辑的方式。它强调方法正确，而 intellectually 强调所使用的能力。"},{"word":"academically","ipa":"/ˌækəˈdemɪkli/","tag":"institution","definition":"with respect to formal education or scholarship. It points to schools and grades; intellectually points to the mind itself, whether or not a school is involved.","definitionCN":"就正规教育或学术而言。它指向学校与成绩；intellectually 指向头脑本身，无论是否涉及学校。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real associations: the Latin pair inter- 'between' + legere 'pick', the living adverb suffix -ly, and the fixed educational phrase 'intellectually demanding'.","cn":"真实联想：拉丁语 inter-“在……之间”+ legere“挑选”这一对成分、活的副词后缀 -ly，以及教育领域的固定说法 intellectually demanding。"},"normal":[{"en":"inter- means 'between' and legere means 'pick': to understand is to pick the right item out of many.","cn":"inter- 意为“在……之间”，legere 意为“挑选”：理解就是从众多事物中挑出正确的那一项。"},{"en":"intellectual is the adjective and -ly turns it into 'in the manner of the intellect'.","cn":"intellectual 是形容词，-ly 把它变成“以智力的方式”。"},{"en":"'Intellectually demanding' is the standard phrase for work that tires the mind, not the body.","cn":"intellectually demanding 是形容“累脑不累身”的工作的标准说法。"},{"en":"The word appears in the phrase 'intellectually honest', meaning willing to follow evidence against one's own opinion.","cn":"这个词出现在 intellectually honest 中，意为愿意顺着证据走、哪怕违背自己的看法。"},{"en":"In philosophy it contrasts with 'sensibly': what is known intellectually is known without images.","cn":"在哲学中它与 sensibly 相对：靠 intellect 认识的东西不带形象。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Light on a page is the right picture: the intellect does not create the text, it makes what is already there readable.","cn":"书页上的一盏灯是最贴切的画面：智性不创造文本，它让已经在那里的东西变得可读。"},{"en":"The adverb never names a quantity of knowledge, only the level at which something is judged — mind rather than hand or heart.","cn":"这个副词从不命名知识的多少，只命名判断所处的层面——头脑，而不是手或心。"},{"en":"Because the root means 'pick between', every intellectual act is also a choice, and the word quietly carries that responsibility.","cn":"因为词根意为“在之间挑”，每一个智性行为同时也是一次选择，这个词悄悄承载着这份责任。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The debate was intellectually serious but emotionally cold.","cn":"这场辩论在智识上很严肃，但情感上很冷淡。"},{"en":"Students who are intellectually curious tend to read beyond the syllabus.","cn":"求知欲强的学生往往会读教学大纲之外的书。"},{"en":"She was intellectually convinced by the argument long before she accepted it emotionally.","cn":"她在理智上早就被这个论证说服，情感上却很久才接受。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因特来者可挑”——在众多说法之间挑出可用的那一条，靠的是智力 → intellectually 智力上、凭理性","word":"intellectually"},"root":"inter-（在……之间）+ 拉丁语 legere“挑选、读”+ -ual + -ly；单个词根义为“在之间挑出”，核心是“凭智性去分辨与判断”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of intellectually all locate an act on the level of the mind: reasoning, studying, understanding theory, enjoying mental challenge, or growing in capacity. The word never describes what is known, only how or where it is known.","cn":"intellectually 的八个义项都把某个行为定位在头脑这一层面：推理、治学、理解理论、享受思维挑战或在能力上成长。这个词从不描述所知的内容，只描述认知的方式与层面。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a lamp over an open book; the light does not write, it makes what is written legible.","cn":"核心意象：一本摊开的书上悬着一盏灯；灯不写字，它让写好的字变得可读。"},"chain":["MIND","SELECTION","UNDERSTANDING","REASON","KNOWLEDGE","JUDGEMENT"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S7","en":"FACULTY: the mind as a capacity, both in everyday use and in the scholastic contrast between intellectus and ratio.","cn":"能力：作为能力的头脑，既见于日常用法，也见于经院哲学中 intellectus 与 ratio 的对立。"},{"senses":"S2 · S3","en":"MANNER: reasoning instead of feeling, and behaving in a way that displays cultivation.","cn":"方式：以推理代替情感，以及以显示修养的方式行事。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"DOMAIN: scholarship and abstract theory, set apart from commerce and from hands-on practice.","cn":"领域：学术与抽象理论，与商业和动手实践相区隔。"},{"senses":"S6","en":"PLEASURE: the mind as something that can be stimulated, refreshed, or starved.","cn":"愉悦：头脑作为可被激发、被刷新或挨饿的东西。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"GROWTH: education measures the mind as a trajectory rather than a fixed level.","cn":"成长：教育把心智看作一条轨迹，而不是固定水平。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Intellectually is intellectual + -ly, and intellectual is Latin intellectualis from intellectus. The affix set mixes English derivatives of intellect with the Latin verb intelligere and its participles.","cn":"intellectually 是 intellectual + -ly，而 intellectual 是拉丁语 intellectualis，源自 intellectus。词缀组混合了 intellect 的英语派生词与拉丁动词 intelligere 及其分词形式。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin family clusters around intelligere 'to understand': intellectus 'understanding', intellectualis 'of the understanding', intelligens 'understanding (participle)', intelligibilis 'able to be understood'. All keep the inter- + legere structure.","cn":"这一拉丁词族围绕 intelligere“理解”：intellectus“理解”、intellectualis“属于理解的”、intelligens“理解的（分词）”、intelligibilis“可被理解的”。它们都保留 inter- + legere 的结构。"},"items":[{"word":"intellectually","structure":"intellectual + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in a mental or reasoned manner","meaningCN":"智力上；凭理性地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The task is intellectually rewarding.","exampleCN":"这项任务在智力上很有收获。"},{"word":"intellectual","structure":"Latin intellectualis, from intellectus + -alis","meaning":"relating to the intellect; a person devoted to ideas","meaningCN":"智力的；知识分子（intellectus + -alis）","example":"The book had a strong intellectual influence.","exampleCN":"这本书产生了很强的思想影响。"},{"word":"intellect","structure":"Latin intellectus 'understanding'","meaning":"the power of reasoning and understanding","meaningCN":"智力；理解力（直接借自拉丁名词）","example":"Her intellect was never in doubt.","exampleCN":"她的才智从未受到怀疑。"},{"word":"intelligence","structure":"Latin intelligentia + -ence","meaning":"the capacity to learn and understand; gathered information","meaningCN":"智力；情报（intelligentia + -ence，兼有“收集信息”义）","example":"Tests measure only part of intelligence.","exampleCN":"测验只测量智力的一部分。"},{"word":"intelligent","structure":"Latin intelligens, present participle of intelligere","meaning":"having good understanding; showing thought","meaningCN":"聪明的；有见地的（intelligere 的现在分词）","example":"That was an intelligent reply.","exampleCN":"那是一个有见地的回答。"},{"word":"intelligible","structure":"Latin intelligibilis + -ible","meaning":"clear enough to be understood","meaningCN":"可理解的；明白易懂的（intelligibilis + -ible）","example":"The recording is barely intelligible.","exampleCN":"这段录音几乎听不清。"},{"word":"intellectualism","structure":"intellectual + -ism","meaning":"the habit or doctrine of relying on reasoning","meaningCN":"智性主义；重理智的倾向（-ism 表主张）","example":"His intellectualism made him impatient with small talk.","exampleCN":"他的智性倾向让他对闲聊不耐烦。"},{"word":"intellectualize","structure":"intellectual + -ize","meaning":"to treat something in abstract, reasoned terms","meaningCN":"使抽象化；以理性方式处理（-ize 表使动）","example":"He tends to intellectualize his own feelings.","exampleCN":"他往往把自己的感受理性化。"},{"word":"unintellectual","structure":"un- + intellectual","meaning":"not concerned with ideas or reasoning","meaningCN":"非智识的；不重思考的（un- 表否定）","example":"The show is deliberately unintellectual.","exampleCN":"这个节目刻意不走智识路线。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"intellegere / intelligere","structure":"inter- 'between' + legere 'pick, choose'","meaning":"to understand, perceive","meaningCN":"理解；领悟"},{"word":"intellectus","structure":"fourth-declension noun from intelligere","meaning":"understanding, intellect","meaningCN":"理解；智力"},{"word":"intellectualis","structure":"intellectus + -alis","meaning":"of the understanding","meaningCN":"属于理解的"},{"word":"intelligibilis","structure":"intelligere + -ibilis","meaning":"able to be understood","meaningCN":"可被理解的"}]}},{"word":"interaction","ipa_uk":"/ˌɪntərˈækʃn/","ipa_us":"/ˌɪntərˈækʃn/","definition_zh":"相互作用；互动；交流；（药物）相互作用；（物理）相互作用","definition_en":"the process by which two or more people, organisms, substances, or forces act on one another and produce effects on each other","core_image":"两支箭头从两边出发、在中间相遇并折返：力在同一个点上交换","scene":"生态课上，研究员在水槽两侧放入两种鱼。The interaction between the two species decides who eats whom.","sceneCN":"这里 interaction 是「相互作用」（第 1 个义项：两方彼此施加影响）；句意：两种鱼之间的相互作用决定了谁吃谁。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"相互作用；互动（可数指一次具体的互动，不可数指互动过程）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（专业）相互作用：药物、粒子、生态等领域的固定术语（常带修饰语）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"social interaction","zh":"社会互动；社交"},{"phrase":"human-computer interaction","zh":"人机交互"},{"phrase":"drug interaction","zh":"药物相互作用"},{"phrase":"interaction between A and B","zh":"A 与 B 之间的相互作用"},{"phrase":"face-to-face interaction","zh":"面对面互动"},{"phrase":"positive interaction","zh":"积极的互动"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"interaction"},{"label":"复数","form":"interactions"},{"label":"作定语（名词修饰名词）","form":"interaction design"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"interact","pos":"v.","zh":"互动；相互作用"},{"word":"interactive","pos":"adj.","zh":"互动的；交互式的"},{"word":"interactively","pos":"adv.","zh":"以互动的方式"},{"word":"interactivity","pos":"n.","zh":"互动性"},{"word":"interactional","pos":"adj.","zh":"互动过程的；交互的"},{"word":"interactionism","pos":"n.","zh":"互动论（社会学、心理学理论）"},{"word":"interactant","pos":"n.","zh":"互动参与者"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Mutual action between two parties","titleCN":"两方之间的相互影响","definition":"the process in which two or more things or people affect each other","definitionCN":"两个或更多事物、人彼此影响的过程","example":"The interaction between climate and soil shapes what can grow there.","exampleCN":"气候与土壤之间的相互作用决定了那里能长什么。","why":"Interaction is an English coinage of the nineteenth century: inter- 'between' + action, from Latin agere 'to do'. The word does not describe a one-way effect but a loop — each party's action is both cause and response.","whyCN":"interaction 是 19 世纪英语的创造：inter-“在……之间”+ action，而 action 源自拉丁语 agere“做”。这个词描述的不是单向作用，而是一个回路——每一方的行动既是原因也是回应。"},{"no":"02","title":"Communication between people","titleCN":"人与人之间的交流互动","definition":"the exchange of words, gestures, or signals between people and the responses these produce","definitionCN":"人与人之间言语、手势或信号的交换以及由此产生的回应","example":"Good teamwork depends on frequent, honest interaction.","exampleCN":"良好的团队合作依赖频繁而坦诚的互动。","why":"The social sense narrows the loop to human signals: one person speaks, the other answers, and the answer changes the next move. This is why the word is preferred over 'communication' when both directions matter.","whyCN":"社会义把这个回路收窄到人的信号：一人说话，另一人回应，而回应又改变下一步。正因为两个方向都重要，人们才宁可用 interaction 而不是 communication。"},{"no":"03","title":"Drug interaction","titleCN":"药物相互作用","definition":"the effect that one drug or substance has on the activity of another when both are taken together","definitionCN":"两种药物或物质同时使用时，一种对另一种活性的影响","example":"The label warns of a dangerous interaction with alcohol.","exampleCN":"标签警告与酒精同时使用会产生危险的相互作用。","why":"Pharmacology borrowed the general noun in the twentieth century and fixed it in the compound 'drug interaction'. The image is still the loop: substance A changes how B is absorbed, and B changes what A does.","whyCN":"药理学在 20 世纪借用了这个普通名词，并固定在 drug interaction 这一复合说法中。意象仍是回路：物质 A 改变 B 的吸收，B 又改变 A 的作用。"},{"no":"04","title":"Interaction of physical forces","titleCN":"物理上的相互作用","definition":"a force or influence that particles, fields, or bodies exert on one another","definitionCN":"粒子、场或物体彼此施加的力或影响","example":"Physicists describe the interaction of electrons and photons with quantum field theory.","exampleCN":"物理学家用量子场论描述电子与光子的相互作用。","why":"In physics the word became a technical term for the fundamental forces: electromagnetic, strong, weak, gravitational. The Latin agere 'to do' survives literally — one particle acts, the other is acted upon.","whyCN":"在物理学中，这个词成为基本作用力的术语：电磁、强、弱、引力。拉丁语 agere“做”字面保留——一个粒子施动，另一个受动。"},{"no":"05","title":"Ecological interaction","titleCN":"生态相互作用","definition":"a relationship between species, such as predation, competition, or mutualism, that affects their survival","definitionCN":"物种之间的关系，如捕食、竞争或互利，影响其生存","example":"The interaction between bees and flowers benefits both partners.","exampleCN":"蜜蜂与花朵之间的相互作用使双方都受益。","why":"Ecology uses the noun for relationships that persist over time: each species is part of the other's environment. The word's two-directional structure fits a system in which nothing acts alone.","whyCN":"生态学用这个名词指长期持续的关系：每个物种都是另一个物种环境的一部分。这个词的双向结构正好适合一个没有谁能单独行动的系统。"},{"no":"06","title":"Social contact in general","titleCN":"一般意义上的社会交往","definition":"ordinary contact and dealings among people, especially as a normal part of daily life","definitionCN":"人们之间日常的接触与往来，尤指作为日常生活的一部分","example":"Older residents value the daily interaction with neighbours.","exampleCN":"年长居民看重与邻居的日常往来。","why":"When the word means mere contact, the emphasis moves from effects to frequency: it is the ongoing business of meeting, talking, and trading. This sense is close to 'social life' and is often uncountable.","whyCN":"当这个词只指接触时，重点从效果转到频率：它是持续不断的见面、交谈与往来事务。这个义项接近 social life，且常作不可数。"},{"no":"07","title":"Human-computer interaction","titleCN":"人机交互","definition":"the study and practice of how people use and respond to computer systems","definitionCN":"研究并实践人如何使用计算机系统以及系统如何回应人","example":"The app was redesigned after a human-computer interaction study.","exampleCN":"经过人机交互研究后，这款应用被重新设计。","why":"This is the newest sense, coined in computing in the 1980s. The machine is treated as a partner in the loop: the user acts, the interface answers, and the answer shapes the next action.","whyCN":"这是最新的义项，1980 年代在计算机领域创造。机器被当作回路中的伙伴：用户操作，界面回应，回应又塑造下一步行动。"},{"no":"08","title":"Classroom interaction","titleCN":"课堂互动","definition":"the exchange between teacher and students or among students during a lesson","definitionCN":"课堂上师生之间或学生之间的交流","example":"The lesson plan allots ten minutes for small-group interaction.","exampleCN":"教案安排了十分钟的小组互动。","why":"Educational research adopted the word to describe turn-taking in class, because learning is treated as something built in exchange rather than delivered one way. The term measures participation, not merely attendance.","whyCN":"教育研究采用这个词描述课堂上的轮次交替，因为学习被视为在交流中建构，而不是单向传递。这个术语衡量的是参与，而不只是出勤。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Interaction is an English compound noun: inter- 'between' plus action, which comes from Latin actio and the verb agere 'to do, drive'. It is not a Latin word but a modern formation that kept its parts transparent.","cn":"interaction 是英语复合名词：inter-“在……之间”加 action，而 action 源自拉丁语 actio 与动词 agere“做、驱动”。它不是拉丁语词，而是保留了各成分透明度的现代构词。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Latin agere meant 'to do, drive, set in motion'; its supine actum and noun actio gave the sense of a completed deed. Inter- meant 'between, among'.","cn":"拉丁语 agere 意为“做、驱动、使动”；其目的动名词 actum 与名词 actio 给出“已完成的行为”之义。inter- 意为“在……之间、在……之中”。"},{"era":"14C.–17C. ENGLISH","en":"English took action from Old French action, derived from actio. For several centuries the word stayed one-directional: someone acts, something is done.","cn":"英语经古法语 action 借入 action，其源头为 actio。数百年间这个词都是单向的：某人行动，某事被做。"},{"era":"1832","en":"Interaction is recorded in the 1830s as a term of natural philosophy for reciprocal action. The new prefix inter- turned the one-way deed into a loop, a coinage rather than an inheritance.","cn":"interaction 于 1830 年代被记录，作为自然哲学中表示“相互作用的”术语。新加的前缀 inter- 把单向行为变成回路，这是新造词而非继承词。"},{"era":"19C.–20C. SCIENCE","en":"Physics, chemistry, and later ecology standardized the noun in phrases such as 'interaction of forces'. Each field needed a word for effects that cannot be assigned to one side only.","cn":"物理学、化学以及后来的生态学把这个名词固定在 interaction of forces 等说法中。每个领域都需要一个词，来描述无法只归因于一方的影响。"},{"era":"20C. SOCIAL AND COMPUTING","en":"Sociology and psychology extended interaction to human exchange, and computing coined 'human-computer interaction' in the 1980s. The same two-party loop now includes machines.","cn":"社会学与心理学把 interaction 扩展到人的交流，计算机领域则在 1980 年代创造 human-computer interaction。同一个双方回路从此把机器也包含在内。"},{"era":"PRESENT","en":"Modern dictionaries treat the noun as fully general, with technical compounds for drugs, species, particles, and interfaces. All of them keep the original shape: two parties, one shared point of action.","cn":"现代词典把这个名词视为完全通用的词，并配有药物、物种、粒子、界面等专业复合词。它们都保留原本形态：两方，一个共同的作用点。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates nouns in inter- that come from different Latin verbs; the near-meaning group separates words for two-way exchange.","cn":"形近组区分以 inter- 开头但来自不同拉丁动词的名词；近义组区分表示双向交换的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"integration","ipa":"/ˌɪntɪˈɡreɪʃn/","tag":"different root: integrare 'make whole'","definition":"the combining of parts into a whole. It comes from Latin integrare 'to make whole', not from agere 'to do'; the two words share only the prefix.","definitionCN":"把部分组合成整体。它源自拉丁语 integrare“使完整”，而非 agere“做”；两词只共享前缀。"},{"word":"intention","ipa":"/ɪnˈtenʃn/","tag":"different root: intendere 'stretch toward'","definition":"an aim or plan. Latin intendere 'stretch toward' supplies the root; there is no element of mutual action.","definitionCN":"意图；打算。词根来自拉丁语 intendere“朝……伸展”，不包含相互作用的成分。"},{"word":"interception","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈsepʃn/","tag":"different root: intercipere 'seize between'","definition":"the act of stopping something on its way. It comes from intercipere 'seize in between', built on capere 'take', a different verb from agere.","definitionCN":"在途中截住某物。它来自 intercipere“在半路夺取”，建立在 capere“拿取”之上，与 agere 不同。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"communication","ipa":"/kəˌmjuːnɪˈkeɪʃn/","tag":"message-focused","definition":"the sending and receiving of information. It can be one-way; interaction always implies a reply that changes the exchange.","definitionCN":"信息的发送与接收。它可以是单向的；interaction 总意味着会改变交流的回应。"},{"word":"exchange","ipa":"/ɪksˈtʃeɪndʒ/","tag":"giving and receiving","definition":"the giving of one thing and receiving of another. It stresses the swap, while interaction stresses the effects the parties have on each other.","definitionCN":"给出一物并得到另一物。它强调交换，而 interaction 强调双方对彼此产生的影响。"},{"word":"reciprocity","ipa":"/ˌresɪˈprɒsəti/","tag":"principle","definition":"the practice of responding to another's action with a comparable action. It names a rule or norm, not a concrete event.","definitionCN":"以对等行动回应他人行动的做法。它命名的是一条规则或规范，而不是具体事件。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real associations: inter- 'between' + action from agere 'do', the modern date 1832, and the fixed compounds drug interaction and human-computer interaction.","cn":"真实联想：inter-“在……之间”+ 源自 agere“做”的 action、1832 年这一现代造词时间，以及 drug interaction、human-computer interaction 等固定复合词。"},"normal":[{"en":"inter- means 'between', action means 'doing': interaction is doing something between two parties, each acting back.","cn":"inter- 意为“在……之间”，action 意为“做”：interaction 就是两方之间的做，而且各自都有回应。"},{"en":"Two arrows meeting in the middle is the whole word: no arrow points only one way.","cn":"两支箭头在中间相遇就是这个词的全部：没有哪支箭头只朝一个方向。"},{"en":"Drug interaction is the same loop at molecular scale: one substance changes what another does.","cn":"drug interaction 是同一回路在分子尺度上的版本：一种物质改变另一种的作用。"},{"en":"Human-computer interaction treats the screen as a partner that answers back.","cn":"human-computer interaction 把屏幕当作会回话的伙伴。"},{"en":"In class, interaction is counted by turns taken, not by minutes sat.","cn":"课堂上的 interaction 按轮次计，而不是按坐着的分钟数计。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The word is built from 'between' plus 'do', so it refuses to describe any act that happens in isolation.","cn":"这个词由“在……之间”加“做”构成，因此拒绝描述任何孤立发生的行动。"},{"en":"Every interaction leaves both sides changed; the loop is the meaning, not the meeting point.","cn":"每一次相互作用都让双方发生改变；意义在回路里，而不在相遇的那一点上。"},{"en":"Because action can be physical, chemical, social, or digital, the same noun scales from quarks to classrooms.","cn":"因为 action 可以是物理的、化学的、社会的或数字的，同一个名词能从夸克一直用到课堂。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The interaction between ocean currents and wind drives the global climate.","cn":"洋流与风的相互作用驱动着全球气候。"},{"en":"The drug has a serious interaction with grapefruit juice.","cn":"这种药与葡萄柚汁有严重的相互作用。"},{"en":"Teachers were trained to increase interaction among shy students.","cn":"教师们接受培训，以增加害羞学生之间的互动。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因它来爱克神”——两方都来，彼此“克”住又彼此回应 → interaction 互动、相互作用","word":"interaction"},"root":"inter-（在……之间）+ 拉丁语 agere/actum“做、驱动”+ -ion；字面义“在两者之间来回地做”，核心是“双向的作用与回应”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of interaction share one loop: two parties act, each receives the other's action, and both are changed. The difference between the senses is only who the parties are — people, drugs, particles, species, or a user and a screen.","cn":"interaction 的八个义项共享一个回路：两方行动，各自接收对方的行动，双方都发生改变。义项之间的差别只在于两方是谁——人、药物、粒子、物种，或用户与屏幕。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: two arrows leaving opposite sides and meeting at one point, then bending back.","cn":"核心意象：两支箭头从两侧出发，在一点相遇，然后折返。"},"chain":["TWO PARTIES","CONTACT","MUTUAL EFFECT","EXCHANGE","RESPONSE","OUTCOME"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S4","en":"MATTER: bodies and particles exert force on one another, the literal version of the loop.","cn":"物质：物体与粒子彼此施力，是这一回路最字面的版本。"},{"senses":"S2 · S6 · S8","en":"PEOPLE: conversation, daily social contact, and classroom turn-taking all depend on a reply.","cn":"人：交谈、日常社会往来与课堂轮次交替都依赖回应。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"MEDICINE: one substance changes how another is absorbed or acts.","cn":"医学：一种物质改变另一种的吸收或作用。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"ECOLOGY: species live inside each other's environment, so neither acts alone.","cn":"生态：物种各自活在对方的环境里，因此没有谁能单独行动。"},{"senses":"S7","en":"MACHINE: the interface answers the user, and the answer shapes the next action.","cn":"机器：界面对用户作出回应，而回应又塑造下一步行动。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Interaction is inter- + action, and action goes back to Latin agere. Its affix family therefore contains English derivatives of interact and the Latin verb with its noun and participle.","cn":"interaction 是 inter- + action，而 action 上溯拉丁语 agere。因此其词缀家族包含 interact 的英语派生词，以及该拉丁动词及其名词、分词形式。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin agere 'to do, drive' yields actus 'a doing', actio 'action', activus 'active', and the frequentative agitare 'to keep driving'. The inter- element is a separate Latin preposition meaning 'between'.","cn":"拉丁语 agere“做、驱动”产生 actus“行为”、actio“行动”、activus“主动的”，以及反复动词 agitare“不断驱动”。inter- 则是另一个拉丁介词，意为“在……之间”。"},"items":[{"word":"interaction","structure":"inter- (between) + action (-ion noun)","meaning":"reciprocal action or influence","meaningCN":"相互作用；互动（inter- + action）","example":"Species interaction shapes the food web.","exampleCN":"物种间的相互作用塑造食物网。"},{"word":"interact","structure":"inter- + act (back-formation from interaction)","meaning":"to act on one another","meaningCN":"互动；相互作用（由 interaction 逆构）","example":"The two chemicals interact violently.","exampleCN":"这两种化学品会发生剧烈反应。"},{"word":"interactive","structure":"interact + -ive","meaning":"acting back and forth; allowing two-way use","meaningCN":"互动的；交互式的（-ive 构成形容词）","example":"The museum has an interactive display.","exampleCN":"博物馆有一个互动展项。"},{"word":"interactivity","structure":"interactive + -ity","meaning":"the quality of responding to user action","meaningCN":"互动性（-ity 构成抽象名词）","example":"The site's interactivity was praised.","exampleCN":"这个网站的互动性受到称赞。"},{"word":"interactional","structure":"interaction + -al","meaning":"relating to interaction","meaningCN":"互动过程的（-al 构成形容词）","example":"She studies interactional norms in meetings.","exampleCN":"她研究会议中的互动规范。"},{"word":"interactionism","structure":"interaction + -ism","meaning":"a theory that treats interaction as central","meaningCN":"互动论（-ism 表理论）","example":"Symbolic interactionism studies how meanings are negotiated.","exampleCN":"符号互动论研究意义如何被协商。"},{"word":"interactant","structure":"interact + -ant","meaning":"a participant in an interaction","meaningCN":"互动参与者（-ant 表施动者）","example":"Each interactant takes a turn.","exampleCN":"每个互动参与者轮流发言。"},{"word":"action","structure":"Latin actio, from agere","meaning":"the doing of something","meaningCN":"行动；行为（actio，源自 agere）","example":"The plan requires immediate action.","exampleCN":"这项计划需要立即行动。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"agere","structure":"third-conjugation verb","meaning":"to do, drive, set in motion","meaningCN":"做；驱动；使动"},{"word":"actio","structure":"agere + -tio (action noun)","meaning":"a doing, action","meaningCN":"行动；行为"},{"word":"actus","structure":"fourth-declension noun from agere","meaning":"a deed, act","meaningCN":"行为；举动"},{"word":"inter","structure":"Latin preposition with accusative","meaning":"between, among","meaningCN":"在……之间；在……之中"}]}},{"word":"interactive","ipa_uk":"/ˌɪntərˈæktɪv/","ipa_us":"/ˌɪntərˈæktɪv/","definition_zh":"互动的；交互式的；相互作用的；（设备或软件）可双向操作的","definition_en":"acting on or responding to one another; involving two-way communication between people, or between a user and a machine that reacts to input","core_image":"手指点向屏幕，屏幕随即亮起并改变画面：一方动作，另一方马上回应","scene":"博物馆里，孩子伸手触碰展项屏幕，讲解员说这是交互式展项。This exhibit is interactive, so the picture changes when you touch the screen.","sceneCN":"这里 interactive 是「交互式的」（第 3 个义项：设备对用户操作作出回应）；句意：这个展项是交互式的，触摸屏幕画面就会改变。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"互动的；交互式的（指双方来回回应，尤指人机之间）"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"相互作用的；相互影响的（用于描述过程、关系或系统）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"interactive display","zh":"互动展项；交互式显示屏"},{"phrase":"interactive learning","zh":"互动式学习"},{"phrase":"interactive software","zh":"交互式软件"},{"phrase":"interactive session","zh":"交互式会话"},{"phrase":"interactive teaching","zh":"互动教学"},{"phrase":"interactive media","zh":"互动媒体"}],"forms":[{"label":"形容词原级","form":"interactive"},{"label":"比较级","form":"more interactive"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most interactive"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"interact","pos":"v.","zh":"互动；相互作用"},{"word":"interaction","pos":"n.","zh":"互动；相互作用"},{"word":"interactively","pos":"adv.","zh":"以交互方式"},{"word":"interactivity","pos":"n.","zh":"互动性；交互性"},{"word":"interactiveness","pos":"n.","zh":"互动程度"},{"word":"noninteractive","pos":"adj.","zh":"非交互的；单向的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Mutually acting","titleCN":"相互作用的","definition":"describing two or more things that act on each other and produce effects on both sides","definitionCN":"描述两个或更多事物彼此施力、双方都受影响","example":"The study models interactive forces inside the cell.","exampleCN":"这项研究对细胞内部相互作用的力进行建模。","why":"Interactive is interaction turned into an adjective: inter- 'between' + act, from Latin agere 'to do'. The -ive suffix makes it a property, so the word says that a relationship has two active ends rather than one.","whyCN":"interactive 是 interaction 转成的形容词：inter-“在……之间”+ act，源自拉丁语 agere“做”。-ive 后缀把它变成一种属性，因此这个词表示一种关系有两个活动的端点，而不是一个。"},{"no":"02","title":"Involving people in exchange","titleCN":"人与人互动交流的","definition":"describing communication in which people speak, listen, and respond to one another","definitionCN":"描述人们彼此说、听、回应的交流","example":"The workshop was interactive, with every participant speaking twice.","exampleCN":"这场工作坊是互动式的，每位参与者都发言了两次。","why":"Applied to people, the adjective describes a pattern rather than a device: turns alternate, and each turn depends on the last. It contrasts with 'lecture-style', where information flows one way.","whyCN":"用在人身上时，这个形容词描述一种模式而非设备：轮次交替，每一轮都取决于上一轮。它与“讲座式”相对，后者信息只朝一个方向流。"},{"no":"03","title":"Responding to user input","titleCN":"（设备）对用户操作作出回应的","definition":"describing a device, screen, or program that reacts immediately to what a user does","definitionCN":"描述对用户操作立即作出反应的设备、屏幕或程序","example":"The new kiosk is fully interactive and works without a keyboard.","exampleCN":"新的自助终端完全交互式，无需键盘即可使用。","why":"This is the computing sense recorded in the 1960s: a program is interactive when it waits for input and answers it. The machine is cast as a partner in the loop, not as a one-way display.","whyCN":"这是 1960 年代记录的计算机义：程序等待输入并回应输入，就是交互式的。机器被设定为回路中的伙伴，而不是单向的显示器。"},{"no":"04","title":"Open to audience participation","titleCN":"可供观众参与的","definition":"describing an exhibition, performance, or broadcast that invites the audience to take part","definitionCN":"描述邀请观众参与其中的展览、演出或节目","example":"The gallery's interactive installation lets visitors draw on the walls.","exampleCN":"美术馆的互动装置让观众可以在墙上作画。","why":"Museums and media borrowed the computing sense and shifted the partner from a machine to an audience. What stays constant is the invitation: the work is unfinished until someone acts.","whyCN":"博物馆与媒体借用了计算机义，把伙伴从机器换成了观众。不变的是那份邀请：作品在有人行动之前尚未完成。"},{"no":"05","title":"Two-way in teaching","titleCN":"互动式的（教学）","definition":"describing teaching in which students ask, answer, and act rather than only listen","definitionCN":"描述学生提问、回答、行动而不只是听讲的教学","example":"Interactive teaching raised the number of questions students asked.","exampleCN":"互动教学提高了学生提问的数量。","why":"Education reform used the adjective as a slogan against passive instruction. The word measures the number of directions in which information travels, so a lecture with questions counts as interactive.","whyCN":"教育改革把这个形容词当作反对被动灌输的口号。这个词衡量信息传播的方向数，所以带提问的讲授也算 interactive。"},{"no":"06","title":"Interactive mode in computing","titleCN":"（程序）交互模式的","definition":"describing a program or session that accepts commands and returns results immediately instead of running a fixed batch","definitionCN":"描述立即接受命令并返回结果、而非按固定批处理运行的程序或会话","example":"Switch to interactive mode to test each query as you type it.","exampleCN":"切换到交互模式，就可以边输入边测试每条查询。","why":"In computing, 'interactive' contrasts with 'batch': a batch job runs alone, while an interactive one waits and answers. The technical difference is where the human sits inside the loop.","whyCN":"计算机领域里 interactive 与 batch（批处理）相对：批处理任务独自运行，交互式任务则等待并回答。技术差别就在于人坐在回路的哪个位置。"},{"no":"07","title":"Mutually influencing in a process","titleCN":"相互影响的过程","definition":"describing a process or relationship in which each change produces a further change in the other party","definitionCN":"描述一种过程或关系，其中一方的变化又引起另一方变化","example":"The report describes an interactive cycle of warming and melting.","exampleCN":"报告描述了一个变暖与融化的相互影响循环。","why":"Here the adjective describes feedback rather than interface: warming melts ice, melting darkens the surface, darkening speeds warming. The word names the circle, not any single step.","whyCN":"这里的形容词描述反馈而非界面：变暖融冰，融冰使地表变暗，变暗又加速变暖。这个词命名的是圆圈，而不是任何单一步骤。"},{"no":"08","title":"Playable in games and media","titleCN":"（游戏、媒体）可操作互动的","definition":"describing entertainment in which the player's choices change what happens next","definitionCN":"描述玩家的选择会改变后续情节的娱乐形式","example":"The novel became an interactive story in which readers choose the ending.","exampleCN":"这部小说变成了互动故事，读者可以选择结局。","why":"Games and digital fiction extend the computing sense to narrative: the work branches according to input. 'Interactive' here means that the audience has authority over the outcome, however small.","whyCN":"游戏与数字小说把计算机义扩展到叙事：作品随输入分岔。这里的 interactive 意味着观众对结局拥有决定权，无论这权力多小。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Interactive is the adjective of interact, itself a back-formation from interaction. The parts are still visible: inter- 'between' plus act, from Latin agere 'to do'. Its computing sense is a twentieth-century specialization of a nineteenth-century word.","cn":"interactive 是 interact 的形容词，而 interact 又是 interaction 的逆构词。成分仍清晰可见：inter-“在……之间”加 act，源自拉丁语 agere“做”。它的计算机义是 19 世纪旧词在 20 世纪的专业化延伸。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Latin agere 'to do, drive' supplied actus and actio. The preposition inter 'between' could combine with almost any verb, giving the pattern 'do something between two parties'.","cn":"拉丁语 agere“做、驱动”提供了 actus 与 actio。介词 inter“在……之间”几乎能与任何动词组合，形成“在两方之间做某事”的模式。"},{"era":"1830s","en":"Interaction appeared in English natural philosophy, and the adjective interactive followed in the same decade with the sense 'mutually acting'. Early uses described forces, not people or machines.","cn":"interaction 出现在英语自然哲学中，形容词 interactive 在同一时期跟进，义为“相互作用的”。早期用法描述的是力，而不是人或机器。"},{"era":"LATE 19C.","en":"The adjective extended to human relations and to systems, often in the phrase 'interactive effects'. It remained a learned word, commoner in science than in daily speech.","cn":"这个形容词扩展到人际关系与系统，常出现在 interactive effects 这一说法中。它长期是学术词，在科学文本中比在日常口语中常见。"},{"era":"1960s COMPUTING","en":"Computer science gave the word its decisive modern sense: a program is interactive if it accepts input and answers during the session. The term separated real-time work from batch processing.","cn":"计算机科学赋予这个词决定性的现代义：程序在会话中接受输入并回答，就是交互式的。这个术语把实时工作与批处理区分开来。"},{"era":"1980s–1990s MEDIA","en":"Museums, schools, and broadcasters adopted 'interactive' as a label for audience participation, extending the computer model of input and response to culture and education.","cn":"博物馆、学校与广播机构把 interactive 用作观众参与的标签，把输入与回应的计算机模型扩展到文化与教育。"},{"era":"PRESENT","en":"Modern usage ranges from particle physics to touch screens. In every case the test is the same: does the other side answer, and does the answer change what happens next?","cn":"现代用法从粒子物理一直延伸到触摸屏。无论哪种情况，检验标准都一样：另一方是否回应，而回应是否改变接下来的发展？"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates adjectival forms built on agere with different prefixes; the near-meaning group separates words for responsiveness and participation.","cn":"形近组区分以 agere 为词根但前缀不同的形容词；近义组区分表示“有回应”与“可参与”的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"reactive","ipa":"/riˈæktɪv/","tag":"same agere, prefix re- 'back'","definition":"responding to a stimulus, often chemically. The re- means 'back', so the word stresses reaction after an event rather than exchange between equals.","definitionCN":"对刺激作出反应，常用于化学。re- 意为“回”，因此这个词强调事件之后的反应，而不是对等双方的交流。"},{"word":"inactive","ipa":"/ɪnˈæktɪv/","tag":"same root, negative prefix","definition":"not active. Here in- is a negating prefix attached to active; there is no second party and no exchange at all.","definitionCN":"不活跃的。这里的 in- 是否定前缀，加在 active 上；不存在第二方，也完全没有交流。"},{"word":"interactional","ipa":"/ˌɪntərˈækʃənl/","tag":"same root, noun-based","definition":"relating to interaction as a process. It describes the study or structure of exchanges, not a device or person that responds.","definitionCN":"与互动过程有关的。它描述交流的研究或结构，而不是会回应的设备或人。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"responsive","ipa":"/rɪˈspɒnsɪv/","tag":"reaction","definition":"quick to react to something. It stresses speed and attentiveness on one side; interactive stresses that both sides act.","definitionCN":"反应迅速的。它强调一方的速度与关注；interactive 强调双方都在行动。"},{"word":"two-way","ipa":"/ˌtuːˈweɪ/","tag":"direction","definition":"allowing movement or communication in both directions. It names the channel, while interactive names the responding behaviour.","definitionCN":"允许双向移动或通信的。它命名通道，而 interactive 命名回应行为。"},{"word":"participatory","ipa":"/ˌpɑːtɪsɪˈpeɪtəri/","tag":"involvement","definition":"involving people as active participants. It stresses membership and taking part, not the back-and-forth of response.","definitionCN":"让人作为积极参与者的。它强调加入与参与，而不是来回的回应。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real associations: the inter- + act pattern, the computing contrast with batch mode, and the everyday phrase interactive display.","cn":"真实联想：inter- + act 的构词模式、与批处理模式相对的计算机用法，以及日常说法 interactive display。"},"normal":[{"en":"inter- 'between' + act 'do' + -ive: something that keeps doing between two sides.","cn":"inter-“在……之间”+ act“做”+ -ive：一直在两方之间做的东西。"},{"en":"If the screen answers your finger, it is interactive; if it only shows, it is not.","cn":"屏幕回应你的手指，就是 interactive；只显示不回应，就不是。"},{"en":"Batch mode runs alone; interactive mode waits for you — that is the difference the word marks.","cn":"批处理模式独自运行；交互模式等你输入——这个词标记的正是这个差别。"},{"en":"An interactive class is measured by how many directions talk travels, not by how loud the teacher is.","cn":"互动课堂按话语传播的方向数来衡量，而不是按老师嗓门大小。"},{"en":"An interactive exhibition is unfinished until a visitor touches it.","cn":"互动展览在观众触碰之前都算未完成。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The word describes a loop with two live ends; remove either end and the adjective no longer applies.","cn":"这个词描述一个两端都活着的回路；去掉任一端，这个形容词就不再适用。"},{"en":"Response is the test: a thing is interactive only if what you do changes what it does next.","cn":"回应是检验标准：只有你的作为改变了它接下来的作为，它才算 interactive。"},{"en":"From particles to novels, the same shape recurs — action, answer, altered next action.","cn":"从粒子到小说，同一个形状反复出现——行动、回应、被改变的下一个行动。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The museum added interactive exhibits that respond to visitors' movements.","cn":"博物馆增设了能对观众动作作出反应的互动展项。"},{"en":"Interactive learning produces more questions than a straight lecture.","cn":"互动式学习比纯讲授产生更多提问。"},{"en":"The software runs in interactive mode so users see results at once.","cn":"这款软件以交互模式运行，用户可以立刻看到结果。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因它来爱克提舞”——它一来，两边就“克”着互动起来 → interactive 互动的、交互式的","word":"interactive"},"root":"inter-（在……之间）+ 拉丁语 agere/actum“做”+ -ive（形容词后缀）；字面义“在两者之间来回做的”，核心是“一方动作、另一方回应”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of interactive all describe a loop with two active ends: forces, people, devices, audiences, classes, programs, feedback cycles, and games. The word is a property, not an event — it says that answering is possible.","cn":"interactive 的八个义项都描述一个两端都在活动的回路：力、人、设备、观众、课堂、程序、反馈循环与游戏。这个词是一种属性，而不是一个事件——它说的是“回应是可能的”。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a finger touches a screen and the screen changes at once; action and answer in one moment.","cn":"核心意象：手指触碰屏幕，屏幕立刻改变；动作与回应在同一瞬间。"},"chain":["TWO ENDS","ACTION","SIGNAL","RESPONSE","ADJUSTMENT","CONTINUING LOOP"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S7","en":"NATURAL PROCESS: forces and feedback cycles act on each other without any user.","cn":"自然过程：力与反馈循环在没有任何使用者的情况下彼此作用。"},{"senses":"S2 · S5","en":"PEOPLE: conversation and two-way teaching depend on alternating turns.","cn":"人：交谈与双向教学依赖轮次的交替。"},{"senses":"S3 · S6","en":"MACHINE: a device or program waits for input and answers it, in contrast with batch operation.","cn":"机器：设备或程序等待输入并回应，与批处理运行相对。"},{"senses":"S4","en":"AUDIENCE: exhibitions and media invite the visitor to act and then answer that act.","cn":"观众：展览与媒体邀请观众动手，再对这一动作作出回应。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"PLAY: choices branch the story, so the audience holds authority over the outcome.","cn":"游戏：选择让故事分岔，观众因此对结局拥有决定权。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Interactive is interact + -ive, and interact is a back-formation from interaction. The family therefore circles around Latin agere 'to do', with inter- 'between' added in English.","cn":"interactive 是 interact + -ive，而 interact 是 interaction 的逆构词。整个家族因此围绕拉丁语 agere“做”，并由英语加上 inter-“在……之间”。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin agere 'to do, drive' gives actus, actio, activus, and the frequentative agitare. The prefix inter- is a separate preposition; it was attached to English act, not inherited as a Latin compound.","cn":"拉丁语 agere“做、驱动”给出 actus、actio、activus 与反复动词 agitare。前缀 inter- 是独立的介词，它是加在英语 act 上，而不是作为拉丁复合词继承下来的。"},"items":[{"word":"interactive","structure":"interact + -ive (adjective)","meaning":"responding to input; mutually acting","meaningCN":"互动的；交互式的（-ive 构成形容词）","example":"The exhibit is interactive.","exampleCN":"这个展项是互动式的。"},{"word":"interact","structure":"inter- + act, back-formed from interaction","meaning":"to act on each other","meaningCN":"互动；相互作用（逆构词）","example":"Users interact with the map by dragging it.","exampleCN":"用户通过拖动地图与它互动。"},{"word":"interaction","structure":"inter- + action (-ion)","meaning":"reciprocal action","meaningCN":"互动；相互作用（-ion 构成名词）","example":"Interaction between the two systems is limited.","exampleCN":"这两个系统之间的交互很有限。"},{"word":"interactively","structure":"interactive + -ly","meaning":"in a two-way manner","meaningCN":"以交互方式（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The data can be explored interactively.","exampleCN":"数据可以交互式地探索。"},{"word":"interactivity","structure":"interactive + -ity","meaning":"the degree to which something responds","meaningCN":"互动性；交互性（-ity 构成抽象名词）","example":"Reviewers praised the app's interactivity.","exampleCN":"评论者称赞这款应用的互动性。"},{"word":"interactiveness","structure":"interactive + -ness","meaning":"the quality of being interactive","meaningCN":"互动程度（-ness 构成抽象名词）","example":"The interactiveness of the lesson surprised the observers.","exampleCN":"这堂课的互动程度让观察者惊讶。"},{"word":"noninteractive","structure":"non- + interactive","meaning":"not responding to input","meaningCN":"非交互的；单向的（non- 表否定）","example":"A noninteractive report cannot be filtered.","exampleCN":"非交互式报表无法筛选。"},{"word":"reactive","structure":"re- (back) + act + -ive","meaning":"acting in response to a stimulus","meaningCN":"反应性的（re-“回”+ act + -ive）","example":"The material is reactive to light.","exampleCN":"这种材料对光有反应。"},{"word":"action","structure":"Latin actio, from agere","meaning":"a deed or the process of doing","meaningCN":"行动；行为（actio，源自 agere）","example":"Action followed the decision at once.","exampleCN":"决定之后立即付诸行动。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"agere","structure":"third-conjugation verb","meaning":"to do, drive, set in motion","meaningCN":"做；驱动；使动"},{"word":"actio","structure":"agere + -tio (action noun)","meaning":"a doing, action","meaningCN":"行动；行为"},{"word":"activus","structure":"actus + -ivus","meaning":"active, of doing","meaningCN":"主动的；活动的"},{"word":"inter","structure":"preposition with accusative","meaning":"between, among","meaningCN":"在……之间；在……之中"}]}},{"word":"interconnection","ipa_uk":"/ˌɪntəkəˈnekʃn/","ipa_us":"/ˌɪntərkəˈnekʃn/","definition_zh":"互联；相互连接；相互关联；（网络、系统之间的）连通","definition_en":"the state or process of being connected with one another, especially of systems, networks, organisms, or ideas","core_image":"几座岛被同一组桥连成一片：每座岛都不再孤立","scene":"电网调度中心里，工程师指着线路图，说各区域电网彼此连通，电力可以互相支援。The interconnection of the regional grids lets one area send power to another.","sceneCN":"这里 interconnection 是「互联、相互连接」（第 1 个义项：系统之间彼此连通）；句意：各区域电网的互联让一个地区可以给另一个地区送电。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"互联；相互连接（可数指一条连接，不可数指互联状态）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（系统、网络）互联互通；相互关联（常带修饰语，如电网、网络）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"network interconnection","zh":"网络互联"},{"phrase":"power grid interconnection","zh":"电网互联"},{"phrase":"interconnection between A and B","zh":"A 与 B 之间的互联"},{"phrase":"global interconnection","zh":"全球互联"},{"phrase":"interconnection of systems","zh":"系统互联"},{"phrase":"close interconnection","zh":"紧密的相互联系"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"interconnection"},{"label":"复数","form":"interconnections"},{"label":"作定语（名词修饰名词）","form":"interconnection network"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"interconnect","pos":"v.","zh":"使互连；互联"},{"word":"interconnected","pos":"adj.","zh":"相互连接的；互联的"},{"word":"interconnectedness","pos":"n.","zh":"互联性；相互关联性"},{"word":"interconnectivity","pos":"n.","zh":"互联互通性"},{"word":"connection","pos":"n.","zh":"连接；联系"},{"word":"connective","pos":"adj./n.","zh":"连接的；连接词"},{"word":"connector","pos":"n.","zh":"连接器；接头"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"State of being linked","titleCN":"相互连接的状态","definition":"the condition in which two or more things are joined or linked to one another","definitionCN":"两个或更多事物彼此连接或联系在一起的状态","example":"The interconnection of the two reservoirs allows water to be shifted between them.","exampleCN":"两座水库的互联使水可以在它们之间调配。","why":"Interconnection is inter- 'between' plus connection, whose Latin source connectere means com- 'together' + nectere 'to bind'. Two layers of joining are stacked: binding together, and doing it between separate things.","whyCN":"interconnection 是 inter-“在……之间”加 connection，后者的拉丁语源 connectere 意为 com-“一起”+ nectere“捆、系”。这里叠了两层连接：把东西捆在一起，而且是在彼此分离的事物之间这样做。"},{"no":"02","title":"Network interconnection","titleCN":"网络互联","definition":"the linking of separate computer or telecommunications networks so that traffic can pass between them","definitionCN":"把彼此独立的计算机或通信网络连接起来，使流量可以在其间通行","example":"Standards made network interconnection possible between competing providers.","exampleCN":"标准使相互竞争的服务商之间的网络互联成为可能。","why":"In networking the word is technical: two networks stay separate as systems but share a boundary where packets cross. The prefix inter- is doing precise work — the link is between networks, not inside one.","whyCN":"在网络领域这个词是术语：两个网络作为系统仍是独立的，只是共享一个数据包可以越过的边界。前缀 inter- 在这里很精确——连接发生在网络之间，而不是网络内部。"},{"no":"03","title":"Mutual relation of facts or ideas","titleCN":"事实或观念之间的相互关联","definition":"a relationship in which one thing explains, supports, or depends on another","definitionCN":"一事物解释、支持或依赖另一事物的关系","example":"The essay traces the interconnection of poverty and poor sanitation.","exampleCN":"这篇文章梳理了贫困与卫生条件差之间的相互关联。","why":"The physical image transfers to reasoning: ideas are joined like reservoirs, so a change in one shows up in the other. This sense is common in academic writing, where causes are rarely single.","whyCN":"物理意象转到推理上：观念像水库一样连通，一处的变化会出现在另一处。这个义项在学术写作中很常见，因为原因很少是单一的。"},{"no":"04","title":"Electrical interconnection","titleCN":"电气互连","definition":"the wiring that joins components or circuits so that current or signals can flow between them","definitionCN":"把元件或电路连接起来，使电流或信号可以在其间流动的布线","example":"A faulty interconnection caused the board to fail.","exampleCN":"一处有故障的互连导致电路板失效。","why":"Electronics uses the word for the physical path itself: solder joints, cables, and pins. Here the 'between' is spatial and measurable, which is why engineers speak of interconnection resistance.","whyCN":"电子学用这个词指实体通路本身：焊点、电缆、引脚。这里的“之间”是空间上可测量的，所以工程师会说互连电阻。"},{"no":"05","title":"Global interconnection","titleCN":"全球互联","definition":"the worldwide linking of economies, communications, and supply chains","definitionCN":"世界经济、通信与供应链在全球范围内的连接","example":"The pandemic exposed the fragility of global interconnection.","exampleCN":"疫情暴露了全球互联的脆弱性。","why":"Twentieth-century globalization writing turned the noun into a slogan: distant places are not separate. The word promises both benefit, shared growth, and risk, shared shock.","whyCN":"20 世纪的全球化写作把这个名词变成口号：遥远的地方并不彼此分离。这个词同时许诺好处（共同增长）与风险（共同震荡）。"},{"no":"06","title":"Ecological interconnection","titleCN":"生态系统的相互连接","definition":"the dependence of species and habitats on one another within an ecosystem","definitionCN":"生态系统内物种与栖息地彼此依赖的关系","example":"The film shows the interconnection of forest, river, and coastal life.","exampleCN":"影片展示了森林、河流与海岸生命之间的相互连接。","why":"Ecology uses interconnection to argue against treating any species in isolation: a river's health is written into the forest's soil. The word carries a moral as well as a descriptive load.","whyCN":"生态学用 interconnection 反对孤立地看待任何物种：河流的健康写在森林的土壤里。这个词既有描述意义，也有道德含义。"},{"no":"07","title":"Interpersonal or organizational links","titleCN":"人际或组织间的联系网络","definition":"the web of relationships through which people or institutions reach one another","definitionCN":"人们或机构借以相互接触的关系网络","example":"The study mapped the interconnection of research groups across universities.","exampleCN":"这项研究绘制了各大学研究团队之间的联系网络。","why":"Social and organizational writing applies the noun to people: who knows whom, and through how many steps. The image is a map with edges, not a hierarchy with levels.","whyCN":"社会与组织研究把这个名词用在人身上：谁认识谁，隔了几步。意象是一张带边的图，而不是有层级的树。"},{"no":"08","title":"Transport network interconnection","titleCN":"交通网络的互联","definition":"the linking of routes, lines, or transport modes so that passengers can transfer without leaving the system","definitionCN":"把路线、线路或交通方式连接起来，使乘客不必离开系统即可换乘","example":"Interconnection between rail and bus services shortened the journey by an hour.","exampleCN":"铁路与公交服务的互联使行程缩短了一小时。","why":"Transport planning uses interconnection for the moment when one network hands a passenger to another. The word measures seamlessness: the link is judged by whether the traveller has to break the journey.","whyCN":"交通规划用 interconnection 指一个网络把乘客交给另一个网络的那一刻。这个词衡量无缝程度：连接的好坏取决于乘客是否必须中断行程。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Interconnection is inter- 'between' plus connection, and connection comes from Latin connectere 'to bind together', built on com- 'together' and nectere 'to bind'. The English noun stacks a Latin prefix on a Latin-derived noun.","cn":"interconnection 是 inter-“在……之间”加 connection，而 connection 源自拉丁语 connectere“捆在一起”，由 com-“一起”与 nectere“捆、系”构成。这个英语名词把拉丁前缀叠在拉丁来源的名词上。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Latin nectere meant 'to bind, tie, fasten'. With com- 'together' it formed connectere 'to fasten together'. The noun connexio named a joining, whether of things, words, or people.","cn":"拉丁语 nectere 意为“捆、系、缚”。加 com-“一起”构成 connectere“捆在一起”。名词 connexio 命名连接，无论是物、词还是人的连接。"},{"era":"14C.–17C. ENGLISH","en":"English connection entered through Old French connexion with the sense 'a linking'. For centuries it described joints, relationships, and logical links without any prefix inter-.","cn":"英语 connection 经古法语 connexion 进入，义为“连接”。数百年间它描述接合、关系与逻辑联系，都不带前缀 inter-。"},{"era":"1820s","en":"Interconnection is recorded in the 1820s as 'state of being interconnected'. It was first used of physical and mechanical systems before it reached networks of people or ideas.","cn":"interconnection 于 1820 年代被记录，义为“相互连接的状态”。它先用于物理与机械系统，后来才延伸到人与观念的网络。"},{"era":"19C.–20C. ENGINEERING","en":"Railways, telegraphy, and electrical grids needed a word for systems that stay distinct yet exchange. Interconnection became a technical measure of how well two networks hand over traffic.","cn":"铁路、电报与电网需要一个词描述“保持独立却彼此交换”的系统。interconnection 成为衡量两个网络交接流量好坏的技术指标。"},{"era":"20C. ECOLOGY AND SOCIETY","en":"Ecology and later sociology adopted the noun to argue that parts cannot be understood alone. The word became a way of asserting relationship over isolation.","cn":"生态学以及后来的社会学采用这个名词，主张部分无法被孤立理解。这个词成为“关系优先于孤立”的一种断言方式。"},{"era":"PRESENT","en":"Modern use spans power grids, computer networks, supply chains, and ecosystems. In every case the same claim is made: the system's behaviour lives in the links, not in the nodes.","cn":"现代用法覆盖电网、计算机网络、供应链与生态系统。无论哪种情况，主张都一样：系统的行为存在于连接之中，而不在节点之中。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates inter- nouns built on different Latin verbs; the near-meaning group separates words for linking and mutual dependence.","cn":"形近组区分以 inter- 开头但词根动词不同的名词；近义组区分表示“连接”与“相互依赖”的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"interjection","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈdʒekʃn/","tag":"different root: iacere 'throw'","definition":"a word thrown into speech, such as 'oh'. It comes from intericere 'throw between', built on iacere 'throw', not nectere 'bind'.","definitionCN":"插入话语中的感叹词，如 oh。它来自 intericere“抛在中间”，词根是 iacere“投掷”，而非 nectere“捆系”。"},{"word":"intersection","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈsekʃn/","tag":"different root: secare 'cut'","definition":"the point where lines cross. Latin intersecare 'cut between' supplies the root secare 'cut'; nothing is bound together.","definitionCN":"线相交的点。拉丁语 intersecare“在中间切”提供词根 secare“切”；这里没有任何东西被捆在一起。"},{"word":"integration","ipa":"/ˌɪntɪˈɡreɪʃn/","tag":"different root: integrare 'make whole'","definition":"the merging of parts into a whole. It comes from integrare 'to make whole'; interconnection keeps the parts distinct while linking them.","definitionCN":"把部分并入整体。它源自 integrare“使完整”；interconnection 则在连接的同时让各部分保持独立。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"connection","ipa":"/kəˈnekʃn/","tag":"base word","definition":"a link or relationship between things. It lacks inter-, so it can describe a link inside one system as well as one between two systems.","definitionCN":"事物之间的连接或关系。它没有 inter-，因此既可描述一个系统内部的连接，也可描述两个系统之间的连接。"},{"word":"linkage","ipa":"/ˈlɪŋkɪdʒ/","tag":"mechanism","definition":"a system of links, often mechanical or institutional. It stresses the mechanism of joining rather than the resulting shared state.","definitionCN":"连接系统，常指机械或制度上的连接。它强调连接机制，而不是由此形成的共享状态。"},{"word":"interdependence","ipa":"/ˌɪntədɪˈpendəns/","tag":"dependence","definition":"mutual reliance, where each side needs the other. Interconnection says the parts are linked; interdependence says they cannot survive apart.","definitionCN":"相互依赖，双方都需要对方。interconnection 说各部分相连；interdependence 说它们不能分离而存。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real associations: inter- 'between' + connectere 'bind together', the double joining, and the technical phrases power grid interconnection and network interconnection.","cn":"真实联想：inter-“在……之间”+ connectere“捆在一起”、双重连接的结构，以及 power grid interconnection、network interconnection 等术语。"},"normal":[{"en":"connect comes from nectere 'bind'; interconnection is binding that is done between separate things.","cn":"connect 来自 nectere“捆系”；interconnection 就是在彼此分离的事物之间进行的捆系。"},{"en":"Two prefixes stack here: com- 'together' inside connection, inter- 'between' outside it.","cn":"这里叠了两个前缀：connection 内部的 com-“一起”，外面的 inter-“在……之间”。"},{"en":"An electrical interconnection is literally a wire: current crosses from one board to another.","cn":"电气互连字面上就是一根线：电流从一块板子越到另一块。"},{"en":"Network interconnection means two networks stay two networks but share a doorway.","cn":"网络互联意味着两个网络仍是两个网络，只是共享一道门。"},{"en":"In ecology the word argues that a river's health is written into the forest's soil.","cn":"在生态学里，这个词主张河流的健康写在森林的土壤里。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The word never merges its parts; it insists that distinct things can share a boundary.","cn":"这个词从不把各部分合并；它坚持独立的事物可以共享一道边界。"},{"en":"Two layers of joining, together and between, make it the natural word for systems that must stay separate yet exchange.","cn":"“一起”与“之间”两层连接，使它成为描述“必须保持独立却又要交换”的系统的天然用词。"},{"en":"Value sits in the links: remove the bridges and the islands are still there, but nothing crosses.","cn":"价值在连接里：拆掉桥，岛还在，但没有东西能过去。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The interconnection of regional power grids reduced the risk of blackouts.","cn":"区域电网的互联降低了停电风险。"},{"en":"Researchers studied the interconnection between sleep quality and memory.","cn":"研究者研究了睡眠质量与记忆之间的相互关联。"},{"en":"Better interconnection between buses and trains would shorten commutes.","cn":"公交与铁路之间更好的互联会缩短通勤时间。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因它来，扣麦克神”——它一来，就把两边“扣”在一起、拴成一片 → interconnection 互联、相互连接","word":"interconnection"},"root":"inter-（在……之间）+ com-（一起）+ 拉丁语 nectere“捆、系”+ -ion；字面义“在两者之间捆在一起”，核心是“彼此独立却共享接口”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of interconnection all describe distinct things that share a boundary: reservoirs, networks, ideas, circuits, economies, species, people, and transport lines. The word never means merging; it means a working link between separate ends.","cn":"interconnection 的八个义项都描述彼此独立却共享边界的对象：水库、网络、观念、电路、经济体、物种、人、交通线。这个词从不表示合并，它表示独立两端之间有效运作的连接。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: several islands joined by one set of bridges, each island still separate.","cn":"核心意象：几座岛由同一组桥连起，每座岛仍然各自独立。"},"chain":["SEPARATE ENDS","LINK","SHARED BOUNDARY","TRANSFER","MUTUAL EFFECT","SYSTEM"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S4","en":"PHYSICAL LINK: reservoirs, wires, and boards are joined by something measurable.","cn":"物理连接：水库、电线与电路板通过可测量的东西相连。"},{"senses":"S2 · S8","en":"INFRASTRUCTURE: networks and transport lines hand traffic across a shared doorway.","cn":"基础设施：网络与交通线在共享的门口交接流量。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"REASONING: facts and ideas support one another, so a change in one appears in the other.","cn":"推理：事实与观念彼此支持，一处的变化会出现在另一处。"},{"senses":"S5 · S7","en":"HUMAN SYSTEMS: economies, institutions, and people form webs rather than hierarchies.","cn":"人类系统：经济体、机构与人形成网状关系而非层级。"},{"senses":"S6","en":"ECOLOGY: species and habitats are written into each other's survival.","cn":"生态：物种与栖息地写进了彼此的生存条件。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Interconnection is inter- + connection; connection is connect + -ion, and connect comes from Latin connectere. The family splits into English derivatives of connect and the Latin verb nectere with its compounds.","cn":"interconnection 是 inter- + connection；connection 是 connect + -ion，而 connect 源自拉丁语 connectere。这个家族分为 connect 的英语派生词与拉丁动词 nectere 及其复合形式。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin nectere 'to bind' yields nexus 'a binding' and connectere 'to bind together'. Announce and annex belong to the same nectere family, which is why their meanings all involve fastening rather than mere proximity.","cn":"拉丁语 nectere“捆系”给出 nexus“联结”与 connectere“捆在一起”。announce 与 annex 同属 nectere 家族，因此它们的含义都与“系上”有关，而不只是靠近。"},"items":[{"word":"interconnection","structure":"inter- + connection (-ion)","meaning":"a link between separate things","meaningCN":"互联；相互连接（inter- + connection）","example":"The interconnection of the grids was completed last year.","exampleCN":"电网互联于去年完成。"},{"word":"interconnect","structure":"inter- + connect (verb)","meaning":"to link separate things to each other","meaningCN":"使互连；互联（inter- + connect）","example":"The devices interconnect over a wireless protocol.","exampleCN":"这些设备通过无线协议互连。"},{"word":"interconnected","structure":"interconnect + -ed (past participle)","meaning":"linked to one another","meaningCN":"相互连接的（-ed 构成形容词）","example":"The world's markets are closely interconnected.","exampleCN":"世界市场紧密互联。"},{"word":"interconnectedness","structure":"interconnected + -ness","meaning":"the quality of being linked","meaningCN":"互联性（-ness 构成抽象名词）","example":"The book stresses the interconnectedness of all life.","exampleCN":"这本书强调万物生命的互联性。"},{"word":"interconnectivity","structure":"inter- + connectivity","meaning":"the degree to which systems can link","meaningCN":"互联互通性（inter- + connectivity）","example":"Interconnectivity is the main design goal.","exampleCN":"互联互通性是主要设计目标。"},{"word":"connection","structure":"connect + -ion, from Latin connexio","meaning":"a link or relationship","meaningCN":"连接；联系（-ion 构成名词）","example":"There is a clear connection between the two events.","exampleCN":"这两个事件之间有明显的联系。"},{"word":"connective","structure":"connect + -ive","meaning":"serving to join things","meaningCN":"连接的；连接词（-ive 构成形容词）","example":"Tissue is the connective material of the body.","exampleCN":"组织是身体的连接性材料。"},{"word":"connector","structure":"connect + -or","meaning":"a device that joins parts","meaningCN":"连接器；接头（-or 表器物）","example":"Replace the damaged connector first.","exampleCN":"先更换损坏的接头。"},{"word":"disconnect","structure":"dis- (apart) + connect","meaning":"to separate what was joined","meaningCN":"断开；使分离（dis- 表相反）","example":"Disconnect the power before opening the panel.","exampleCN":"打开面板前先断开电源。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"nectere","structure":"third-conjugation verb","meaning":"to bind, tie, fasten","meaningCN":"捆；系；缚"},{"word":"connectere","structure":"com- 'together' + nectere 'bind'","meaning":"to bind together","meaningCN":"捆在一起；连接"},{"word":"connexio","structure":"connectere + -tio (action noun)","meaning":"a joining, connection","meaningCN":"连接；联结"},{"word":"nexus","structure":"fourth-declension noun from nectere","meaning":"a binding, interconnection","meaningCN":"联结；联系"}]}},{"word":"interdependence","ipa_uk":"/ˌɪntədɪˈpendəns/","ipa_us":"/ˌɪntərdɪˈpendəns/","definition_zh":"相互依赖；相互依存；（生态、经济、政治上的）互赖关系","definition_en":"the condition in which two or more people, groups, species, or systems depend on each other for survival, support, or normal functioning","core_image":"两个人各扶住同一架梯子的一端：谁松手，两人都会摔下来","scene":"全球经济课上，教授指着供应链图说，一处缺货就能波及全世界。Global supply chains show how deep the interdependence of nations has become.","sceneCN":"这里 interdependence 是「相互依赖」（第 1 个义项：双方彼此需要才能运转）；句意：全球供应链显示出各国之间的相互依赖有多深。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"相互依赖；相互依存（不可数，指状态；可数时指一种具体的互赖关系）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（专业）互赖：经济、生态、国际政治等领域的术语（常带修饰语）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"economic interdependence","zh":"经济上的相互依存"},{"phrase":"interdependence between A and B","zh":"A 与 B 之间的相互依赖"},{"phrase":"mutual interdependence","zh":"相互依赖"},{"phrase":"global interdependence","zh":"全球互赖"},{"phrase":"complex interdependence","zh":"复合相互依存（国际关系术语）"},{"phrase":"ecological interdependence","zh":"生态上的相互依存"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数（一般／不可数）","form":"interdependence"},{"label":"复数（多种互赖关系）","form":"interdependences"},{"label":"作定语（名词修饰名词）","form":"interdependence theory"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"interdependent","pos":"adj.","zh":"相互依赖的；互赖的"},{"word":"interdependently","pos":"adv.","zh":"以相互依赖的方式"},{"word":"depend","pos":"v.","zh":"依赖；取决于"},{"word":"dependent","pos":"adj./n.","zh":"依赖的；受抚养者"},{"word":"dependence","pos":"n.","zh":"依赖；依存"},{"word":"dependency","pos":"n.","zh":"依赖关系；附属地"},{"word":"independent","pos":"adj.","zh":"独立的；不受支配的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Mutual reliance in general","titleCN":"一般意义上的相互依赖","definition":"a situation in which each of two or more parties needs the others in order to function or succeed","definitionCN":"两个或更多方中，每一方都需要其他方才能运转或成功的情形","example":"The partnership rests on a genuine interdependence rather than one-sided need.","exampleCN":"这种伙伴关系建立在真正的相互依赖之上，而不是单方面的需要。","why":"Interdependence adds inter- 'between' to dependence, from Latin dependere 'hang from', built on de- 'down' and pendere 'hang'. The image is a weight hanging from a hook: each side is a support for the other, so neither can simply let go.","whyCN":"interdependence 在 dependence 上加 inter-“在……之间”，而 dependence 源自拉丁语 dependere“悬挂于”，由 de-“向下”与 pendere“悬挂”构成。意象是重物挂在钩上：每一方都是对方的支点，谁都不能随便松手。"},{"no":"02","title":"Economic interdependence","titleCN":"经济上的相互依存","definition":"the condition in which economies rely on each other for trade, investment, and supply","definitionCN":"各经济体在贸易、投资与供应上彼此依赖的状态","example":"Trade data show how quickly economic interdependence transmits a local shortage.","exampleCN":"贸易数据表明，经济互赖会让局部短缺迅速传导。","why":"Economics adopted the noun to describe gains and risks of the same fact: specialisation raises output but also exposes each country to shocks elsewhere. The word names a two-sided vulnerability, not merely cooperation.","whyCN":"经济学采用这个名词来描述同一事实的两面：专业化提高产量，也让每个国家暴露在他处的冲击之下。这个词命名的是双向的脆弱性，而不只是合作。"},{"no":"03","title":"Ecological interdependence","titleCN":"生态上的相互依存","definition":"the reliance of species and habitats on one another within an ecosystem","definitionCN":"生态系统内物种与栖息地彼此依赖的关系","example":"Pollinators and flowering plants show a clear interdependence.","exampleCN":"传粉昆虫与开花植物表现出明显的相互依存。","why":"Ecology generalised the word to food webs: a predator depends on prey, and prey numbers depend on predators. Removal of one node is felt elsewhere, which is exactly what the hanging image predicts.","whyCN":"生态学把这个词推广到食物网：捕食者依赖猎物，猎物的数量又取决于捕食者。移除一个节点，别处就会感到，这正是悬挂意象所预示的。"},{"no":"04","title":"Psychological or social reliance","titleCN":"心理与社会层面的互赖","definition":"a relationship in which people rely on one another for emotional support, care, or daily tasks","definitionCN":"人们彼此依赖以获得情感支持、照料或完成日常事务的关系","example":"Healthy families balance interdependence with personal autonomy.","exampleCN":"健康的家庭在相互依赖与个人自主之间取得平衡。","why":"Psychology uses the noun for mature reliance: needing others without losing oneself. It is contrasted with 'dependence' as a pathology, because inter- makes the reliance reciprocal and therefore non-exploitative.","whyCN":"心理学用这个名词指成熟的依赖：需要他人而不失去自我。它与作为病态的 dependence 相对，因为 inter- 使依赖成为相互的，因而没有剥削性。"},{"no":"05","title":"Complex interdependence in politics","titleCN":"国际政治中的复合相互依存","definition":"the condition in which states are linked through many channels so that force becomes costly and less useful","definitionCN":"各国通过多种渠道相连，以致使用武力代价高昂且效用下降的状态","example":"The theory of complex interdependence explains why trade disputes rarely become wars.","exampleCN":"复合相互依存理论解释了贸易争端为何很少演变为战争。","why":"Robert Keohane and Joseph Nye made the phrase a term of international relations in the 1970s. The word carries their argument: multiple channels of contact change the calculus of power.","whyCN":"罗伯特·基欧汉与约瑟夫·奈在 1970 年代把这个说法变成国际关系术语。这个词承载着他们的论点：多渠道的接触改变了权力的计算方式。"},{"no":"06","title":"Interdependence of technical systems","titleCN":"技术系统之间的互赖","definition":"the coupling of infrastructures such that a failure in one propagates into another","definitionCN":"基础设施彼此耦合，一处故障会传播到另一处","example":"Engineers map the interdependence of power and water systems before planning outages.","exampleCN":"工程师在规划停运前先绘制电力与供水系统的互赖关系。","why":"Infrastructure studies borrowed the term for cascading failure: water pumps need electricity, and power plants need water. The word describes a shared fate that operators cannot ignore.","whyCN":"基础设施研究借用这个术语来描述级联失效：水泵需要电力，电厂需要水。这个词描述一种运营者无法忽视的共同命运。"},{"no":"07","title":"Interdependence among organizations","titleCN":"组织之间的相互依赖","definition":"the reliance of firms or institutions on one another for resources, information, or legitimacy","definitionCN":"企业或机构在资源、信息或合法性上彼此依赖","example":"Suppliers and manufacturers develop a long-term interdependence.","exampleCN":"供应商与制造商形成长期的相互依赖。","why":"Organization theory uses the noun to explain why firms cooperate without merging: each controls resources the other needs, so the link holds without ownership.","whyCN":"组织理论用这个名词解释企业为何合作而不合并：各自掌握对方需要的资源，因此连接在没有所有权的情况下也能维持。"},{"no":"08","title":"Biological mutual dependence","titleCN":"生物学上的共生依赖","definition":"a close association in which two organisms depend on each other for survival","definitionCN":"两种生物彼此依赖才能存活的紧密关系","example":"Lichens are a textbook case of interdependence between fungus and alga.","exampleCN":"地衣是真菌与藻类相互依存的教科书案例。","why":"Biology applies the noun to symbiosis, where the partnership is not optional. Here the hanging image is literal: neither organism can live detached from the other.","whyCN":"生物学把这个名词用于共生，那里的伙伴关系并非可选。这里的悬挂意象是字面的：两种生物都无法脱离对方存活。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Interdependence is inter- 'between' plus dependence, from Latin dependere 'to hang from', built on de- 'down' and pendere 'hang'. The word pictures each party as a support from which the other hangs.","cn":"interdependence 是 inter-“在……之间”加 dependence，后者源自拉丁语 dependere“悬挂于”，由 de-“向下”与 pendere“悬挂”构成。这个词把每一方都画成对方悬挂其上的支点。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Latin pendere meant 'to hang, weigh'. With de- 'down from' it formed dependere, 'to hang from, be dependent on'. The image was physical before it became social.","cn":"拉丁语 pendere 意为“悬挂、称重”。加 de-“从……向下”构成 dependere“悬挂于、依赖于”。这个意象在变成社会义之前是物理的。"},{"era":"15C.–17C. ENGLISH","en":"English depend and dependence entered through French. Dependence described both physical hanging and the relation of a person or thing controlled by another.","cn":"英语 depend 与 dependence 经法语进入。dependence 既描述物理悬挂，也描述人或物受另一人控制的关系。"},{"era":"EARLY 19C.","en":"Interdependence is recorded in the early nineteenth century as 'mutual dependence'. It answered a new need: describing relationships in which no side is simply the master.","cn":"interdependence 于 19 世纪初被记录，义为“相互依赖”。它回应了一种新需要：描述没有哪一方只是主人的关系。"},{"era":"19C.–20C. BIOLOGY AND ECONOMICS","en":"Biology applied it to symbiosis, and economics to trade between specialised nations. In both fields the word named a shared fate that could help or hurt.","cn":"生物学把它用于共生，经济学把它用于专业化国家之间的贸易。两个领域里，这个词都命名一种既能造福也能致害的共同命运。"},{"era":"1970s POLITICS","en":"Keohane and Nye's theory of complex interdependence made the noun a standard term for states linked through many channels. The word then implied that force had lost some of its usefulness.","cn":"基欧汉与奈的复合相互依存理论使这个名词成为描述多渠道相连国家的标准术语。这个词由此暗示武力已部分失去效用。"},{"era":"PRESENT","en":"Modern usage covers supply chains, infrastructure, ecosystems, and families. In every case the test is the same: does the withdrawal of one party hurt the other?","cn":"现代用法覆盖供应链、基础设施、生态系统与家庭。无论哪种情况，检验标准都一样：一方退出是否会伤及另一方？"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates nouns built on the same pendere root with different prefixes; the near-meaning group separates words of reliance and linkage.","cn":"形近组区分以同一 pendere 词根但前缀不同的名词；近义组区分表示“依赖”与“连接”的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"independence","ipa":"/ˌɪndɪˈpendəns/","tag":"same root, negative prefix","definition":"freedom from control by others. Here in- negates dependence entirely, so the word is the opposite of the sense at issue.","definitionCN":"不受他人控制的自由。这里 in- 完全否定 dependence，因此这个词与前文所论的义项相反。"},{"word":"dependence","ipa":"/dɪˈpendəns/","tag":"base noun, no inter-","definition":"reliance on someone or something. It can be one-sided and is often used of addiction or burden, unlike reciprocal interdependence.","definitionCN":"对某人或某物的依赖。它可以是单方面的，常用于成瘾或负担，与相互的 interdependence 不同。"},{"word":"dependency","ipa":"/dɪˈpendənsi/","tag":"same root, different suffix","definition":"the state of relying on something, or a territory controlled by another state. The -cy form often names a concrete territory or a political relation.","definitionCN":"依赖状态，或受他国控制的属地。-cy 形式常命名具体属地或政治关系。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"reliance","ipa":"/rɪˈlaɪəns/","tag":"one side","definition":"the act of depending on someone or something. It usually describes one party's trust; interdependence requires the reliance to run both ways.","definitionCN":"依赖某人或某物的行为。它通常描述一方的信赖；interdependence 要求依赖是双向的。"},{"word":"interconnection","ipa":"/ˌɪntəkəˈnekʃn/","tag":"linkage","definition":"the state of being linked. It describes the channel itself, while interdependence describes the need that makes the channel necessary.","definitionCN":"相互连接的状态。它描述通道本身，而 interdependence 描述使通道成为必要的需要。"},{"word":"mutualism","ipa":"/ˈmjuːtʃuəlɪzəm/","tag":"biology","definition":"an ecological relationship that benefits both species. It is a specific biological category, narrower than general interdependence.","definitionCN":"对两种物种都有益的生态关系。它是一个具体的生物类别，比一般的相互依赖更窄。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real associations: depend from de- 'down' + pendere 'hang', the reciprocal inter-, and the international-relations phrase complex interdependence.","cn":"真实联想：depend 来自 de-“向下”+ pendere“悬挂”、相互的 inter-，以及国际关系术语 complex interdependence。"},"normal":[{"en":"pendere means 'hang': to depend is to hang from something, and interdependence means both sides hang from each other.","cn":"pendere 意为“悬挂”：depend 是挂在某物上，而 interdependence 是双方互相挂在对方上。"},{"en":"A pendulum and a pendant share the same root; so does the idea of being suspended.","cn":"钟摆（pendulum）与吊坠（pendant）同根，被悬置的概念也同根。"},{"en":"In trade, one country's shortage becomes everyone's shortage — that is economic interdependence.","cn":"在贸易中，一国的短缺会变成所有人的短缺——这就是经济互赖。"},{"en":"Lichens are the classic case: fungus and alga cannot live apart.","cn":"地衣是经典案例：真菌与藻类无法分离而活。"},{"en":"Complex interdependence is the political version: many channels make force expensive.","cn":"复合相互依存是政治版本：渠道众多使动武代价高昂。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The word is not about weakness; it says that support is mutual, so both sides hold a hook.","cn":"这个词不是讲软弱；它说支撑是相互的，因此双方都握着一个钩子。"},{"en":"Every interdependence cuts both ways: the same link that shares growth also shares shock.","cn":"每一种相互依赖都是双刃的：分享增长的同一连接，也分享冲击。"},{"en":"Independence removes the hook; interdependence keeps it but makes it symmetrical.","cn":"独立拆掉了钩子；相互依赖保留钩子，但让它变得对称。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Economic interdependence means that a factory closure in one country is felt in another.","cn":"经济上的相互依存意味着，一国工厂关闭会在另一国被感受到。"},{"en":"The ecosystem's interdependence became clear when one pollinator disappeared.","cn":"当一种传粉昆虫消失时，生态系统的相互依存就变得清晰。"},{"en":"Complex interdependence theory explains cooperation among trading democracies.","cn":"复合相互依存理论解释了贸易民主国家之间的合作。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因它来低盆等死”——它一来，两边的盆都低低地吊着，谁离开谁都不行 → interdependence 相互依赖","word":"interdependence"},"root":"inter-（在……之间）+ de-（向下）+ 拉丁语 pendere“悬挂”+ -ence；字面义“彼此悬挂在对方身上”，核心是“双方互为支点、无法单方松手”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of interdependence all describe support that runs both ways: people, economies, species, systems, states, firms, and organisms. The word never means simple weakness; it means that each side is a hook for the other.","cn":"interdependence 的八个义项都描述双向的支撑：人、经济体、物种、系统、国家、企业与生物。这个词从不表示单纯的软弱；它表示每一方都是对方的挂钩。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: two people each holding one end of the same ladder; if either lets go, both fall.","cn":"核心意象：两人各扶同一架梯子的一端；任一方松手，两人都会倒下。"},"chain":["TWO PARTIES","NEED","SUPPORT","RECIPROCITY","SHARED RISK","COEXISTENCE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S4","en":"PERSONAL: people need each other for care and autonomy, without one side owning the other.","cn":"个人：人们在照料与自主上彼此需要，而没有一方占有另一方。"},{"senses":"S2 · S7","en":"ECONOMIC: trade and supply chains make firms and countries share both growth and shortage.","cn":"经济：贸易与供应链让企业与国家共享增长，也共享短缺。"},{"senses":"S3 · S8","en":"ECOLOGICAL: food webs and symbioses make survival a joint condition.","cn":"生态：食物网与共生使生存成为共同条件。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"POLITICAL: many channels of contact make force costly and cooperation rational.","cn":"政治：多渠道接触使武力代价高昂、合作变得理性。"},{"senses":"S6","en":"TECHNICAL: coupled infrastructures carry failure from one system into the next.","cn":"技术：耦合的基础设施把故障从一个系统带进下一个。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Interdependence is inter- + dependence, and dependence is depend + -ence from Latin dependere. The family turns on the verb pendere 'hang', with prefixes changing who hangs from whom.","cn":"interdependence 是 inter- + dependence，而 dependence 是 depend + -ence，源自拉丁语 dependere。这个家族围绕动词 pendere“悬挂”，前缀改变的是谁挂在谁身上。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin pendere 'to hang, weigh' yields pendulus 'hanging', pendulum 'a hanging weight', and dependere 'hang from'. The same root also gives expensive and pension, where the idea is weighing out money.","cn":"拉丁语 pendere“悬挂、称重”给出 pendulus“悬挂的”、pendulum“摆”、dependere“悬挂于”。同一词根还给出 expensive 与 pension，那里的意思是“称出钱来”。"},"items":[{"word":"interdependence","structure":"inter- + dependence (-ence)","meaning":"mutual reliance","meaningCN":"相互依赖（inter- + dependence）","example":"The two industries show close interdependence.","exampleCN":"这两个行业表现出紧密的相互依赖。"},{"word":"interdependent","structure":"inter- + dependent","meaning":"relying on each other","meaningCN":"相互依赖的（-ent 构成形容词）","example":"The regions are economically interdependent.","exampleCN":"这些地区在经济上相互依赖。"},{"word":"interdependently","structure":"interdependent + -ly","meaning":"in a mutually reliant way","meaningCN":"以相互依赖的方式（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The species evolved interdependently.","exampleCN":"这些物种相互依赖地演化。"},{"word":"depend","structure":"de- (down from) + pendere (hang)","meaning":"to rely on; to be determined by","meaningCN":"依赖；取决于（字面“悬挂于”）","example":"The outcome depends on the sample size.","exampleCN":"结果取决于样本量。"},{"word":"dependent","structure":"depend + -ent","meaning":"relying on another; contingent","meaningCN":"依赖的；由……决定的（-ent 构成形容词）","example":"The project is dependent on funding.","exampleCN":"这个项目依赖资金。"},{"word":"dependence","structure":"depend + -ence","meaning":"the state of relying on something","meaningCN":"依赖；依存（-ence 构成名词）","example":"Dependence on one supplier is risky.","exampleCN":"依赖单一供应商有风险。"},{"word":"dependency","structure":"dependent + -cy","meaning":"a reliance or a dependent territory","meaningCN":"依赖关系；附属地（-cy 构成名词）","example":"The island was once a dependency.","exampleCN":"这座岛曾是附属地。"},{"word":"dependable","structure":"depend + -able","meaning":"reliable enough to be trusted","meaningCN":"可靠的（-able 表能力）","example":"She is a dependable colleague.","exampleCN":"她是一位可靠的同事。"},{"word":"independent","structure":"in- (not) + dependent","meaning":"not relying on others","meaningCN":"独立的（in- 表否定）","example":"The audit must be independent.","exampleCN":"审计必须独立。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"pendere","structure":"third-conjugation verb","meaning":"to hang, weigh, pay out","meaningCN":"悬挂；称重；付出"},{"word":"dependere","structure":"de- 'down from' + pendere 'hang'","meaning":"to hang from, depend on","meaningCN":"悬挂于；依赖"},{"word":"pendulum","structure":"neuter noun from pendere","meaning":"a hanging weight, pendulum","meaningCN":"摆；悬挂的重物"},{"word":"dependentia","structure":"dependere + -ntia (abstract noun)","meaning":"dependence","meaningCN":"依赖；依存"}]}},{"word":"interdisciplinary","ipa_uk":"/ˌɪntədɪsəˈplɪnəri/","ipa_us":"/ˌɪntərˈdɪsəpləneri/","definition_zh":"跨学科的；学科交叉的；涉及两门以上学科的","definition_en":"combining or involving two or more academic disciplines within a single project, course, team, or approach","core_image":"几间挂着不同学科牌子的教室被一条走廊打通，学生在同一张桌上拼出答案","scene":"大学实验室里，生物学家与工程师共用一张工作台。They work on an interdisciplinary project that needs both fields.","sceneCN":"这里 interdisciplinary 是「跨学科的」（第 1 个义项：涉及两门以上学科）；句意：他们做一个需要两个领域的跨学科项目。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"跨学科的（用于研究、课程、团队等，指结合多门学科）"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"学科交叉的（用于形容方法、视角或领域本身）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"interdisciplinary research","zh":"跨学科研究"},{"phrase":"interdisciplinary course","zh":"跨学科课程"},{"phrase":"interdisciplinary team","zh":"跨学科团队"},{"phrase":"interdisciplinary approach","zh":"跨学科方法"},{"phrase":"interdisciplinary program","zh":"跨学科项目"},{"phrase":"interdisciplinary collaboration","zh":"跨学科协作"}],"forms":[{"label":"形容词原级","form":"interdisciplinary"},{"label":"比较级","form":"more interdisciplinary"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most interdisciplinary"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"discipline","pos":"n./v.","zh":"学科；纪律；训练"},{"word":"disciplinary","pos":"adj.","zh":"学科的；纪律的"},{"word":"disciplinarian","pos":"n.","zh":"严格执行纪律者"},{"word":"multidisciplinary","pos":"adj.","zh":"多学科的"},{"word":"transdisciplinary","pos":"adj.","zh":"超学科的；跨学科整合的"},{"word":"cross-disciplinary","pos":"adj.","zh":"交叉学科的"},{"word":"disciplinarity","pos":"n.","zh":"学科性"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Combining disciplines in research","titleCN":"研究上结合多门学科","definition":"describing research that draws methods or data from two or more established fields to answer one question","definitionCN":"描述为回答一个问题而借用两门以上成熟学科的方法或数据的研究","example":"The interdisciplinary study combined geology and archaeology to date the eruption.","exampleCN":"这项跨学科研究结合地质学与考古学来确定喷发年代。","why":"Interdisciplinary is inter- 'between' plus disciplinary, from Latin disciplina 'instruction, knowledge'. The adjective asserts that a question sits between fields — no single discipline owns it.","whyCN":"interdisciplinary 是 inter-“在……之间”加 disciplinary，而后者源自拉丁语 disciplina“教导、知识”。这个形容词主张某个问题处在学科之间——没有哪一门学科独占它。"},{"no":"02","title":"Spanning disciplines in teaching","titleCN":"教学上横跨多门学科","definition":"describing a course or curriculum that teaches content from several fields in one programme","definitionCN":"描述在一门课程或培养方案中教授多个领域内容的课程","example":"The university offers an interdisciplinary major in climate and public policy.","exampleCN":"这所大学开设气候与公共政策方向的跨学科专业。","why":"Education uses the adjective to describe structure: one timetable, several departments. The word signals that students are expected to move between vocabularies, not to master one.","whyCN":"教育领域用这个形容词描述结构：一张课表，几个院系。这个词表明学生要在不同词汇体系之间移动，而不是精通其中一门。"},{"no":"03","title":"Working across disciplines in a team","titleCN":"团队跨学科协作","definition":"describing a group whose members are trained in different fields and share a task","definitionCN":"描述成员受训于不同领域并共担任务的团队","example":"An interdisciplinary team of engineers and physicians designed the device.","exampleCN":"由工程师与医生组成的跨学科团队设计了这台设备。","why":"Here the adjective describes people rather than knowledge: the team's strength is that no member can read the whole problem alone. The prefix marks the seam between specialisms.","whyCN":"这里的形容词描述人而不是知识：团队的力量在于没有哪个成员能独自读懂整个问题。前缀标记的正是专业之间的接缝。"},{"no":"04","title":"Borrowing methods across fields","titleCN":"方法上借用其他学科","definition":"describing an approach that applies the tools or models of one field to the problems of another","definitionCN":"描述把一个领域的工具或模型用于另一个领域问题的做法","example":"The paper takes an interdisciplinary approach, using network theory to read historical records.","exampleCN":"这篇论文采用跨学科方法，用网络理论解读历史记录。","why":"The adjective often attaches to 'approach' or 'method', where the borrowing is deliberate rather than accidental. A method becomes interdisciplinary when its assumptions are imported along with its techniques.","whyCN":"这个形容词常修饰 approach 或 method，那里的借用是有意的而非偶然。当一套方法的假设连同技术一起被引入时，它就变成跨学科的。"},{"no":"05","title":"Naming an emerging field","titleCN":"命名新兴的交叉领域","definition":"describing a field that exists only where two or more disciplines overlap, such as bioinformatics","definitionCN":"描述仅在两门或更多学科交叠处存在的领域，如生物信息学","example":"Bioinformatics is an interdisciplinary field born from biology and computer science.","exampleCN":"生物信息学是由生物学与计算机科学孕育出的交叉学科领域。","why":"When a hybrid field matures, the adjective becomes part of its name. The word then no longer describes a project but a territory that belongs to no single department.","whyCN":"当一个杂交领域成熟时，这个形容词就成为它名字的一部分。此时这个词不再描述一个项目，而描述一块不属于任何单一院系的领地。"},{"no":"06","title":"Institutional cross-department arrangement","titleCN":"机构层面的跨系安排","definition":"describing centres, institutes, or programmes set up to connect departments that normally work apart","definitionCN":"描述为连接通常各自为政的院系而设立的中心、研究所或项目","example":"The interdisciplinary centre reports to three faculties at once.","exampleCN":"这个跨学科中心同时向三个学院汇报。","why":"Universities invented such units to solve an administrative problem: budgets and appointments sit inside departments, while problems do not. The word names the exception built to cross those walls.","whyCN":"大学发明这类单位是为了解决一个管理难题：预算与人事都在院系内部，而问题不在。这个词命名的是为穿越这些墙而建的例外。"},{"no":"07","title":"An interdisciplinary perspective","titleCN":"跨学科的视角","definition":"describing an analytical view that deliberately holds several disciplinary framings at once","definitionCN":"描述有意同时持有多种学科框架的分析视角","example":"Her interdisciplinary reading of the novel draws on economics and theology.","exampleCN":"她对这部小说的跨学科解读借用了经济学与神学。","why":"This sense is about seeing, not organising: the analyst keeps two frames active and lets them correct each other. The prefix becomes a way of preventing a single frame from claiming the whole truth.","whyCN":"这个义项关乎“看”，而非“组织”：分析者让两个框架同时工作，并让它们互相纠正。前缀由此成为一种手段，防止单一框架宣称掌握全部真相。"},{"no":"08","title":"Interdisciplinary in a degree or publication","titleCN":"学位或成果的跨学科属性","definition":"describing a thesis, journal, or degree formally labelled as spanning more than one discipline","definitionCN":"描述被正式标注为横跨一门以上学科的论文、期刊或学位","example":"The dissertation was accepted as interdisciplinary work by a joint committee.","exampleCN":"这篇论文被联合委员会接受为跨学科成果。","why":"Institutions need labels for evaluation: a joint committee, a mixed methodology, a shared credit. The adjective here is a classification with real consequences for funding and hiring.","whyCN":"机构需要用于评估的标签：联合委员会、混合方法、共享学分。这里的形容词是一种分类，对经费与聘任有实际后果。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Interdisciplinary is inter- 'between' plus disciplinary, from Latin disciplina 'teaching, knowledge', itself from discipulus 'pupil' and discere 'to learn'. The compound is a twentieth-century English coinage, not a Latin word.","cn":"interdisciplinary 是 inter-“在……之间”加 disciplinary，后者源自拉丁语 disciplina“教导、知识”，而 disciplina 又来自 discipulus“学生”与 discere“学习”。这个复合词是 20 世纪英语的创造，不是拉丁语词。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Latin discere meant 'to learn'; discipulus 'pupil' and disciplina 'instruction, field of knowledge' came from it. Disciplina already carried both meanings that English still keeps: training and a branch of study.","cn":"拉丁语 discere 意为“学习”；discipulus“学生”与 disciplina“教导、知识领域”由此而来。disciplina 已经带有英语仍保留的两重含义：训练与一门学问。"},{"era":"13C.–16C. ENGLISH","en":"English discipline entered through Old French with the senses 'instruction', 'a branch of learning', and 'correction'. The punitive sense and the academic sense grew side by side from the same idea of training.","cn":"英语 discipline 经古法语进入，义为“教导”“一门学问”“纠正”。惩罚义与学术义从同一个“训练”观念中并肩生长出来。"},{"era":"19C. UNIVERSITY","en":"The modern research university organized knowledge into departments, and 'discipline' became the word for those units. Boundaries were the point: each field had its own methods and journals.","cn":"现代研究型大学把知识组织成系科，discipline 于是成为这些单位的名称。边界正是关键：每个领域有自己的方法与期刊。"},{"era":"1920s–1930s","en":"Interdisciplinary is generally dated to the 1920s and 1930s, when foundations and universities began funding work that crossed departments. The exact first use is uncertain, but the coinage is not in doubt.","cn":"interdisciplinary 一般被认为产生于 1920 至 1930 年代，当时基金会与大学开始资助跨越院系的工作。确切首次使用来源不确定，但属新造词这一点无疑。"},{"era":"20C. POST-WAR SCIENCE","en":"Cold War research projects, area studies, and later environmental science made cross-department work normal. The adjective moved from describing exceptions to naming whole programmes and fields.","cn":"冷战时期的研究项目、区域研究以及后来的环境科学使跨系工作成为常态。这个形容词从描述例外，转为命名整个项目与领域。"},{"era":"PRESENT","en":"Today the word sits beside multidisciplinary and transdisciplinary, each marking a different depth of integration. Interdisciplinary usually means fields cooperate on a shared question while keeping their methods.","cn":"今天这个词与 multidisciplinary、transdisciplinary 并列，各自标记不同的整合深度。interdisciplinary 通常指各领域围绕共同问题合作，同时保留各自的方法。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates the multi-, cross-, and trans- forms, which differ in how deeply the disciplines are integrated; the near-meaning group separates words for combined and cooperative work.","cn":"形近组区分 multi-、cross-、trans- 三种形式，它们的学科整合深度不同；近义组区分表示“结合”与“合作”的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"multidisciplinary","ipa":"/ˌmʌltidɪsəˈplɪnəri/","tag":"multi-: side by side","definition":"involving several disciplines placed next to each other. Multi- 'many' suggests parallel contributions rather than a single fused method, which is weaker integration than interdisciplinary.","definitionCN":"涉及多门学科并置。multi-“多”暗示各学科平行贡献，而不是融合成一套方法，整合程度比 interdisciplinary 弱。"},{"word":"transdisciplinary","ipa":"/ˌtrænzdɪsəˈplɪnəri/","tag":"trans-: across and beyond","definition":"crossing disciplinary boundaries so thoroughly that a new framework is created. Trans- 'across, beyond' marks deeper integration than interdisciplinary.","definitionCN":"如此彻底地穿越学科边界，以致产生新框架。trans-“越过、之外”标记比 interdisciplinary 更深的整合。"},{"word":"disciplinary","ipa":"/ˈdɪsəplɪnəri/","tag":"base word, no inter-","definition":"relating to a discipline of study, or to correction and punishment. Without inter- it stays inside one field or refers to rules.","definitionCN":"与某一学科有关的，或与惩戒有关的。没有 inter- 时，它仍在一门学科之内，或指规则。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"cross-disciplinary","ipa":"/ˌkrɒs dɪsəˈplɪnəri/","tag":"equivalent","definition":"working across the boundaries of disciplines. It is close to interdisciplinary but more often describes a single crossing, such as a team drawn from two departments.","definitionCN":"跨越学科边界工作。它接近 interdisciplinary，但更常描述单次跨越，例如由两个院系组成的团队。"},{"word":"integrated","ipa":"/ˈɪntɪɡreɪtɪd/","tag":"result","definition":"combined into a working whole. It describes the outcome, while interdisciplinary describes the range of fields involved.","definitionCN":"结合成一个可运转的整体。它描述结果，而 interdisciplinary 描述所涉领域的范围。"},{"word":"collaborative","ipa":"/kəˈlæbərətɪv/","tag":"process","definition":"involving people working together. It names the cooperation itself, not the academic disciplines of the participants.","definitionCN":"涉及人们一起工作的。它命名合作本身，而不是参与者的学科归属。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real associations: inter- 'between' + disciplina 'knowledge', the department walls of the modern university, and the standard phrases interdisciplinary research and interdisciplinary team.","cn":"真实联想：inter-“在……之间”+ disciplina“知识”、现代大学的院系之墙，以及 interdisciplinary research、interdisciplinary team 等标准说法。"},"normal":[{"en":"inter- means 'between': interdisciplinary work happens in the corridor between two departments, not in either office.","cn":"inter- 意为“在……之间”：跨学科工作发生在两个院系之间的走廊里，而不在任何一间办公室。"},{"en":"discipline means both 'a field of study' and 'training', so the word is about trained fields meeting.","cn":"discipline 既指“一门学问”，也指“训练”，所以这个词讲的是受过训练的领域相遇。"},{"en":"A bioinformatics lab is the clearest picture: half computer science, half biology, one room.","cn":"生物信息学实验室是最清楚的画面：一半计算机科学，一半生物学，同一间屋子。"},{"en":"If two fields merely sit side by side, say multidisciplinary; if they fuse, say interdisciplinary.","cn":"两门学科只是并排放着，就用 multidisciplinary；如果融合了，就用 interdisciplinary。"},{"en":"An interdisciplinary degree is judged by a joint committee because no single department owns it.","cn":"跨学科学位由联合委员会评定，因为没有哪个院系独占它。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The word does not mean 'knowing a little of everything'; it means holding two rigorous methods at once.","cn":"这个词不是“什么都懂一点”；它指同时持有两套严谨的方法。"},{"en":"Its value is the seam: at the boundary each discipline is forced to explain assumptions it normally hides.","cn":"它的价值在接缝处：在边界上，每门学科都被迫解释它平时藏起来的假设。"},{"en":"Departments organize knowledge; interdisciplinary work organizes questions, and questions do not respect walls.","cn":"院系组织知识；跨学科工作组织问题，而问题不尊重围墙。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The interdisciplinary project brought together geologists and historians.","cn":"这个跨学科项目把地质学家与历史学家聚到一起。"},{"en":"She chose an interdisciplinary major combining economics and environmental science.","cn":"她选择了结合经济学与环境科学的跨学科专业。"},{"en":"Interdisciplinary research is often judged by committees drawn from several faculties.","cn":"跨学科研究常由来自多个学院的委员会评审。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因它来，弟子扑来呢”——它一来，几门学科的弟子都扑到一张桌子上 → interdisciplinary 跨学科的","word":"interdisciplinary"},"root":"inter-（在……之间）+ 拉丁语 discere“学习”/discipulus“学生”/disciplina“教导、学问”+ -ary；字面义“处于学科之间的”，核心是“多门学科围绕同一问题合作”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of interdisciplinary all place a question, course, team, method, field, centre, reading, or degree between established disciplines. The word marks a seam rather than a mixture: fields cooperate while keeping their own standards.","cn":"interdisciplinary 的八个义项都把某个问题、课程、团队、方法、领域、中心、解读或学位放在成熟学科之间。这个词标记的是一条接缝，而不是一锅混合：各领域合作，同时保留各自的标准。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: several classrooms with different subject signs joined by one corridor, all working at one table.","cn":"核心意象：几间挂着不同学科牌子的教室由一条走廊连通，共用一张桌子工作。"},"chain":["DISCIPLINE","BOUNDARY","QUESTION","BORROWING","COOPERATION","NEW FIELD"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S4","en":"METHOD: research and analysis borrow tools across a boundary while keeping each field's assumptions visible.","cn":"方法：研究与分析跨边界借用工具，同时让每个领域的假设保持可见。"},{"senses":"S2 · S8","en":"INSTITUTION: courses, degrees, and joint committees are formal arrangements for crossing walls.","cn":"制度：课程、学位与联合委员会是为穿墙而设的正式安排。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"PEOPLE: a team is interdisciplinary when no member can read the whole problem alone.","cn":"人：当没有成员能独自读懂整个问题时，团队就是跨学科的。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"FIELD: a hybrid subject such as bioinformatics exists only in the overlap.","cn":"领域：生物信息学这类杂交学科只存在于交叠处。"},{"senses":"S6 · S7","en":"PERSPECTIVE: centres and cross-readings keep two frames active so neither claims the whole truth.","cn":"视角：中心与交叉解读让两个框架同时工作，使任何一方都不能宣称掌握全部真相。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Interdisciplinary is inter- + disciplinary, and disciplinary is discipline + -ary. Discipline comes from Latin disciplina. The affix set contrasts the multi-, cross-, and trans- variants with the base word.","cn":"interdisciplinary 是 inter- + disciplinary，而 disciplinary 是 discipline + -ary。discipline 源自拉丁语 disciplina。词缀组把 multi-、cross-、trans- 各变体与基础词对照起来。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin disciplina 'instruction, knowledge' derives from discipulus 'pupil', from discere 'to learn'. The older link to docere 'to teach' is generally accepted but the exact derivation is debated, so it is marked as probable rather than certain.","cn":"拉丁语 disciplina“教导、知识”源自 discipulus“学生”，而 discipulus 又来自 discere“学习”。它与 docere“教”的更早关联一般被认为是成立的，但确切派生过程有争议，因此标为“一般认为”而非确定。"},"items":[{"word":"interdisciplinary","structure":"inter- + disciplinary","meaning":"spanning more than one field of study","meaningCN":"跨学科的（inter- + disciplinary）","example":"The centre runs interdisciplinary research.","exampleCN":"这个中心开展跨学科研究。"},{"word":"discipline","structure":"Latin disciplina 'instruction, knowledge'","meaning":"a field of study; controlled training","meaningCN":"学科；纪律；训练（直接借自拉丁名词）","example":"History is a demanding discipline.","exampleCN":"历史学是一门要求很高的学科。"},{"word":"disciplinary","structure":"discipline + -ary","meaning":"relating to a field or to correction","meaningCN":"学科的；纪律的（-ary 构成形容词）","example":"The paper crosses disciplinary lines.","exampleCN":"这篇论文跨越学科界线。"},{"word":"disciplinarian","structure":"discipline + -arian","meaning":"one who enforces strict rules","meaningCN":"严格执行纪律者（-arian 表人）","example":"The coach was a strict disciplinarian.","exampleCN":"这位教练严格执行纪律。"},{"word":"disciplinarity","structure":"disciplinary + -ity","meaning":"the quality of belonging to a discipline","meaningCN":"学科性（-ity 构成抽象名词）","example":"The essay questions traditional disciplinarity.","exampleCN":"这篇文章质疑传统的学科性。"},{"word":"multidisciplinary","structure":"multi- (many) + disciplinary","meaning":"using several disciplines side by side","meaningCN":"多学科的（multi-“多”+ disciplinary）","example":"A multidisciplinary panel reviewed the plan.","exampleCN":"一个多学科小组评审了这项方案。"},{"word":"transdisciplinary","structure":"trans- (across, beyond) + disciplinary","meaning":"crossing disciplines to build a new frame","meaningCN":"超学科的（trans-“越过”+ disciplinary）","example":"Transdisciplinary work dissolves old boundaries.","exampleCN":"超学科工作消解旧的边界。"},{"word":"cross-disciplinary","structure":"cross- + disciplinary","meaning":"working across disciplinary lines","meaningCN":"交叉学科的（cross- + disciplinary）","example":"The grant supports cross-disciplinary teams.","exampleCN":"这笔资助支持交叉学科团队。"},{"word":"undisciplined","structure":"un- (not) + disciplined","meaning":"lacking training or control","meaningCN":"缺乏训练的；无纪律的（un- 表否定）","example":"The undisciplined method produced noisy data.","exampleCN":"缺乏规范的方法产生了嘈杂的数据。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"discere","structure":"third-conjugation verb","meaning":"to learn","meaningCN":"学习"},{"word":"discipulus","structure":"discere + -pulus (agent noun)","meaning":"pupil, learner","meaningCN":"学生；学习者"},{"word":"disciplina","structure":"discipulus + -ina (abstract noun)","meaning":"instruction, knowledge, a branch of study","meaningCN":"教导；知识；一门学问"},{"word":"doctor","structure":"docere 'teach' + -tor (agent noun)","meaning":"teacher; the root is related but the exact path is debated","meaningCN":"教师；词根与 discere 相关，但确切派生路径有争议（来源不确定）"}]}},{"word":"interpretation","ipa_uk":"/ɪnˌtɜːprɪˈteɪʃn/","ipa_us":"/ɪnˌtɜːrprɪˈteɪʃn/","definition_zh":"解释；理解；诠释；（口译）翻译；（艺术作品的）演绎；（数据或证据的）解读","definition_en":"the act of explaining the meaning of something, or the meaning given to it; an explanation, an oral translation, or a performer's realization of a work","core_image":"两人隔河相对，一人把对岸的话转述过来，还要让听者真正听懂","scene":"国际会议上，译员戴着耳机把发言人的话转成中文。The live interpretation let the audience follow the speech.","sceneCN":"这里 interpretation 是「口译」（第 5 个义项：把一种语言的话当场转成另一种语言）；句意：这场现场口译让听众跟得上发言。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"解释；理解；诠释（可数指一种解释，不可数指解释行为）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（专业）口译；艺术演绎；数据解读（常带修饰语，如 simultaneous interpretation）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"simultaneous interpretation","zh":"同声传译"},{"phrase":"interpretation of data","zh":"对数据的解读"},{"phrase":"a matter of interpretation","zh":"解释角度的问题"},{"phrase":"judicial interpretation","zh":"司法解释"},{"phrase":"alternative interpretation","zh":"另一种解读"},{"phrase":"interpretation of a text","zh":"对文本的诠释"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"interpretation"},{"label":"复数","form":"interpretations"},{"label":"作定语（名词修饰名词）","form":"interpretation service"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"interpret","pos":"v.","zh":"解释；理解为；口译"},{"word":"interpreter","pos":"n.","zh":"口译员；解释者"},{"word":"interpretive","pos":"adj.","zh":"解释性的；诠释的"},{"word":"interpretative","pos":"adj.","zh":"解释性的；演绎的"},{"word":"misinterpret","pos":"v.","zh":"误解；曲解"},{"word":"reinterpret","pos":"v.","zh":"重新解释"},{"word":"interpretable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可解释的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Explanation of meaning","titleCN":"对含义的解释","definition":"the act of making the meaning of something clear, or the explanation produced","definitionCN":"把某事物的含义讲清楚的行为，或由此产生的说明","example":"The guide's interpretation of the poem was both clear and cautious.","exampleCN":"导览者对这首诗的解释既清晰又谨慎。","why":"Interpretation is interpret + -ation. Interpret goes back to Latin interpretari 'to explain, expound', from interpres 'agent, translator'. The suffix names both the act and its product, so one word covers the explaining and the explanation.","whyCN":"interpretation 是 interpret + -ation。interpret 上溯拉丁语 interpretari“解释、阐明”，源自 interpres“中间人、译者”。后缀同时命名行为与产物，因此一个词既指解释的过程，也指解释的结果。"},{"no":"02","title":"A particular reading","titleCN":"一种特定的理解","definition":"the meaning that a particular person or group takes from something, especially when other readings are possible","definitionCN":"某个人或群体从某事物中读出的含义，尤指存在其他解读可能时","example":"Her interpretation of the results differs sharply from the authors'.","exampleCN":"她对结果的解读与作者们的解读截然不同。","why":"Because an interpres stands between two parties, the noun naturally implies a viewpoint rather than the single truth. This is why the word is often followed by 'of' and preceded by a possessive: whose reading is it?","whyCN":"因为 interpres 站在两方之间，这个名词天然暗示一种视角，而不是唯一真理。所以它常接 of，前面带所有格：这是谁的理解？"},{"no":"03","title":"Realization of an artwork","titleCN":"对艺术作品的演绎","definition":"the way a performer or director realizes a written work, giving it a particular shape in performance","definitionCN":"表演者或导演把写定的作品实现出来的方式，赋予其特定形态","example":"The director's interpretation moves the play into the present day.","exampleCN":"导演的演绎把这部戏搬到了当代。","why":"Performance makes the 'between' literal: the artist stands between the score or script and the audience, and what the audience hears is one realization among many possible ones.","whyCN":"表演把“在之间”变得字面化：艺术家站在乐谱或剧本与观众之间，观众听到的是众多可能实现中的一种。"},{"no":"04","title":"Legal interpretation","titleCN":"法律上的解释","definition":"the process by which courts determine what a statute or clause means and how it applies","definitionCN":"法院确定法条或条款含义及其如何适用的过程","example":"The ruling turned on the court's interpretation of a single phrase.","exampleCN":"这项判决取决于法院对某一个短语的解释。","why":"Law separates the text from its application, and interpretation is the bridge. The word here carries authority: one official reading settles what the words will mean for everyone.","whyCN":"法律把文本与适用分开，而解释就是那座桥。这个词在此带有权威：一种官方解读决定了这些字对所有人意味着什么。"},{"no":"05","title":"Oral translation","titleCN":"口译","definition":"the act of translating spoken language in real time from one language into another","definitionCN":"把口语当场从一种语言转换成另一种语言的行为","example":"Simultaneous interpretation allowed the delegates to follow in six languages.","exampleCN":"同声传译让代表们可以用六种语言跟上发言。","why":"The Latin interpres was a negotiator or go-between, and translation is the oldest concrete form of standing between two parties. The noun kept this sense while the adjective interpreter became the person's title.","whyCN":"拉丁语 interpres 是谈判者或中间人，而翻译是“站在两方之间”最古老的具体形式。名词保留了这一义，而 interpeter 一词则成为这个人的头衔。"},{"no":"06","title":"Interpretation of data","titleCN":"对数据的解读","definition":"the process of deciding what measurements or observations mean, beyond the numbers themselves","definitionCN":"在数字之外判定测量或观察结果意味着什么的过程","example":"The same data permit a cautious interpretation and an alarming one.","exampleCN":"同样的数据可以引出谨慎的解读，也可以引出令人警觉的解读。","why":"Science uses the word to draw a line between recording and concluding. Interpretation is where assumptions enter, which is why methods sections describe statistics but discussion sections interpret.","whyCN":"科学用这个词在记录与结论之间划一条线。解释正是假设进入的地方，所以方法部分描述统计，讨论部分才做解读。"},{"no":"07","title":"Musical realization","titleCN":"音乐上的演绎","definition":"a performer's or conductor's shaping of a piece, including tempo, phrasing, and tone","definitionCN":"演奏者或指挥对作品的处理，包括速度、分句与音色","example":"Two pianists gave radically different interpretations of the same sonata.","exampleCN":"两位钢琴家对同一首奏鸣曲给出了完全不同的演绎。","why":"Music makes interpretation audible: the notes are fixed, but tempo and phrasing are decisions. The word measures how much of the performer is present in the sound.","whyCN":"音乐让解释变得可听：音符是固定的，速度与分句却是决定。这个词衡量的是声音里有多少演奏者本人。"},{"no":"08","title":"Psychoanalytic interpretation","titleCN":"精神分析中的解释","definition":"the analyst's explanation of a dream, symptom, or slip as expressing a hidden conflict","definitionCN":"分析者对梦、症状或口误的解释，认为它们表达了隐藏的冲突","example":"Freud's interpretation of dreams treated images as disguised wishes.","exampleCN":"弗洛伊德对梦的解释把意象视为被伪装起来的愿望。","why":"Psychoanalysis pushed the word toward uncovering: the text to be read is the patient's own behaviour, and the interpres claims access to a meaning the speaker cannot see. This sense is the most contested of the eight.","whyCN":"精神分析把这个词推向“揭开幕布”：要读的文本是病人自己的行为，而解释者声称能触及说话者自己看不见的意义。这是八个义项中最具争议的一个。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Interpretation is interpret + -ation. Interpret comes from Latin interpretari 'to explain, expound', from interpres (genitive interpretis) 'agent, go-between, translator'. The deeper origin of interpres is uncertain: the common proposal is inter- 'between' plus a root related to pretium 'price', picturing a broker who sets a value between two parties.","cn":"interpretation 是 interpret + -ation。interpret 源自拉丁语 interpretari“解释、阐明”，来自 interpres（属格 interpretis）“中间人、译者”。interpres 的更早来源不确定：常见说法是 inter-“在……之间”加一个与 pretium“价格”相关的词根，描绘在双方之间定价的经纪人。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Latin interpres named a go-between, especially a negotiator or translator. The verb interpretari meant 'to act as go-between, expound, translate'. The noun interpretatio named the explaining and its result.","cn":"拉丁语 interpres 指中间人，尤指谈判者或译者。动词 interpretari 意为“充当中间人、阐明、翻译”。名词 interpretatio 命名解释行为及其结果。"},{"era":"ORIGIN UNCERTAIN","en":"The internal structure of interpres is disputed. The most cited proposal links inter- 'between' with pretium 'price', as if a broker who names a value between buyer and seller; other accounts leave the second element unexplained. No reconstruction is treated here as certain.","cn":"interpres 的内部结构有争议。最常被引用的说法把 inter-“在……之间”与 pretium“价格”联系起来，仿佛在买卖双方之间定价的经纪人；其他说法则未解释第二个成分。此处不把任何重构视为确定。"},{"era":"14C.–15C. ENGLISH","en":"English interpret and interpretation entered through Old French. Early uses covered explaining texts and translating speech, the two roles the Latin word already joined.","cn":"英语 interpret 与 interpretation 经古法语进入。早期用法涵盖解释文本与翻译话语，正是拉丁语词原本兼有的两种角色。"},{"era":"16C.–17C. LAW AND THEOLOGY","en":"Reformation disputes and legal practice made interpretation a technical matter: who has authority to say what a text means. The noun acquired its weight of official decision.","cn":"宗教改革争论与法律实践使 interpretation 成为技术问题：谁有权断定文本的含义。这个名词由此获得了官方裁决的分量。"},{"era":"18C.–19C. MUSIC AND SCIENCE","en":"Music criticism applied the word to performance, and scientific writing applied it to data. In both cases the fixed text or measurements had to be turned into meaning.","cn":"音乐评论把这个词用于演奏，科学写作把它用于数据。两种情况里，固定的文本或测量都必须被转化为意义。"},{"era":"20C. PSYCHOANALYSIS AND LAW","en":"Freud made dream interpretation a therapeutic technique, and modern courts built doctrines of statutory interpretation. The word now spans the most private and the most public kinds of reading.","cn":"弗洛伊德使释梦成为治疗方法，现代法院则建立了法条解释学说。这个词如今同时覆盖最私密与最公共的阅读。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates inter- nouns built on different Latin verbs; the near-meaning group separates explanation, translation, and reading.","cn":"形近组区分以 inter- 开头但词根动词不同的名词；近义组区分解释、翻译与解读。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"interpolation","ipa":"/ɪnˌtɜːpəˈleɪʃn/","tag":"different root: polire 'polish'","definition":"the insertion of extra material into a text or of a value between known points. Latin interpolare meant 'refurbish, insert', built on polire 'polish', not on interpres.","definitionCN":"在文本中插入额外材料，或在已知点之间插入数值。拉丁语 interpolare 意为“翻新、插入”，建立在 polire“打磨”之上，而非 interpres。"},{"word":"interpellation","ipa":"/ɪnˌtɜːpəˈleɪʃn/","tag":"different root: pellere 'drive'","definition":"the act of interrupting with a question, or a theory of how identity is summoned. It comes from interpellare 'interrupt', from pellere 'drive', a different root.","definitionCN":"以提问打断的行为，或关于身份如何被召唤的理论。它来自 interpellare“打断”，词根为 pellere“驱动”，与前述不同。"},{"word":"interrogation","ipa":"/ɪnˌterəˈɡeɪʃn/","tag":"different root: rogare 'ask'","definition":"formal or aggressive questioning. Latin interrogare joins inter- with rogare 'ask'; it names asking, not explaining.","definitionCN":"正式或强硬的提问。拉丁语 interrogare 由 inter- 与 rogare“问”构成；它命名提问，而非解释。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"explanation","ipa":"/ˌekspləˈneɪʃn/","tag":"making clear","definition":"a statement that makes something understandable. It stresses clarity for the listener; interpretation stresses the act of construing meaning, which may remain disputed.","definitionCN":"使某事物可被理解的说明。它强调对听者的清晰；interpretation 强调建构意义的行为，而该意义可能仍有争议。"},{"word":"translation","ipa":"/trænsˈleɪʃn/","tag":"language transfer","definition":"the rendering of text or speech from one language into another. It covers the linguistic task; interpretation often means the spoken, real-time version of it.","definitionCN":"把文本或话语从一种语言转成另一种语言。它涵盖语言转换任务；interpretation 常指其中口语、实时的那一种。"},{"word":"reading","ipa":"/ˈriːdɪŋ/","tag":"informal","definition":"an understanding of a text or situation. It is the everyday word; interpretation is the formal one and carries more weight of method and authority.","definitionCN":"对文本或情境的一种理解。它是日常用词；interpretation 是正式用词，承载更多方法与权威的分量。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real associations: Latin interpres 'go-between', the two roles of explaining and translating, and the standard phrases simultaneous interpretation and interpretation of data.","cn":"真实联想：拉丁语 interpres“中间人”、解释与翻译这两种角色，以及 simultaneous interpretation、interpretation of data 等标准说法。"},"normal":[{"en":"interpres was a go-between: interpretation is what happens in the space between a text and a reader.","cn":"interpres 是中间人：interpretation 就是发生在文本与读者之间的事。"},{"en":"The word covers both the act and the result, so 'an interpretation' can be a sentence or a whole performance.","cn":"这个词兼指行为与结果，所以 an interpretation 可以是一句话，也可以是一整场演出。"},{"en":"In a concert, the notes are fixed and the interpretation is the pianist's decisions.","cn":"音乐会上音符是固定的，interpretation 是钢琴家做出的决定。"},{"en":"In court, interpretation decides what the words will mean for everyone.","cn":"在法庭上，interpretation 决定这些字对所有人意味着什么。"},{"en":"In science, methods record and discussion interprets — the line is marked by that word.","cn":"在科学里，方法记录、讨论解释——这条线就由这个词标出。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The word insists that meaning is not simply present in a text; someone must stand between and carry it across.","cn":"这个词坚持：意义并不现成地躺在文本里；必须有人站在中间把它带过去。"},{"en":"Because it names a viewpoint, it makes disagreement legitimate: two interpretations can both be careful.","cn":"因为它命名一种视角，它使分歧变得正当：两种解释都可以是谨慎的。"},{"en":"Every interpretation adds a reader to the text, and that addition is both the risk and the value.","cn":"每一次解释都在文本上增添了一个读者，这份增添既是风险，也是价值。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The two historians offered opposite interpretations of the same treaty.","cn":"两位历史学家对同一条约给出了相反的解释。"},{"en":"Simultaneous interpretation was provided in five languages at the summit.","cn":"峰会以五种语言提供同声传译。"},{"en":"The survey data are open to more than one interpretation.","cn":"这份调查数据可以有不止一种解读。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因它扑来泰神”——它一扑上来，就在两方之间把话“抬升”过去 → interpretation 解释、口译、演绎","word":"interpretation"},"root":"inter-（在……之间）+ 拉丁语 interpres“中间人、译者”（更早来源不确定，常见说法与 pretium“价格”相关）+ -ation；核心是“站在两方之间把意义传过去”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of interpretation all place someone between a text, a score, a law, a language, or a data set and the people who need its meaning. The differences lie in what is being carried across and who has the authority to carry it.","cn":"interpretation 的八个义项都把某人置于文本、乐谱、法律、语言或数据与需要其含义的人之间。差别在于被运送的是什么，以及谁有运送的权威。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: two people on opposite banks; one carries the other's words across and makes them understood.","cn":"核心意象：两人隔河而立；一人把对方的话带过河，并让听者听懂。"},"chain":["TEXT","GO-BETWEEN","MEANING","CARRYING ACROSS","READER OR LISTENER","UNDERSTANDING"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"MEANING: explaining a text and holding a particular reading are two sides of the same construing act.","cn":"意义：解释文本与持有一种解读，是同一建构行为的两个侧面。"},{"senses":"S3 · S7","en":"PERFORMANCE: a script or score is realized in sound or action, one version among many.","cn":"表演：剧本或乐谱在声音与行动中被实现，是众多版本之一。"},{"senses":"S4","en":"LAW: an official reading settles what the words mean in practice.","cn":"法律：官方解读决定这些字在实践中意味着什么。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"LANGUAGE: the interpreter stands between two languages in real time.","cn":"语言：口译员实时站在两种语言之间。"},{"senses":"S6 · S8","en":"UNCOVERING: data and dreams must be read for a meaning that is not printed on their surface.","cn":"揭示：数据与梦都必须被读出其表面未印出的意义。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Interpretation is interpret + -ation, from Latin interpretari and interpres. The affix family includes the agent noun interpreter, the two adjective forms interpretive and interpretative, and the productive prefix mis- and re-.","cn":"interpretation 是 interpret + -ation，源自拉丁语 interpretari 与 interpres。词缀家族包括施动名词 interpreter、两个形容词形式 interpretive 与 interpretative，以及能产的 mis- 与 re- 前缀。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin interpres (genitive interpretis) 'go-between' produced interpretari 'explain, translate' and interpretatio 'explanation'. The etymology of interpres itself is disputed; the link with pretium 'price' is a common proposal, not an established fact.","cn":"拉丁语 interpres（属格 interpretis）“中间人”产生 interpretari“解释、翻译”与 interpretatio“解释”。interpres 本身的词源有争议；与 pretium“价格”的联系是常见说法，而非既定事实。"},"items":[{"word":"interpretation","structure":"interpret + -ation","meaning":"the act or result of explaining meaning","meaningCN":"解释；诠释（-ation 构成名词）","example":"Her interpretation of the poem was persuasive.","exampleCN":"她对这首诗的诠释很有说服力。"},{"word":"interpret","structure":"Latin interpretari 'explain, translate'","meaning":"to explain; to understand as; to translate orally","meaningCN":"解释；理解为；口译（源自拉丁动词）","example":"How do you interpret this clause?","exampleCN":"你如何理解这一条款？"},{"word":"interpreter","structure":"interpret + -er (agent)","meaning":"one who translates speech or explains","meaningCN":"口译员；解释者（-er 表施动者）","example":"The interpreter worked without a break.","exampleCN":"口译员一刻不停地工作。"},{"word":"interpretive","structure":"interpret + -ive","meaning":"serving to explain or reveal meaning","meaningCN":"解释性的；诠释的（-ive 构成形容词）","example":"The museum offers interpretive signs.","exampleCN":"博物馆设有解说牌。"},{"word":"interpretative","structure":"interpret + -ative","meaning":"relating to interpretation, especially in performance","meaningCN":"解释性的；演绎的（-ative 构成形容词）","example":"Her interpretative choices divided critics.","exampleCN":"她的演绎选择让评论界意见分歧。"},{"word":"misinterpret","structure":"mis- (wrongly) + interpret","meaning":"to understand or explain wrongly","meaningCN":"误解；曲解（mis- 表错误）","example":"The press misinterpreted his silence.","exampleCN":"媒体误解了他的沉默。"},{"word":"reinterpret","structure":"re- (again) + interpret","meaning":"to explain in a new way","meaningCN":"重新解释（re- 表再次）","example":"Each generation reinterprets the classics.","exampleCN":"每一代人都重新解释经典。"},{"word":"interpretable","structure":"interpret + -able","meaning":"able to be explained or understood","meaningCN":"可解释的（-able 表可能）","example":"The results are interpretable but incomplete.","exampleCN":"结果可以解释，但并不完整。"},{"word":"interpretation","structure":"interpret + -ation (second nominal use)","meaning":"a formal statement of meaning in law or criticism","meaningCN":"（法律、批评中的）正式解释","example":"The court issued a narrow interpretation.","exampleCN":"法院给出了狭义解释。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"interpres","structure":"interpres, interpretis (third declension); deeper origin uncertain","meaning":"go-between, negotiator, translator","meaningCN":"中间人；谈判者；译者（更早来源不确定）"},{"word":"interpretari","structure":"interpres + -ari (verb)","meaning":"to explain, expound, translate","meaningCN":"解释；阐明；翻译"},{"word":"interpretatio","structure":"interpretari + -tio (action noun)","meaning":"explanation, interpretation","meaningCN":"解释；诠释"},{"word":"pretium","structure":"second-declension noun; proposed but unproven link","meaning":"price, value","meaningCN":"价格；价值（与 interpres 的关联为推测，来源不确定）"}]}},{"word":"interpretative","ipa_uk":"/ɪnˈtɜːprɪtətɪv/","ipa_us":"/ɪnˈtɜːrprɪteɪtɪv/","definition_zh":"解释的；诠释性的；（艺术表演）演绎的；带解读性质的","definition_en":"relating to interpretation; serving to explain or reveal meaning, especially in scholarship, law, exhibition texts, or performance","core_image":"一个人举着放大镜看画，把画里藏的线索引给旁边的人看","scene":"美术馆里，策展人指着画旁的小牌子。The label is interpretative text that explains the symbols in the painting.","sceneCN":"这里 interpretative 是「诠释性的」（第 1 个义项：用于解释含义的）；句意：说明牌是诠释性文字，解释画中的象征。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"解释的；诠释性的（用于说明文字、研究、法律解释等）"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"演绎的；带个人解读的（用于表演、艺术处理）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"interpretative text","zh":"诠释性文字；解说文字"},{"phrase":"interpretative approach","zh":"诠释性方法"},{"phrase":"interpretative dance","zh":"表现性舞蹈"},{"phrase":"interpretative flexibility","zh":"解释上的弹性"},{"phrase":"interpretative framework","zh":"解释框架"},{"phrase":"interpretative statement","zh":"解释性声明"}],"forms":[{"label":"形容词原级（英式常见形式）","form":"interpretative"},{"label":"同义变体（更常用）","form":"interpretive"},{"label":"比较级","form":"more interpretative"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"interpret","pos":"v.","zh":"解释；理解为；口译"},{"word":"interpretation","pos":"n.","zh":"解释；诠释；口译"},{"word":"interpreter","pos":"n.","zh":"口译员；解释者"},{"word":"interpretive","pos":"adj.","zh":"解释性的；诠释的"},{"word":"interpretatively","pos":"adv.","zh":"以诠释的方式"},{"word":"interpretivism","pos":"n.","zh":"诠释主义（社会科学方法论）"},{"word":"misinterpret","pos":"v.","zh":"误解；曲解"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Serving to explain","titleCN":"起解释作用的","definition":"describing writing, labels, or speech that explains the meaning of something to an audience","definitionCN":"描述向受众解释某事物含义的文字、标签或话语","example":"Interpretative panels guide visitors through the old factory.","exampleCN":"解说牌引导观众参观这座旧工厂。","why":"Interpretative is interpret + -ative, an adjective of function: it names what a text or object is for. The Latin verb interpretari meant 'to expound', so the suffix makes the explaining into a purpose.","whyCN":"interpretative 是 interpret + -ative，一个表示功能用途的形容词：它命名一个文本或物件是用来做什么的。拉丁动词 interpretari 意为“阐明”，后缀把解释变成一种用途。"},{"no":"02","title":"Scholarly reading","titleCN":"学术上的诠释性","definition":"describing research or criticism that proposes a reading of texts, events, or evidence","definitionCN":"描述提出对文本、事件或证据之解读的研究或批评","example":"The book is more interpretative than descriptive.","exampleCN":"这本书偏诠释而非描述。","why":"Scholarship distinguishes description from interpretation: the first records, the second argues for a meaning. The adjective marks work that takes that second step and therefore invites disagreement.","whyCN":"学术区分描述与诠释：前者记录，后者为某种意义辩护。这个形容词标记迈出第二步的工作，因此也招来异议。"},{"no":"03","title":"Realized in performance","titleCN":"以表演方式演绎的","definition":"describing a performance that presents one chosen reading of a work rather than a neutral delivery","definitionCN":"描述呈现某种选定解读、而非中性呈现的表演","example":"The production offered an interpretative reading of the final scene.","exampleCN":"这版制作对最后一幕作了演绎性解读。","why":"Performance cannot avoid choice: tempo, casting, and staging all decide meaning. The adjective acknowledges that choice instead of hiding it behind 'faithful' delivery.","whyCN":"表演无法回避选择：速度、选角与舞台调度都在决定意义。这个形容词承认这种选择，而不是把它藏在“忠实呈现”后面。"},{"no":"04","title":"Interpretative in law","titleCN":"法律解释上的","definition":"describing a doctrine, ruling, or statement that sets out how a legal text should be understood","definitionCN":"描述阐明法律文本应如何被理解的学说、裁决或声明","example":"The agency issued an interpretative rule rather than a binding regulation.","exampleCN":"该机构发布的是解释性规则，而非有约束力的法规。","why":"In law the adjective signals a distinction of force: an interpretative document explains the agency's reading but may not carry the same legal weight as a regulation.","whyCN":"在法律中，这个形容词标记效力上的区别：解释性文件说明机构的解读，但其法律分量可能不等同于法规。"},{"no":"05","title":"Hermeneutic in philosophy","titleCN":"哲学诠释学意义上的","definition":"describing the view that understanding always involves interpretation by a situated observer","definitionCN":"描述“理解总是涉及处于特定处境的观察者的解释”这一观点","example":"Interpretative theory holds that no observation is entirely neutral.","exampleCN":"诠释理论认为没有哪种观察是完全中立的。","why":"Hermeneutics generalised the adjective: if all understanding is interpretation, then every description already carries a reading. The word becomes a claim about knowledge, not about texts.","whyCN":"诠释学把这个形容词普遍化：如果一切理解都是解释，那么每一种描述都已带着解读。这个词由此成为关于知识的主张，而不只是关于文本。"},{"no":"06","title":"Subjective or personal reading","titleCN":"带主观解读成分的","definition":"describing an account that reflects the observer's own perspective more than the object itself","definitionCN":"描述更多反映观察者自身视角而非对象本身的叙述","example":"His interpretative account of the strike emphasized motives over dates.","exampleCN":"他对罢工的解读性叙述更重动机而轻日期。","why":"This sense carries a warning as well as a description: interpretative work may be insightful or may simply project. The adjective leaves the judgement open, which is why it is often followed by 'rather than factual'.","whyCN":"这个义项既描述也提醒：诠释性工作可能很有洞见，也可能只是投射。形容词把判断留空，所以常接 rather than factual。"},{"no":"07","title":"Interpretative with data or evidence","titleCN":"对数据或证据作解读的","definition":"describing analysis that assigns meaning to findings rather than merely reporting them","definitionCN":"描述赋予研究结果以意义、而不只是报告结果的分析","example":"The interpretative section of the report explains why the trend matters.","exampleCN":"报告的解读部分说明这一趋势为何重要。","why":"Reports separate findings from interpretation so that readers can check the first against the second. The adjective marks the part where judgement enters the chain.","whyCN":"报告把发现与解释分开，好让读者用前者核对后者。这个形容词标记判断进入链条的那一部分。"},{"no":"08","title":"Interpretative art form","titleCN":"表现性艺术形式的","definition":"describing a style such as interpretative dance that conveys meaning through expressive movement rather than literal narrative","definitionCN":"描述表现性舞蹈这类通过富有意味的动作而非字面叙事传达意义的风格","example":"The festival opened with an interpretative dance about migration.","exampleCN":"艺术节以一支关于迁徙的表现性舞蹈开幕。","why":"The arts use the adjective for works that translate an idea into another medium instead of describing it. The audience is asked to read the movement, so the word keeps its oldest meaning: carrying meaning across.","whyCN":"艺术领域用这个形容词指把某个观念转换到另一种媒介、而非直接描述的作品。观众被要求去读这些动作，因此这个词保留了最古老的含义：把意义运送过去。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Interpretative is interpret + -ative, formed in English on the Latin verb interpretari and its noun interpres 'go-between'. Interpretive is the shorter variant, and both are standard; interpretative is older in British usage.","cn":"interpretative 是 interpret + -ative，在英语中由拉丁动词 interpretari 及其名词 interpres“中间人”构成。interpretive 是较短的变体，两者都是标准形式；interpretative 在英式用法中更早。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Interpretari 'to explain, expound, translate' came from interpres, the go-between who carries words across. The past participle interpretatus supplied the stem for later adjectives.","cn":"interpretari“解释、阐明、翻译”来自 interpres，即把话带过河的中间人。过去分词 interpretatus 为后来的形容词提供了词干。"},{"era":"ORIGIN UNCERTAIN","en":"The formation of interpres itself is disputed; a link with pretium 'price' is often proposed but not proven. The adjective therefore inherits a root whose second element cannot be stated with certainty.","cn":"interpres 本身的构词有争议；与 pretium“价格”的联系常被提出但未获证明。因此这个形容词继承的词根，其第二个成分无法确定地说明。"},{"era":"16C. ENGLISH","en":"English formed interpretative on the model of Latin -ativus adjectives. Early uses were scholarly: explaining Scripture, law, and dreams.","cn":"英语仿照拉丁语 -ativus 形容词的模式构成 interpretative。早期用法是学术性的：解释经文、法律与梦。"},{"era":"17C.–18C.","en":"The word extended to performance and to any act of assigning meaning. Interpretive appeared as a shortened rival form, especially in American usage.","cn":"这个词扩展到表演以及任何赋予意义的行为。interpretive 作为缩短的竞争形式出现，尤其在美式用法中。"},{"era":"19C.–20C. HUMANITIES","en":"Hermeneutics and literary criticism made 'interpretative' a marker of method: work that argues for a reading rather than merely recording facts.","cn":"诠释学与文学批评使 interpretative 成为方法标记：为某种解读辩护、而非只记录事实的工作。"},{"era":"PRESENT","en":"Modern usage ranges from museum labels and legal notices to dance and philosophy. The word always marks a step beyond description, toward meaning.","cn":"现代用法从博物馆说明牌、法律公告一直延伸到舞蹈与哲学。这个词总标记着超越描述、走向意义的那一步。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates adjectives ending in -ative or -ive that come from different verbs; the near-meaning group separates explanatory, expressive, and analytical words.","cn":"形近组区分以 -ative 或 -ive 结尾但来自不同动词的形容词；近义组区分表示“解释”“表现”与“分析”的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"interpretive","ipa":"/ɪnˈtɜːrprətɪv/","tag":"same root, shortened variant","definition":"the shorter form of the same adjective, now more common in American English. It carries the same meanings and differs only in style and frequency.","definitionCN":"同一形容词的较短形式，在美式英语中更常用。含义相同，只在语体与使用频率上有差别。"},{"word":"imitative","ipa":"/ˈɪmɪtətɪv/","tag":"different root: imitari 'copy'","definition":"copying or reproducing something. It comes from imitari 'to copy', not from interpres; it describes resemblance, not explanation.","definitionCN":"模仿或复制某物。它来自 imitari“模仿”，而非 interpres；描述相似，而不是解释。"},{"word":"illustrative","ipa":"/ɪˈlʌstrətɪv/","tag":"different root: illustrare 'light up'","definition":"serving as an example or clarification. Latin illustrare 'light up, make clear' is the source; the word shows by example rather than by construing meaning.","definitionCN":"用作例证或说明的。拉丁语 illustrare“照亮、使清楚”是其来源；这个词通过举例来展示，而不是通过建构意义。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"explanatory","ipa":"/ɪkˈsplænətəri/","tag":"clarifying","definition":"intended to make something clear. It is the plain functional word; interpretative adds that a particular reading is being offered.","definitionCN":"意在使某事物清楚的。它是朴素的功能性用词；interpretative 额外表示所提供的是某一种解读。"},{"word":"expressive","ipa":"/ɪkˈspresɪv/","tag":"art","definition":"conveying feeling or meaning through form. It is about the power of the medium, while interpretative is about the reading being presented.","definitionCN":"通过形式传达情感或意义。它讲媒介的力量，而 interpretative 讲所呈现的解读。"},{"word":"analytical","ipa":"/ˌænəˈlɪtɪkl/","tag":"method","definition":"breaking something into parts to understand it. It names a procedure, while interpretative names the goal of arriving at meaning.","definitionCN":"把事物拆成部分以理解。它命名一种程序，而 interpretative 命名抵达意义的目标。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real associations: the -ative adjective suffix on interpret, the rival shorter form interpretive, and the museum phrase interpretative panel.","cn":"真实联想：interpret 上的 -ative 形容词后缀、较短的竞争形式 interpretive，以及博物馆用语 interpretative panel。"},"normal":[{"en":"interpret + -ative: an adjective that says this thing is for explaining.","cn":"interpret + -ative：这个形容词表示“这个东西是用来解释的”。"},{"en":"interpretive is the same word with a shorter tail; choose one and be consistent.","cn":"interpretive 是同一个词、尾巴更短；选一个并保持一致。"},{"en":"An interpretative panel stands between the object and the visitor, carrying meaning across.","cn":"解说牌站在展品与观众之间，把意义送过去。"},{"en":"An interpretative ruling explains the agency's reading but binds less than a regulation.","cn":"解释性裁决说明机构的解读，但约束力不如法规。"},{"en":"Interpretative dance asks the audience to read movement as meaning.","cn":"表现性舞蹈要求观众把动作读成意义。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The word marks the step after description: first record, then say what it means.","cn":"这个词标记描述之后的那一步：先记录，再说它意味着什么。"},{"en":"It admits that a reading is being offered, and that admission is what makes criticism possible.","cn":"它承认所提供的是一个解读，这份承认正是批评得以可能的原因。"},{"en":"To interpret is to stand between; the adjective keeps that position visible instead of pretending to be neutral.","cn":"解释就是站在中间；这个形容词让那个位置保持可见，而不假装中立。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The exhibition relies on interpretative labels rather than long captions.","cn":"这个展览依靠诠释性说明牌，而不是长篇图注。"},{"en":"Her interpretative essay changed how scholars read the letter.","cn":"她的诠释性论文改变了学者对这封信的读法。"},{"en":"The agency's interpretative guidance does not have the force of law.","cn":"该机构的解释性指引不具有法律效力。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因它扑来特提舞”——它扑过来，特别把意思“提”到你面前，还带着动作 → interpretative 诠释性的、演绎的","word":"interpretative"},"root":"inter-（在……之间）+ 拉丁语 interpres“中间人、译者”（更早来源不确定）+ -ative；核心是“把意义带到听者面前、具有解释功能的”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of interpretative all describe something that carries or proposes meaning: a label, a study, a performance, a legal notice, a philosophy, a personal account, an analysis, or a dance. The word always admits that a reading is being offered.","cn":"interpretative 的八个义项都描述携带或提出意义的东西：说明牌、研究、表演、法律公告、哲学主张、个人叙述、分析或舞蹈。这个词始终承认所提供的是一个解读。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a magnifying glass over a painting, with a guide pointing out the hidden symbols.","cn":"核心意象：一幅画上悬着放大镜，有人把藏着的象征指给旁人看。"},"chain":["OBJECT","HIDDEN MEANING","GUIDE","READING","AUDIENCE","UNDERSTANDING"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S7","en":"EXPLANATION: labels, reports, and analyses exist to turn findings into meaning.","cn":"解释：说明牌、报告与分析的存在，就是把发现变成意义。"},{"senses":"S2 · S6","en":"READING: scholarship and personal accounts both offer a viewpoint that can be contested.","cn":"解读：学术与个人叙述都提供可被质疑的视角。"},{"senses":"S3 · S8","en":"PERFORMANCE: staging and dance realize one chosen reading in sound or movement.","cn":"表演：舞台调度与舞蹈用声音或动作实现某一种选定解读。"},{"senses":"S4","en":"LAW: an interpretative document explains a reading without always binding like a regulation.","cn":"法律：解释性文件说明一种解读，但不一定像法规那样具有约束力。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"PHILOSOPHY: if all understanding is interpretation, every description already carries a reading.","cn":"哲学：如果一切理解都是解释，那么每种描述都已带着解读。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Interpretative is interpret + -ative; interpretive is the shortened variant. Both descend from Latin interpretari and interpres. The family also includes the agent noun and the mis- and re- prefixed verbs.","cn":"interpretative 是 interpret + -ative；interpretive 是缩短的变体。两者都源自拉丁语 interpretari 与 interpres。家族还包括施动名词以及带 mis-、re- 前缀的动词。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin interpres 'go-between' and interpretari 'explain, translate' are the base. The origin of interpres is uncertain, with a proposed link to pretium 'price' that is not proven; the -ativus suffix is a Latin adjectival pattern.","cn":"基础是拉丁语 interpres“中间人”与 interpretari“解释、翻译”。interpres 的来源不确定，与 pretium“价格”的联系只是推测、未获证明；-ativus 后缀是拉丁形容词构词模式。"},"items":[{"word":"interpretative","structure":"interpret + -ative","meaning":"serving to explain or offer a reading","meaningCN":"解释性的；诠释性的（-ative 构成形容词）","example":"The signs are interpretative, not decorative.","exampleCN":"这些标牌是解说性的，不是装饰性的。"},{"word":"interpretive","structure":"interpret + -ive (shortened variant)","meaning":"same meaning, shorter form","meaningCN":"同义变体（更短形式）","example":"The park has an interpretive trail.","exampleCN":"这座公园有一条解说步道。"},{"word":"interpret","structure":"Latin interpretari","meaning":"to explain or translate","meaningCN":"解释；翻译（源自拉丁动词）","example":"Readers interpret the ending differently.","exampleCN":"读者对结局有不同解读。"},{"word":"interpretation","structure":"interpret + -ation","meaning":"an explanation or reading","meaningCN":"解释；诠释（-ation 构成名词）","example":"The interpretation was published separately.","exampleCN":"这份解释另行发表。"},{"word":"interpreter","structure":"interpret + -er","meaning":"one who explains or translates speech","meaningCN":"口译员；解释者（-er 表施动者）","example":"The interpreter sat beside the witness.","exampleCN":"口译员坐在证人旁边。"},{"word":"interpretatively","structure":"interpretative + -ly","meaning":"in an explanatory manner","meaningCN":"以诠释的方式（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The gallery was interpretatively organized.","exampleCN":"展厅按诠释线索布置。"},{"word":"interpretivism","structure":"interpretive + -ism","meaning":"the methodological view that meaning must be interpreted","meaningCN":"诠释主义（-ism 表主张）","example":"Interpretivism favours qualitative methods.","exampleCN":"诠释主义偏好质性方法。"},{"word":"misinterpret","structure":"mis- (wrongly) + interpret","meaning":"to read wrongly","meaningCN":"误解；曲解（mis- 表错误）","example":"Critics misinterpreted the title.","exampleCN":"评论者误解了这个标题。"},{"word":"reinterpret","structure":"re- (again) + interpret","meaning":"to read in a new way","meaningCN":"重新解释（re- 表再次）","example":"Later historians reinterpreted the treaty.","exampleCN":"后来的历史学家重新解释了这条约。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"interpres","structure":"interpres, interpretis (third declension); deeper origin uncertain","meaning":"go-between, translator","meaningCN":"中间人；译者（更早来源不确定）"},{"word":"interpretari","structure":"interpres + -ari (verb)","meaning":"to explain, expound","meaningCN":"解释；阐明"},{"word":"interpretatus","structure":"past participle of interpretari","meaning":"explained, expounded","meaningCN":"已解释的；已阐明的"},{"word":"pretium","structure":"second-declension noun; proposed but unproven link","meaning":"price, value","meaningCN":"价格；价值（与 interpres 的关联为推测，来源不确定）"}]}},{"word":"interruption","ipa_uk":"/ˌɪntəˈrʌpʃn/","ipa_us":"/ˌɪntəˈrʌpʃn/","definition_zh":"打断；中断；打扰；中止；（供应或服务的）中断","definition_en":"the act of breaking in on someone who is speaking or working, or the stopping of a process that was continuing","core_image":"一条正在画的直线被一只手按住，笔迹断开，留下一个明显的缺口","scene":"研讨会上，学生举手打断了教授的发言。The student's interruption broke the professor's line of argument.","sceneCN":"这里 interruption 是「打断」（第 1 个义项：在别人说话或做事时插进来）；句意：学生的打断让教授的论证断线。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"打断；中断；打扰（可数指一次打断，不可数指被打断的状态）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（供应、服务、赛事等的）中断（常带修饰语，如 power interruption）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"power interruption","zh":"供电中断"},{"phrase":"constant interruptions","zh":"不断的打扰"},{"phrase":"without interruption","zh":"不间断地"},{"phrase":"service interruption","zh":"服务中断"},{"phrase":"an interruption to traffic","zh":"交通中断"},{"phrase":"sorry for the interruption","zh":"抱歉打断一下"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"interruption"},{"label":"复数","form":"interruptions"},{"label":"作定语（名词修饰名词）","form":"interruption rate"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"interrupt","pos":"v.","zh":"打断；中断"},{"word":"interrupter","pos":"n.","zh":"打断者；断流器"},{"word":"interruptive","pos":"adj.","zh":"打断性的"},{"word":"uninterrupted","pos":"adj.","zh":"不间断的；未受打扰的"},{"word":"disrupt","pos":"v.","zh":"扰乱；使中断"},{"word":"rupture","pos":"n./v.","zh":"破裂；断裂"},{"word":"abrupt","pos":"adj.","zh":"突然的；唐突的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Breaking in on speech","titleCN":"打断别人说话","definition":"the act of speaking while another person is still speaking, so that their turn is cut short","definitionCN":"在他人尚未说完时开口，使对方的说话轮次被截短","example":"He raised a hand to excuse the interruption before making his point.","exampleCN":"他抬手为打断表示歉意，然后说出自己的观点。","why":"Interruption is interrupt + -ion. Interrupt comes from Latin interrumpere, inter- 'between' + rumpere 'to break': the word pictures a line being broken in the middle. Speech is the most familiar line, so this is the first sense.","whyCN":"interruption 是 interrupt + -ion。interrupt 源自拉丁语 interrumpere，inter-“在……之间”+ rumpere“折断”：这个词描绘一条线从中间被折断。话语是最熟悉的线，所以这是第一个义项。"},{"no":"02","title":"Stopping a process","titleCN":"中断一个进程","definition":"the stopping of an activity or process that had been going on continuously","definitionCN":"使原本持续进行的活动或过程中止","example":"The interruption of the experiment cost the team two weeks.","exampleCN":"实验中断让团队损失了两周。","why":"The image widens from speech to any continuing line: a process, a sequence, a production run. The word does not say the line is destroyed, only that it is broken and may resume later.","whyCN":"意象从话语扩展到任何持续的线：过程、序列、生产批次。这个词没有说线被毁掉，只说它被折断，之后还可能接上。"},{"no":"03","title":"Disturbance from noise or visitors","titleCN":"噪音或来客造成的打扰","definition":"an unwanted event that distracts people from what they are doing","definitionCN":"使人从正在做的事情上分心的不想要的事件","example":"The open office suffers from constant interruptions.","exampleCN":"开放式办公室饱受不断打扰之苦。","why":"Here the break happens to attention rather than to a process. The plural is common, because the word counts each knock, call, or question as a separate cut.","whyCN":"这里的断裂发生在注意力上，而不是过程上。复数形式很常见，因为每一声敲门、来电或提问都被算作一次独立的切断。"},{"no":"04","title":"A break in continuity","titleCN":"连续性中的间断","definition":"a gap or pause in something otherwise continuous, such as a view, a journey, or a story","definitionCN":"原本连续的事物中的缺口或停顿，如视野、旅程或故事","example":"The hills rise without interruption to the horizon.","exampleCN":"群山连绵不断，一直延伸到地平线。","why":"This sense is spatial or narrative: something continuous is described by the absence of breaks. The phrase 'without interruption' is the standard way to praise an unbroken line.","whyCN":"这个义项是空间或叙事性的：某段连续之物以“没有断点”来描述。without interruption 是称赞一条不断之线的标准说法。"},{"no":"05","title":"Supply or service interruption","titleCN":"供应或服务中断","definition":"a temporary failure in the delivery of electricity, water, network access, or a public service","definitionCN":"电力、供水、网络或公共服务供应的临时中断","example":"A power interruption shut down the servers for forty minutes.","exampleCN":"一次供电中断让服务器停机四十分钟。","why":"Utilities adopted the word because service is imagined as a flow: the pipe or wire carries something continuously, and a failure cuts the flow. The noun measures downtime, not damage.","whyCN":"公用事业采用这个词，因为服务被想象成流：管道或电线持续输送某物，故障则切断这股流。这个名词衡量的是停机时间，而不是损坏。"},{"no":"06","title":"Breaking a train of thought","titleCN":"打断思路","definition":"a distraction that makes someone lose the thread of what they were thinking or saying","definitionCN":"使人失去思路或话语线索的分心","example":"One interruption and the whole argument vanished from his mind.","exampleCN":"一次打断，整个论证就从他的脑子里消失了。","why":"This sense makes the 'line' mental: thought is a thread that can snap. English commonly says 'lose one's train of thought', and interruption is the usual cause.","whyCN":"这个义项把“线”放在头脑里：思路是一条可以绷断的线。英语常说 lose one's train of thought，而 interruption 正是常见的原因。"},{"no":"07","title":"An inserted break in an event","titleCN":"活动中的间歇","definition":"a scheduled or unscheduled pause during a meeting, performance, or journey","definitionCN":"会议、演出或旅途中事先安排或临时的停顿","example":"The chair announced a short interruption for lunch.","exampleCN":"主席宣布短暂休会用餐。","why":"In meetings and broadcasting the break can be planned, and the word loses its negative tone: an interruption is simply a gap inserted into the running order.","whyCN":"在会议与广播中，中断可以是事先安排的，这个词因此失去贬义：interruption 只是插入既定流程中的一个空档。"},{"no":"08","title":"Suspension of a sports event","titleCN":"赛事的中断","definition":"a temporary stop in a match or competition, usually because of weather or an incident","definitionCN":"比赛或竞赛的临时停止，通常因天气或突发事件","example":"Play resumed twenty minutes after the rain interruption.","exampleCN":"雨中中断二十分钟后比赛恢复。","why":"Sport uses the word for an official stoppage that does not cancel the result. The clock stops, the line breaks, and the game continues from the same point.","whyCN":"体育用这个词指官方暂停，但结果不被取消。计时停止，线断开，比赛从同一点继续。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Interruption is interrupt + -ion. Interrupt comes from Latin interruptus, the past participle of interrumpere, built on inter- 'between, apart' and rumpere 'to break'. The same rumpere supplies rupture, abrupt, disrupt, and corrupt.","cn":"interruption 是 interrupt + -ion。interrupt 源自拉丁语 interruptus，即 interrumpere 的过去分词，由 inter-“在……之间、分开”与 rumpere“折断”构成。同一 rumpere 还提供 rupture（破裂）、abrupt（突然的）、disrupt（扰乱）与 corrupt（腐坏）。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Latin rumpere meant 'to break, burst'. With inter- it formed interrumpere 'to break apart, break off'. The participle interruptus described something cut in the middle.","cn":"拉丁语 rumpere 意为“折断、爆裂”。加 inter- 构成 interrumpere“折断、中断”。分词 interruptus 描述从中间被切断的东西。"},{"era":"LATE LATIN / MEDIEVAL","en":"Interruptio named a breaking off, and the word passed through Old French into English. Medieval legal and medical writing used it for suspended actions.","cn":"interruptio 命名中断，该词经古法语进入英语。中世纪的法律与医学文书中用它表示被中止的行为。"},{"era":"14C. ENGLISH","en":"English interruption is recorded in the fourteenth century with the sense 'a breaking off'. Early examples concern speech, prayer, and work.","cn":"英语 interruption 于 14 世纪被记录，义为“中断”。早期例子涉及话语、祈祷与工作。"},{"era":"17C.–18C.","en":"Polite writing fixed phrases such as 'without interruption' and 'excuse the interruption'. The word acquired its social etiquette, not only its physical meaning.","cn":"17 至 18 世纪的礼貌写作固定了 without interruption、excuse the interruption 等说法。这个词除物理义外，也获得了社交礼节上的含义。"},{"era":"19C.–20C. TECHNOLOGY","en":"Telegraphy, telephony, and electricity gave the noun a technical sense: an unintended break in supply or signal. Downtime became measurable in interruption minutes.","cn":"电报、电话与电力给这个名词一个技术义：供应或信号的非预期中断。停机时间开始以“中断分钟”计量。"},{"era":"PRESENT","en":"Modern usage covers conversation, work, utilities, travel, and sport. The common thread is a line that was continuous and is now broken, whether or not it later resumes.","cn":"现代用法覆盖谈话、工作、公用事业、出行与体育。共同线索是一条原本连续、如今被折断的线，无论之后是否续上。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates inter- nouns whose Latin roots differ, plus one same-root relative; the near-meaning group separates words for breaks, pauses, and disturbances.","cn":"形近组区分以 inter- 开头但拉丁词根不同的名词，并附一个同根亲属词；近义组区分表示“中断”“暂停”与“骚扰”的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"intervention","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈvenʃn/","tag":"different root: venire 'come'","definition":"the act of stepping into a situation to change it. It comes from intervenire 'come between', built on venire 'come', not rumpere 'break'.","definitionCN":"介入某种情形以改变它。它来自 intervenire“来到中间”，词根是 venire“来”，而非 rumpere“折断”。"},{"word":"interception","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈsepʃn/","tag":"different root: capere 'take'","definition":"the act of catching something on its way. Latin intercipere 'seize in between' rests on capere 'take', so nothing is broken, only caught.","definitionCN":"在途中截住某物。拉丁语 intercipere“在半路夺取”建立在 capere“拿”上，因此没有东西被折断，只是被截住。"},{"word":"corruption","ipa":"/kəˈrʌpʃn/","tag":"same rumpere, different prefix","definition":"dishonest conduct or the decay of something. Latin corruptio comes from com- (fully) + rumpere, so it shares the root but means breaking something wholly, not breaking into it.","definitionCN":"不诚实的行为，或某物的腐坏。拉丁语 corruptio 来自 com-（完全）+ rumpere，因此同根，但意思是把某物彻底破坏，而不是闯入其中。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"disruption","ipa":"/dɪsˈrʌpʃn/","tag":"stronger","definition":"a serious disturbance that prevents something from continuing normally. It is stronger than interruption and usually implies damage or disorder, not a brief pause.","definitionCN":"使某事物无法正常继续的严重扰乱。它比 interruption 更强，通常暗示损坏或混乱，而不是短暂停顿。"},{"word":"pause","ipa":"/pɔːz/","tag":"voluntary","definition":"a deliberate stop before continuing. It is chosen and orderly; an interruption is imposed from outside.","definitionCN":"继续之前的故意停止。它是有意而有序的；interruption 则是外部强加的。"},{"word":"disturbance","ipa":"/dɪˈstɜːbəns/","tag":"environment","definition":"an event that upsets normal conditions, often noise or disorder. It describes the unsettling effect rather than the break in a line.","definitionCN":"扰乱正常状况的事件，常指噪声或混乱。它描述令人不安的影响，而不是线索的断裂。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real associations: Latin rumpere 'break' with inter- 'between', the unfolding 'without interruption', and the technical phrase power interruption.","cn":"真实联想：拉丁语 rumperere“折断”加 inter-“在……之间”这一结构、常用语 without interruption，以及技术说法 power interruption。"},"normal":[{"en":"rumpere means 'break': an interruption is a line broken in the middle, like a pencil snapped in two.","cn":"rumpere 意为“折断”：interruption 就是从中间被折断的线，像铅笔被折成两段。"},{"en":"The same rumpere gives rupture, abrupt, disrupt, and corrupt — all about breaking.","cn":"同一个 rumpere 给出 rupture（破裂）、abrupt（突然的）、disrupt（扰乱）、corrupt（腐坏）——都与“破”有关。"},{"en":"'Without interruption' means the line runs unbroken to the end.","cn":"without interruption 意为这条线一直不断，直到尽头。"},{"en":"A power interruption is a cut in a flow, measured in minutes of downtime.","cn":"power interruption 是流动被切断，以停机分钟来计量。"},{"en":"In sport, a rain interruption stops the clock but does not cancel the match.","cn":"体育里，雨中中断停下计时，但不取消比赛。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The word never says the line is gone; it says the line is broken and may be rejoined.","cn":"这个词从不说线消失了；它说线被折断，之后还可能重新接上。"},{"en":"Every interruption costs something — time, thread, flow — which is why the word so often carries an apology.","cn":"每一次中断都有代价——时间、思路、流动——所以这个词常带着歉意。"},{"en":"Planned or imposed, the shape is the same: a continuous thing acquires a gap.","cn":"无论是有计划的还是被强加的，形状都一样：连续之物出现了一个缺口。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Frequent interruptions made it impossible to finish the analysis.","cn":"频繁的打断使分析无法完成。"},{"en":"The storm caused a power interruption across three districts.","cn":"暴风雨造成三个区供电中断。"},{"en":"She read the whole report without interruption.","cn":"她一口气读完了整份报告，没有被打断。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因它拉破神”——它一来就把线“拉破”，中间断了个口子 → interruption 打断、中断","word":"interruption"},"root":"inter-（在……之间、分开）+ 拉丁语 rumpere“折断”+ -ion；字面义“从中间折断”，核心是“原本连续的东西出现缺口”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of interruption all describe a continuous line that acquires a gap: speech, a process, attention, a view, a supply, a train of thought, a schedule, or a match. The word names the break itself, not the damage that may follow.","cn":"interruption 的八个义项都描述一条连续之线出现缺口：话语、过程、注意力、视野、供应、思路、日程或比赛。这个词命名的是断裂本身，而不是随之可能发生的损坏。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a hand pressing down on a pencil line, leaving a visible gap in the stroke.","cn":"核心意象：一只手按在正在画的铅笔线上，笔画留下可见的缺口。"},"chain":["CONTINUOUS LINE","BREAK","GAP","LOSS OF FLOW","PAUSE","RESUMPTION"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S6","en":"SPEECH AND THOUGHT: a turn or a thread is cut, and the speaker must recover it.","cn":"话语与思维：轮次或线索被切断，说话者必须重新拾起。"},{"senses":"S2 · S7","en":"PROCESS AND SCHEDULE: a running activity stops, either by accident or by plan.","cn":"过程与日程：进行中的活动停止，或出于意外，或出于安排。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"ATTENTION: noise and visitors break concentration rather than a physical line.","cn":"注意力：噪声与来客打断的是专注，而不是物理的线。"},{"senses":"S4","en":"CONTINUITY: a view, journey, or story is described by the absence of gaps.","cn":"连续性：视野、旅程或故事以“没有缺口”来描述。"},{"senses":"S5 · S8","en":"SERVICE AND SPORT: supply and play are stopped and later resumed from the same point.","cn":"服务与体育：供应与比赛被停止，之后从同一点恢复。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Interruption is interrupt + -ion, and interrupt is Latin interruptus from interrumpere. The family is unusually rich because rumpere also produced rupture, abrupt, disrupt, and corrupt.","cn":"interruption 是 interrupt + -ion，而 interrupt 是拉丁语 interruptus，源自 interrumpere。这个家族格外丰富，因为 rumpere 还产生了 rupture、abrupt、disrupt 与 corrupt。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin rumpere 'to break' is the engine of the family: interruptus 'broken off', ruptura 'a breaking', abruptus 'broken away', disruptus 'broken apart', corruptus 'broken entirely'. The prefixes change only the direction or completeness of the break.","cn":"拉丁语 rumpere“折断”是这个家族的核心：interruptus“中断的”、ruptura“断裂”、abruptus“断裂开去的”、disruptus“被拆散的”、corruptus“被彻底破坏的”。前缀只改变断裂的方向或彻底程度。"},"items":[{"word":"interruption","structure":"interrupt + -ion","meaning":"a breaking in or a stop","meaningCN":"打断；中断（-ion 构成名词）","example":"There were three interruptions during the talk.","exampleCN":"演讲过程中有三次打断。"},{"word":"interrupt","structure":"Latin interruptus, from interrumpere","meaning":"to break in on; to stop temporarily","meaningCN":"打断；使中断（源自拉丁分词）","example":"Please do not interrupt the speaker.","exampleCN":"请不要打断发言者。"},{"word":"interrupter","structure":"interrupt + -er","meaning":"one who interrupts; a device that breaks a circuit","meaningCN":"打断者；断流器（-er 表施动者或器物）","example":"The interrupter cut the current every second.","exampleCN":"断流器每秒切断电流一次。"},{"word":"interruptive","structure":"interrupt + -ive","meaning":"tending to interrupt","meaningCN":"打断性的（-ive 构成形容词）","example":"His interruptive habit annoyed the panel.","exampleCN":"他爱打断人的习惯让评审组不快。"},{"word":"uninterrupted","structure":"un- (not) + interrupted","meaning":"continuous, without a break","meaningCN":"不间断的（un- 表否定）","example":"They worked for six uninterrupted hours.","exampleCN":"他们不间断地工作了六小时。"},{"word":"disrupt","structure":"dis- (apart) + rumpere 'break'","meaning":"to throw into disorder; to break up","meaningCN":"扰乱；使中断（dis-“分开”+ rumpere）","example":"The strike disrupted rail services.","exampleCN":"罢工扰乱了铁路服务。"},{"word":"disruption","structure":"disrupt + -ion","meaning":"serious disturbance","meaningCN":"扰乱；中断（-ion 构成名词）","example":"The disruption lasted all morning.","exampleCN":"混乱持续了整个上午。"},{"word":"rupture","structure":"Latin ruptura, from rumpere","meaning":"a breaking or bursting","meaningCN":"破裂；断裂（ruptura）","example":"The pipe suffered a rupture.","exampleCN":"管道发生了破裂。"},{"word":"abrupt","structure":"ab- (away) + rumpere 'break'","meaning":"sudden, as if broken off","meaningCN":"突然的；唐突的（ab-“离开”+ rumpere）","example":"The meeting came to an abrupt end.","exampleCN":"会议突然结束。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"rumpere","structure":"third-conjugation verb","meaning":"to break, burst","meaningCN":"折断；爆裂"},{"word":"interrumpere","structure":"inter- 'between, apart' + rumpere","meaning":"to break apart, break off","meaningCN":"折断；中断"},{"word":"interruptus","structure":"past participle of interrumpere","meaning":"broken off, interrupted","meaningCN":"被中断的；被打断的"},{"word":"interruptio","structure":"interrumpere + -tio (action noun)","meaning":"a breaking off","meaningCN":"中断；打断"}]}},{"word":"intervention","ipa_uk":"/ˌɪntəˈvenʃn/","ipa_us":"/ˌɪntərˈvenʃn/","definition_zh":"干预；介入；调停；（医疗）干预措施；（政府）调控","definition_en":"the act of becoming involved in a situation in order to change its course, especially in politics, medicine, social policy, or law","core_image":"两个人正要撞上，第三个人伸开双臂站到中间","scene":"病房里，医生看着监测仪。Early medical intervention cut the risk of complications sharply.","sceneCN":"这里 intervention 是「医疗干预」（第 4 个义项：为改变结果而采取的措施）；句意：早期医疗干预大幅降低了并发症风险。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"干预；介入；调停（可数指一次行动，不可数指介入行为）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（医疗、社会、经济领域的）干预措施（常带修饰语，如 early intervention）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"early intervention","zh":"早期干预"},{"phrase":"government intervention","zh":"政府干预"},{"phrase":"military intervention","zh":"军事干预"},{"phrase":"humanitarian intervention","zh":"人道主义干预"},{"phrase":"intervention in A","zh":"对 A 的干预"},{"phrase":"crisis intervention","zh":"危机干预"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"intervention"},{"label":"复数","form":"interventions"},{"label":"作定语（名词修饰名词）","form":"intervention programme"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"intervene","pos":"v.","zh":"干预；介入；调停"},{"word":"intervening","pos":"adj.","zh":"介入的；中间的"},{"word":"interventionist","pos":"n./adj.","zh":"干预主义者；干预的"},{"word":"interventionism","pos":"n.","zh":"干预主义"},{"word":"nonintervention","pos":"n.","zh":"不干预"},{"word":"convene","pos":"v.","zh":"召集；召开"},{"word":"prevent","pos":"v.","zh":"预防；阻止"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Stepping into a situation","titleCN":"介入某种情形","definition":"the act of entering a situation that one was not originally part of, in order to influence it","definitionCN":"进入一个原本与自己无关的情形，以对其施加影响的行为","example":"A neighbour's intervention stopped the argument from turning violent.","exampleCN":"邻居的介入阻止了争吵演变成暴力。","why":"Intervention is intervene + -tion. Intervene comes from Latin intervenire, inter- 'between' + venire 'to come': literally 'to come between'. The word pictures a third party arriving in the space between two sides.","whyCN":"intervention 是 intervene + -tion。intervene 源自拉丁语 intervenire，inter-“在……之间”+ venire“来”：字面就是“来到中间”。这个词描绘第三方进入两方之间的空隙。"},{"no":"02","title":"Political or military intervention","titleCN":"政治或军事干预","definition":"the action of one state or force entering another country's affairs, often without invitation","definitionCN":"一国或一支力量介入他国事务，往往未经邀请","example":"The intervention was condemned as a violation of sovereignty.","exampleCN":"这次干预被谴责为侵犯主权。","why":"In politics the 'between' is the border: an outside power comes into a space it does not own. The word therefore carries an immediate question of legitimacy, which is why it is so often disputed.","whyCN":"在政治中，“之间”就是边界：外部力量进入一块它并不拥有的空间。这个词因此立刻带有合法性问题，所以常引发争议。"},{"no":"03","title":"Mediation between parties","titleCN":"双方的调停","definition":"the act of helping two sides in a dispute reach an agreement","definitionCN":"帮助争执双方达成协议的行为","example":"The union welcomed the minister's intervention in the talks.","exampleCN":"工会欢迎部长在谈判中的调停。","why":"This is the friendliest sense: the third party comes between the two sides precisely because both need someone in the middle. The Latin image is unchanged, only the intent is cooperative.","whyCN":"这是最友善的义项：第三方来到两方之间，恰恰因为双方都需要一个中间人。拉丁意象未变，只是意图是合作性的。"},{"no":"04","title":"Medical intervention","titleCN":"医疗干预","definition":"a treatment, procedure, or programme intended to prevent or change the course of a disease","definitionCN":"旨在预防疾病或改变病程的治疗、操作或方案","example":"Early intervention reduced the number of severe cases.","exampleCN":"早期干预减少了重症病例数。","why":"Medicine uses the noun for anything done to alter the natural course of a condition: surgery, drugs, screening, counselling. The word implies that without the intervention the course would be different.","whyCN":"医学用这个名词指任何为改变病情自然进程而做的事：手术、药物、筛查、咨询。这个词暗示：没有干预，进程会不同。"},{"no":"05","title":"Social or educational programme","titleCN":"社会或教育干预项目","definition":"an organized programme designed to improve outcomes for a group, such as early-childhood or literacy support","definitionCN":"为改善某群体结果而设计的有组织方案，如幼儿支持或识字项目","example":"The city funded interventions for families at risk.","exampleCN":"市政府资助面向高风险家庭的干预项目。","why":"Policy language uses the plural 'interventions' for packaged measures with measurable goals. Here the word becomes countable: one intervention is one designed programme.","whyCN":"政策语言用复数 interventions 指有可测目标的成套措施。这里这个词变得可数：一项干预就是一个设计好的方案。"},{"no":"06","title":"Crisis intervention","titleCN":"危机干预","definition":"immediate support given to a person in acute distress to prevent harm","definitionCN":"对处于急性痛苦中的人给予即时支持，以防止伤害","example":"Trained volunteers provide crisis intervention within minutes.","exampleCN":"受过训练的志愿者在几分钟内提供危机干预。","why":"In psychology the word stresses timing: the third party must arrive before the situation resolves badly. 'Intervention' here is measured in minutes, not policies.","whyCN":"在心理学中，这个词强调时机：第三方必须在情形恶化之前到达。这里的 intervention 以分钟计，而不是以政策计。"},{"no":"07","title":"Economic intervention","titleCN":"经济干预","definition":"government action such as regulation, subsidy, or rate setting intended to alter market outcomes","definitionCN":"政府通过监管、补贴或定价等手段改变市场结果的行为","example":"Central bank intervention stabilized the currency.","exampleCN":"央行干预稳定了货币。","why":"Economics contrasts intervention with the 'natural' working of the market, and the word inherits that contrast. An intervention is always defined against a baseline it is trying to change.","whyCN":"经济学把干预与市场的“自然”运行相对照，这个词继承了这一对照。干预总是相对于一个它试图改变的基线来定义的。"},{"no":"08","title":"Third-party intervention in law","titleCN":"诉讼中的第三人介入","definition":"the formal entry of a third party into a legal case to protect its own interests","definitionCN":"第三方为保护自身利益而正式加入诉讼","example":"The environmental group was granted leave to intervene in the case.","exampleCN":"该环保团体获准介入此案。","why":"Law uses the verb 'intervene' for a party who was not named but has a stake. The noun keeps the spatial sense: someone comes between the plaintiff and the defendant.","whyCN":"法律用动词 intervene 指未被列为当事人但有利害关系的一方。名词保留空间义：某人来到原告与被告之间。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Intervention is intervene + -tion. Intervene comes from Latin intervenire, inter- 'between' + venire 'to come', literally 'to come between'. The same venire supplies convene, prevent, and avenue, each with a different prefix direction.","cn":"intervention 是 intervene + -tion。intervene 源自拉丁语 intervenire，inter-“在……之间”+ venire“来”，字面意为“来到中间”。同一 venire 还提供 convene、prevent 与 avenue，各自的前缀方向不同。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Latin venire meant 'to come, go'. With inter- it formed intervenire 'to come between, intervene'. The noun interventio named the act of coming into the middle of something.","cn":"拉丁语 venire 意为“来、去”。加 inter- 构成 intervenire“来到中间、介入”。名词 interventio 命名进入事物中间的行为。"},{"era":"15C. ENGLISH","en":"English intervention first appears in the fifteenth century with the sense 'interposition'. Early uses were legal and diplomatic rather than medical.","cn":"英语 intervention 最早于 15 世纪出现，义为“居中插入”。早期用法是法律与外交上的，而非医学上的。"},{"era":"17C.–18C. POLITICS","en":"The word became a term of statecraft: one power intervening in another's affairs. Its legitimacy was debated from the start, and the noun carried that debate.","cn":"这个词成为治国术语：一国介入他国事务。其合法性从一开始就有争论，名词承载着这场争论。"},{"era":"19C. MEDICINE","en":"Clinical writing adopted 'intervention' for surgical and later pharmacological action, contrasting it with watchful waiting. The word then implied a decision to alter the natural course.","cn":"临床写作采用 intervention 指手术以及后来的药物处理，与“观察等待”相对。这个词由此暗示改变自然病程的决定。"},{"era":"20C. SOCIAL POLICY","en":"Welfare, education, and psychology turned the noun into countable programmes: early intervention, crisis intervention. The word now names a designed measure, not only an act.","cn":"福利、教育与心理学把这个名词变成可数的方案：early intervention、crisis intervention。这个词如今命名一种设计好的措施，而不只是一个行动。"},{"era":"PRESENT","en":"Modern use spans diplomacy, medicine, markets, and courtrooms. In all of them the structure is a third party arriving in the space between two sides.","cn":"现代用法覆盖外交、医疗、市场与法庭。它们结构相同：第三方来到两方之间的空隙。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates words built on the same venire 'come' root with different prefixes; the near-meaning group separates interference, mediation, and involvement.","cn":"形近组区分以同一 venire“来”为词根但前缀不同的词；近义组区分“干涉”“调停”与“参与”。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"prevention","ipa":"/prɪˈvenʃn/","tag":"same venire, prefix prae- 'before'","definition":"stopping something before it happens. Prae- 'before' + venire gives 'come before', so prevention arrives earlier than intervention, which arrives during.","definitionCN":"在事情发生之前阻止它。prae-“在前”+ venire 给出“先来”，因此 prevention 比“在过程中进入”的 intervention 更早。"},{"word":"convention","ipa":"/kənˈvenʃn/","tag":"same venire, prefix com- 'together'","definition":"a formal gathering or an accepted custom. Con- 'together' + venire 'come' means 'come together', with none of the 'between' sense.","definitionCN":"正式集会或公认惯例。con-“一起”+ venire“来”意为“聚到一起”，没有“在中间”的意思。"},{"word":"interference","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈfɪərəns/","tag":"different root: ferire 'strike'","definition":"unwanted meddling or the disruption of a signal. It comes from inter- + ferire 'strike', so the image is a blow in between, not a coming between.","definitionCN":"不受欢迎的插手，或信号的干扰。它来自 inter- + ferire“击打”，意象是中途一击，而不是来到中间。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"mediation","ipa":"/ˌmediˈeɪʃn/","tag":"cooperative","definition":"assisted negotiation between disputing parties. It is a specific, agreed form of intervention in which the third party helps rather than decides.","definitionCN":"在争执双方之间协助谈判。它是干预的一种具体、经同意的形式，第三方提供帮助而非裁决。"},{"word":"involvement","ipa":"/ɪnˈvɒlvmənt/","tag":"neutral","definition":"taking part in something. It is neutral about purpose; intervention always implies an intent to change the outcome.","definitionCN":"参与某事。它对目的保持中性；intervention 总暗示改变结果的意图。"},{"word":"interference","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈfɪərəns/","tag":"negative","definition":"unwelcome intrusion into another's affairs. It is the critical word for the same action that a supporter might call intervention.","definitionCN":"对他人事务不受欢迎的侵入。这是批评用词，而支持者可能把同一行为称为 intervention。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real associations: venire 'come' with inter- 'between', the medical phrase early intervention, and the political debate over legitimacy.","cn":"真实联想：venire“来”加 inter-“在……之间”的结构、医疗说法 early intervention，以及围绕合法性的政治争论。"},"normal":[{"en":"venire means 'come': intervention is literally 'coming between' two sides.","cn":"venire 意为“来”：intervention 字面就是“来到两方之间”。"},{"en":"prevent is prae- 'before' + venire, so prevention comes earlier than intervention.","cn":"prevent 是 prae-“在前”+ venire，所以 prevention 比 intervention 更早。"},{"en":"A third person stepping between two people about to collide is the whole word.","cn":"第三个人站到两个即将相撞的人中间，就是这个词的全部。"},{"en":"Early intervention is measured in months saved, crisis intervention in minutes.","cn":"早期干预以省下的月数计量，危机干预以分钟计量。"},{"en":"Calling the same act 'intervention' or 'interference' decides who is the villain.","cn":"把同一行为称为 intervention 还是 interference，决定了谁是坏人。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The word always implies a baseline: something would have gone differently without the third party.","cn":"这个词总暗示一条基线：没有第三方，事情会走向别处。"},{"en":"It carries legitimacy as a question, not an answer — hence the endless arguments about who may intervene.","cn":"它把合法性作为问题而非答案携带在身上——所以关于谁可以干预的争论无休无止。"},{"en":"Coming between is neutral in shape; only the intent and the invitation decide whether it helps or harms.","cn":"“来到中间”在形状上是中性的；只有意图与是否受邀决定它是有益还是有害。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Early intervention in hearing loss improves language outcomes.","cn":"对听力损失的早期干预能改善语言发展结果。"},{"en":"The central bank's intervention calmed the currency market.","cn":"央行干预稳定了货币市场。"},{"en":"The court allowed the charity to intervene in the dispute.","cn":"法院允许该慈善机构介入这场争端。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因它来问神”——它一来就插到中间“问”个究竟，替两边做主 → intervention 干预、介入","word":"intervention"},"root":"inter-（在……之间）+ 拉丁语 venire“来”+ -tion；字面义“来到两者之间”，核心是“第三方进入情形以改变其走向”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of intervention all place a third party in the space between two sides: neighbours, states, disputants, patients and disease, families and risk, a person in crisis, markets, and litigants. The word always implies an intent to change what would otherwise happen.","cn":"intervention 的八个义项都把第三方置于两方之间的空隙：邻居与争吵、国家与他国、争执双方、病人与疾病、家庭与风险、危机中的人、市场、诉讼双方。这个词总暗示改变原本会发生的结果的意图。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: two people about to collide, and a third stepping between them with arms out.","cn":"核心意象：两人即将相撞，第三个人张开双臂站到中间。"},"chain":["TWO SIDES","GAP","THIRD PARTY","ARRIVAL","ALTERED COURSE","NEW OUTCOME"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S3","en":"PERSONAL: a neighbour or mediator comes between two parties to stop or settle a dispute.","cn":"个人层面：邻居或调停人来到两方之间，阻止或了结争执。"},{"senses":"S2 · S7","en":"POWER: states and central banks enter spaces they do not own, raising questions of legitimacy.","cn":"权力：国家与央行进入并不属于自己的空间，引出合法性问题。"},{"senses":"S4 · S6","en":"HEALTH: treatment and crisis support arrive in time to change a course that would otherwise worsen.","cn":"健康：治疗与危机支持及时到达，改变原本会恶化的病程。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"POLICY: designed programmes become countable interventions with measurable goals.","cn":"政策：设计好的方案成为可数、有可测目标的干预。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"LAW: a stakeholder not named in the case formally enters between plaintiff and defendant.","cn":"法律：未被列名的利害关系人正式进入原告与被告之间。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Intervention is intervene + -tion, from Latin intervenire. The affix family is organised around venire 'come': convene, prevent, and avenue differ only in the direction of the prefix.","cn":"intervention 是 intervene + -tion，源自拉丁语 intervenire。词缀家族围绕 venire“来”组织：convene、prevent、avenue 只在前缀方向上不同。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin venire 'to come' yields intervenire 'come between', convenire 'come together', praevenire 'come before', and advenire 'come to'. The prefix, not the root, decides the meaning of each English descendant.","cn":"拉丁语 venire“来”给出 intervenire“来到中间”、convenire“聚到一起”、praevenire“先来”、advenire“来到”。决定每个英语后裔意义的，是前缀而非词根。"},"items":[{"word":"intervention","structure":"intervene + -tion","meaning":"the act of coming between to alter events","meaningCN":"干预；介入（-tion 构成名词）","example":"The intervention prevented an escalation.","exampleCN":"这次干预阻止了事态升级。"},{"word":"intervene","structure":"Latin intervenire, inter- + venire 'come'","meaning":"to step in; to come between","meaningCN":"干预；介入（字面“来到中间”）","example":"The referee intervened to stop the fight.","exampleCN":"裁判介入制止了斗殴。"},{"word":"intervening","structure":"intervene + -ing","meaning":"coming between; occurring in between","meaningCN":"介入的；中间的（-ing 构成形容词）","example":"In the intervening years the town changed.","exampleCN":"在中间那些年里，小镇变了。"},{"word":"interventionist","structure":"intervention + -ist","meaning":"one who favours intervention","meaningCN":"干预主义者（-ist 表人）","example":"Interventionists urged immediate action.","exampleCN":"干预主义者主张立即行动。"},{"word":"interventionism","structure":"intervention + -ism","meaning":"the policy of intervening","meaningCN":"干预主义（-ism 表主张）","example":"Economic interventionism divided the party.","exampleCN":"经济干预主义使党内分裂。"},{"word":"nonintervention","structure":"non- (not) + intervention","meaning":"the policy of not intervening","meaningCN":"不干预（non- 表否定）","example":"The doctrine of nonintervention was abandoned.","exampleCN":"不干预原则被放弃。"},{"word":"prevent","structure":"prae- (before) + venire 'come'","meaning":"to stop before it happens","meaningCN":"预防；阻止（prae-“在前”+ venire）","example":"Vaccination prevents disease.","exampleCN":"接种疫苗可以预防疾病。"},{"word":"convene","structure":"com- (together) + venire 'come'","meaning":"to call or come together","meaningCN":"召集；召开（com-“一起”+ venire）","example":"The board convened at noon.","exampleCN":"董事会中午召开。"},{"word":"avenue","structure":"ad- (to) + venire 'come'","meaning":"a way by which something comes or is approached","meaningCN":"途径；大道（ad-“向”+ venire）","example":"They explored every avenue for funding.","exampleCN":"他们探索了所有筹资途径。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"venire","structure":"fourth-conjugation verb","meaning":"to come, go","meaningCN":"来；去"},{"word":"intervenire","structure":"inter- 'between' + venire 'come'","meaning":"to come between, intervene","meaningCN":"来到中间；介入"},{"word":"interventio","structure":"intervenire + -tio (action noun)","meaning":"a coming between; intervention","meaningCN":"介入；调停"},{"word":"praevenire","structure":"prae- 'before' + venire 'come'","meaning":"to come before, prevent","meaningCN":"先来；预防"}]}},{"word":"investigation","ipa_uk":"/ɪnˌvestɪˈɡeɪʃn/","ipa_us":"/ɪnˌvestɪˈɡeɪʃn/","definition_zh":"调查；侦查；调查研究；（医学）检查；（学术）探究","definition_en":"the act or process of examining a matter carefully in order to discover the facts, especially a crime, an accident, a scientific question, or an official complaint","core_image":"有人在泥地上发现一串脚印，蹲下身顺着痕迹一路追下去","scene":"实验室里，调查员对着受污染的样本做记录。The investigation will keep going until it reaches the source of the pollution.","sceneCN":"这里 investigation 是「调查」（第 1 个义项：为查明事实而系统追查）；句意：这项调查会一直追到污染源头为止。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"调查；侦查（可数指一项调查，不可数指调查过程）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（学术）探究；（医学）检查（常带修饰语，如 laboratory investigation）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"criminal investigation","zh":"刑事侦查"},{"phrase":"under investigation","zh":"正在调查中"},{"phrase":"launch an investigation","zh":"展开调查"},{"phrase":"investigation into A","zh":"对 A 的调查"},{"phrase":"scientific investigation","zh":"科学探究"},{"phrase":"internal investigation","zh":"内部调查"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"investigation"},{"label":"复数","form":"investigations"},{"label":"作定语（名词修饰名词）","form":"investigation team"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"investigate","pos":"v.","zh":"调查；侦查；研究"},{"word":"investigator","pos":"n.","zh":"调查员；侦查员"},{"word":"investigative","pos":"adj.","zh":"调查的；调查性的"},{"word":"investigatory","pos":"adj.","zh":"调查性质的"},{"word":"reinvestigate","pos":"v.","zh":"重新调查"},{"word":"vestige","pos":"n.","zh":"痕迹；遗迹"},{"word":"vestigial","pos":"adj.","zh":"残留的；退化的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Systematic fact-finding","titleCN":"系统地查明事实","definition":"the careful process of gathering evidence and establishing what happened","definitionCN":"收集证据并确定发生了什么的谨慎过程","example":"A thorough investigation established the cause of the fire.","exampleCN":"一次彻底调查确定了火灾原因。","why":"Investigation is investigate + -ion. Investigate comes from Latin investigare, in- 'into' + vestigare 'to track, trace', from vestigium 'footprint'. The whole word is a trail followed to its source.","whyCN":"investigation 是 investigate + -ion。investigate 源自拉丁语 investigare，in-“进入”+ vestigare“追踪”，而 vestigare 来自 vestigium“脚印”。整个词就是一条被追到源头的痕迹。"},{"no":"02","title":"Criminal investigation","titleCN":"刑事侦查","definition":"the official police process of gathering evidence about a suspected offence","definitionCN":"警方为涉嫌犯罪收集证据的官方过程","example":"The investigation led to two arrests within a week.","exampleCN":"这次侦查在一周内导致两人被捕。","why":"Police work makes the trail literal: suspects leave traces, and investigators follow them. The noun is often paired with 'into' because the trail leads into a matter.","whyCN":"警务工作让“痕迹”变得字面化：嫌疑人留下痕迹，侦查员循迹而行。这个名词常接 into，因为痕迹通向一桩事情内部。"},{"no":"03","title":"Scientific inquiry","titleCN":"科学探究","definition":"a planned study designed to answer a question about nature through observation and experiment","definitionCN":"通过观察与实验回答自然问题的有计划研究","example":"The investigation tested how the soil responds to drought.","exampleCN":"这项探究检验土壤如何回应干旱。","why":"Science uses the word for inquiry that follows a method rather than a suspect. The vestigium here is data: the trail is whatever the evidence allows you to reconstruct.","whyCN":"科学用这个词指遵循方法而非追查嫌疑人的探究。这里的 vestigium 是数据：痕迹就是证据允许你重建的那条路径。"},{"no":"04","title":"Journalistic investigation","titleCN":"新闻调查","definition":"reporting that digs into documents and sources to expose something not publicly known","definitionCN":"深挖文件与消息源、揭露不为人知之事报道","example":"The newspaper's investigation revealed how the contracts were awarded.","exampleCN":"该报的调查揭露了合同是如何被授予的。","why":"Journalism borrowed the police model and made the trail public: records, interviews, and leaks replace footprints. The word legitimises the digging as a public service.","whyCN":"新闻业借用了警务模型，把痕迹公开化：文件、访谈与爆料取代了脚印。这个词使这种挖掘获得公共服务的正当性。"},{"no":"05","title":"Internal or administrative inquiry","titleCN":"机构内部调查","definition":"an inquiry ordered by an organization into its own conduct or procedures","definitionCN":"组织对自身行为或程序发起的调查","example":"An internal investigation found that safety checks had been skipped.","exampleCN":"内部调查发现安全检查被跳过。","why":"Institutions investigate themselves when a complaint or accident crosses a threshold. The noun signals a formal procedure with findings, not an informal chat.","whyCN":"当投诉或事故越过某个门槛时，机构会调查自己。这个名词标记一项有结论的正式程序，而不是非正式谈话。"},{"no":"06","title":"Medical investigation","titleCN":"医学检查","definition":"a test or series of tests used to establish a diagnosis, often called 'investigations' in British usage","definitionCN":"用于确定诊断的一项或一组检查，英式用法常作复数 investigations","example":"The doctor ordered blood investigations before prescribing treatment.","exampleCN":"医生在开药前安排了血液检查。","why":"Medicine uses the plural for tests that trace a symptom to its cause. The trail image fits: each test narrows the possible source, as tracks narrow a search.","whyCN":"医学用复数指把症状追溯到病因的检查。痕迹意象很贴合：每项检查收窄可能的来源，正如足迹收窄搜索范围。"},{"no":"07","title":"Academic research project","titleCN":"学术研究项目","definition":"a sustained scholarly study of a question, often with a formal report of methods and findings","definitionCN":"对某一问题的持续学术研究，通常附方法与发现的正式报告","example":"Her investigation of the archive took three summers.","exampleCN":"她对档案的研究花了三个夏天。","why":"Academic English prefers 'investigation' when the emphasis is on methodical pursuit rather than on a hypothesis. It is the word for following a question wherever it leads.","whyCN":"当重点在有条理的追索而非假设时，学术英语偏好 investigation。这个词用于“问题引到哪里就追到哪里”。"},{"no":"08","title":"Philosophical inquiry","titleCN":"哲学上的探究","definition":"a sustained examination of a concept or problem in order to clarify it rather than to convict anyone","definitionCN":"为澄清概念或问题而进行的持续考察，而非为了给人定罪","example":"The book is an investigation into what we mean by justice.","exampleCN":"这本书是对我们所谓“正义”的探究。","why":"Philosophy keeps the earliest broad sense: an examination that follows a question to its foundations. Here nothing is suspected; the object is a concept, and the trail ends in definitions.","whyCN":"哲学保留最早宽泛的义项：顺着问题追到根基的考察。这里没有嫌疑人，对象是概念，痕迹止于定义。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Investigation is investigate + -ion. Investigate comes from Latin investigare, built on in- 'into' and vestigare 'to track, trace', itself from vestigium 'footprint'. The word is a footprint followed until the source is found.","cn":"investigation 是 investigate + -ion。investigate 源自拉丁语 investigare，由 in-“进入”与 vestigare“追踪”构成，而 vestigare 又来自 vestigium“脚印”。这个词就是一枚被追到源头的脚印。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Latin vestigium meant 'footprint, trace, mark'. The verb vestigare meant 'to track, follow a trail', and investigare added in- 'into' to intensify the search: to follow the tracks into the matter.","cn":"拉丁语 vestigium 意为“脚印、痕迹、标记”。动词 vestigare 意为“追踪、循迹”，investigare 加 in-“进入”来加强搜索：循着痕迹进入事情内部。"},{"era":"LATE LATIN / MEDIEVAL","en":"Investigatio appeared in legal and scholarly Latin for a formal examination. The word travelled through Old French into English with its judicial flavour intact.","cn":"investigatio 见于法律与学术拉丁语，指正式审查。该词经古法语进入英语，其司法色彩完好保留。"},{"era":"15C. ENGLISH","en":"English investigation is recorded in the mid-fifteenth century, first in legal and ecclesiastical contexts. The sense 'a formal inquiry into conduct' is therefore older than the scientific one.","cn":"英语 investigation 于 15 世纪中叶被记录，最早见于法律与教会语境。因此“对行为的正式调查”这一义项比科学义更早。"},{"era":"17C.–18C. SCIENCE","en":"Natural philosophy adopted the noun for systematic study of nature. The trail became an experiment, but the word kept its sense of following evidence rather than guessing.","cn":"自然哲学采用这个名词指对自然的系统研究。痕迹变成实验，但这个词仍保留“循证据而行、而非猜测”的含义。"},{"era":"19C.–20C. POLICE AND PRESS","en":"Professional police forces and investigative journalism institutionalised the word. 'Under investigation' became a standard public formula for a matter not yet resolved.","cn":"职业警队与调查报道使这个词制度化。under investigation 成为“事情尚未了结”的标准公开说法。"},{"era":"PRESENT","en":"Modern usage spans crime, science, medicine, academia, and philosophy. Every sense keeps the original picture: a trace is found, and someone follows it to its source.","cn":"现代用法覆盖犯罪、科学、医学、学术与哲学。每个义项都保留原本画面：发现痕迹，并有人顺迹追到源头。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates in- and inter- words built on different roots, including the near-trap investment; the near-meaning group separates inquiry, examination, and probe.","cn":"形近组区分以 in-、inter- 开头但词根不同的词，包括 investment 这一近似陷阱；近义组区分“询问”“审查”与“探查”。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"investment","ipa":"/ɪnˈvestmənt/","tag":"different root: vestis 'garment'","definition":"the putting of money into something for profit. It comes from investire 'to clothe', from vestis 'garment', not from vestigium 'footprint'.","definitionCN":"为获利而把钱投入某处。它来自 investire“给……穿衣”，词根是 vestis“衣服”，而非 vestigium“脚印”。"},{"word":"intervention","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈvenʃn/","tag":"different root: venire 'come'","definition":"the act of stepping between parties. It comes from venire 'come', with no tracing or evidence-gathering.","definitionCN":"站到两方之间的行为。它来自 venire“来”，与追踪或取证无关。"},{"word":"invention","ipa":"/ɪnˈvenʃn/","tag":"different root: venire 'come upon'","definition":"the creation of something new. Latin invenire meant 'come upon, find', a different verb from vestigare 'track'.","definitionCN":"新事物的创造。拉丁语 invenire 意为“遇到、找到”，与 vestigare“追踪”是不同的动词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"inquiry","ipa":"/ɪnˈkwaɪəri/","tag":"asking","definition":"a request for information or an official examination. It stresses asking questions; investigation stresses gathering evidence and following a trail.","definitionCN":"信息请求或官方审查。它强调提问；investigation 强调收集证据与循迹追查。"},{"word":"examination","ipa":"/ɪɡˌzæmɪˈneɪʃn/","tag":"inspection","definition":"a close look at something. It can be a single inspection; investigation usually implies a process lasting some time.","definitionCN":"对某物的仔细查看。它可以是一次性检查；investigation 通常暗示持续一段时间的进程。"},{"word":"probe","ipa":"/prəʊb/","tag":"informal and forceful","definition":"a thorough and often intrusive inquiry. It is more journalistic and confrontational than the neutral investigation.","definitionCN":"彻底且常带侵入性的调查。它比中性的 investigation 更具新闻性与对抗性。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real associations: vestigium 'footprint', in- 'into', the standard phrase under investigation, and the British medical plural investigations.","cn":"真实联想：vestigium“脚印”、in-“进入”、标准说法 under investigation，以及英式医学复数 investigations。"},"normal":[{"en":"vestigium means 'footprint': an investigation is a trail followed into the matter.","cn":"vestigium 意为“脚印”：investigation 就是循着痕迹进入事情内部。"},{"en":"The same root gives vestige, a remaining trace — exactly what an investigator looks for.","cn":"同一词根给出 vestige“残留痕迹”——正是调查者要找的东西。"},{"en":"Police follow footprints; scientists follow data; reporters follow documents — one word covers all.","cn":"警察循脚印，科学家循数据，记者循文件——一个词全都涵盖。"},{"en":"'Under investigation' means the trail is still open and no conclusion is official yet.","cn":"under investigation 意为痕迹仍在延伸，尚无官方结论。"},{"en":"In a hospital, 'investigations' are the tests that trace a symptom to its cause.","cn":"在医院里，investigations 就是把症状追溯到病因的检查。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The word assumes the truth left marks; the task is not to invent an answer but to follow what remains.","cn":"这个词假定真相留下了痕迹；任务不是发明答案，而是跟随残存之物。"},{"en":"It is defined by direction: always inward, from surface trace to underlying source.","cn":"它由方向定义：总是向内，从表面痕迹追到背后的来源。"},{"en":"Every investigation has a point where the trail ends, and the word does not promise that it will be reached.","cn":"每一次调查都有痕迹终止之处，而这个词并不保证一定能抵达。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The police opened an investigation into the cause of the collapse.","cn":"警方对坍塌原因展开调查。"},{"en":"Her investigation of the letters changed the accepted history.","cn":"她对这些信件的研究改变了公认的历史。"},{"en":"The company is under investigation for falsifying safety records.","cn":"这家公司因伪造安全记录正在接受调查。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因外斯提给神”——沿着外面的脚印一路“提”到神那里去问个明白 → investigation 调查、侦查","word":"investigation"},"root":"in-（进入）+ 拉丁语 vestigium“脚印”、vestigare“追踪”+ -ion；字面义“循着脚印进去”，核心是“顺着痕迹追到源头”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of investigation all describe a trace that is followed to its source: a fire, a crime, a natural process, a hidden deal, an internal failure, a symptom, an archive, or a concept. The word names the following, not the verdict.","cn":"investigation 的八个义项都描述一条被追到源头的痕迹：火灾、罪行、自然过程、隐藏交易、内部失误、症状、档案或概念。这个词命名的是追踪，而不是判决。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: footprints in mud, and a person crouching to follow them.","cn":"核心意象：泥地上的脚印，一个人蹲下来顺着它们走。"},"chain":["TRACE","NOTICE","PURSUIT","EVIDENCE","RECONSTRUCTION","SOURCE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"CRIME AND ACCIDENT: official fact-finding follows physical and testimonial traces.","cn":"犯罪与事故：官方的事实查明沿着物证与证言的痕迹走。"},{"senses":"S3 · S7","en":"SCIENCE AND SCHOLARSHIP: data and documents are the trail, and method decides how far it can be followed.","cn":"科学与学术：数据与文献是痕迹，方法决定能追多远。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"PRESS AND INSTITUTIONS: reporting and internal reviews make the trail public or formal.","cn":"新闻与机构：报道与内部审查让痕迹公开化或正式化。"},{"senses":"S6","en":"MEDICINE: tests narrow the source of a symptom the way tracks narrow a search.","cn":"医学：检查收窄症状的来源，正如足迹收窄搜索范围。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"PHILOSOPHY: the object is a concept, and the trail ends in definitions rather than in a culprit.","cn":"哲学：对象是概念，痕迹止于定义而非罪人。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Investigation is investigate + -ion, from Latin investigare and vestigium. The family includes the agent and adjective forms, plus vestige and vestigial, which keep the literal footprint.","cn":"investigation 是 investigate + -ion，源自拉丁语 investigare 与 vestigium。家族包括施动名词与形容词，以及保留字面“脚印”义的 vestige 与 vestigial。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin vestigium 'footprint' produced vestigare 'track' and investigare 'track into, search out'. The English trap is invest, which comes from investire 'clothe' (in- + vestis 'garment'), a completely different root.","cn":"拉丁语 vestigium“脚印”产生 vestigare“追踪”与 investigare“追进去、查出”。英语中的陷阱是 invest，它来自 investire“穿衣”（in- + vestis“衣服”），词根完全不同。"},"items":[{"word":"investigation","structure":"investigate + -ion","meaning":"a systematic inquiry","meaningCN":"调查；侦查（-ion 构成名词）","example":"The investigation took six months.","exampleCN":"这项调查花了六个月。"},{"word":"investigate","structure":"Latin investigare, in- + vestigare 'track'","meaning":"to examine by following evidence","meaningCN":"调查；侦查（字面“循迹进入”）","example":"Officials came to investigate the complaint.","exampleCN":"官员前来调查这项投诉。"},{"word":"investigator","structure":"investigate + -or","meaning":"one who conducts an inquiry","meaningCN":"调查员；侦查员（-or 表施动者）","example":"The investigator recorded every item.","exampleCN":"调查员记录了每一件物品。"},{"word":"investigative","structure":"investigate + -ive","meaning":"relating to investigation","meaningCN":"调查的；调查性的（-ive 构成形容词）","example":"She is known for investigative reporting.","exampleCN":"她以调查报道闻名。"},{"word":"investigatory","structure":"investigate + -ory","meaning":"of the nature of an inquiry","meaningCN":"调查性质的（-ory 构成形容词）","example":"The committee has investigatory powers.","exampleCN":"该委员会拥有调查权。"},{"word":"reinvestigate","structure":"re- (again) + investigate","meaning":"to investigate once more","meaningCN":"重新调查（re- 表再次）","example":"The case was reinvestigated in 2010.","exampleCN":"此案在 2010 年被重新调查。"},{"word":"vestige","structure":"Latin vestigium 'footprint'","meaning":"a small remaining trace","meaningCN":"痕迹；遗迹（直接借自拉丁名词）","example":"Only a vestige of the wall remains.","exampleCN":"墙上只剩一点残迹。"},{"word":"vestigial","structure":"vestigium + -alis → vestigial + -al","meaning":"remaining as a small trace, often functionless","meaningCN":"残留的；退化的（vestigium + -al）","example":"The bone is vestigial in modern humans.","exampleCN":"这块骨在现代人身上已退化。"},{"word":"invest","structure":"Latin investire 'clothe', from vestis 'garment'","meaning":"to put money or effort into something","meaningCN":"投资；投入（同形不同源：vestis“衣服”）","example":"They invested heavily in research.","exampleCN":"他们在研究上投入很大。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"vestigium","structure":"second-declension noun","meaning":"footprint, trace, mark","meaningCN":"脚印；痕迹；标记"},{"word":"vestigare","structure":"verb from vestigium","meaning":"to track, follow a trail","meaningCN":"追踪；循迹"},{"word":"investigare","structure":"in- 'into' + vestigare 'track'","meaning":"to track down, search out","meaningCN":"追查；查出"},{"word":"investigatio","structure":"investigare + -tio (action noun)","meaning":"a searching out, inquiry","meaningCN":"调查；探究"}]}},{"word":"investigative","ipa_uk":"/ɪnˈvestɪɡətɪv/","ipa_us":"/ɪnˈvestɪɡeɪtɪv/","definition_zh":"调查的；调查性的；侦查的；用于查明事实的","definition_en":"relating to or used for investigation, especially the systematic search for facts about a crime, accident, complaint, or research question","core_image":"一束探照灯沿着脚印一路照过去，不放过任何一处痕迹","scene":"新闻编辑部里，主编说这个团队追一条资金链追了半年。Their investigative reporting followed the money for six months.","sceneCN":"这里 investigative 是「调查性的」（第 1 个义项：用于查明事实的）；句意：他们的调查性报道追了这条资金链半年。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"调查的；调查性的（用于报道、工作、方法等）"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"侦查的；有调查职能或权限的（用于机构、委员会、权力）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"investigative journalism","zh":"调查性报道"},{"phrase":"investigative reporter","zh":"调查记者"},{"phrase":"investigative work","zh":"调查工作"},{"phrase":"investigative committee","zh":"调查委员会"},{"phrase":"investigative powers","zh":"调查权"},{"phrase":"investigative technique","zh":"侦查手段"}],"forms":[{"label":"形容词原级","form":"investigative"},{"label":"比较级","form":"more investigative"},{"label":"同义变体（较少用）","form":"investigatory"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"investigate","pos":"v.","zh":"调查；侦查"},{"word":"investigation","pos":"n.","zh":"调查；侦查"},{"word":"investigator","pos":"n.","zh":"调查员；侦查员"},{"word":"investigatory","pos":"adj.","zh":"调查性质的"},{"word":"reinvestigate","pos":"v.","zh":"重新调查"},{"word":"vestige","pos":"n.","zh":"痕迹；遗迹"},{"word":"vestigial","pos":"adj.","zh":"残留的；退化的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Relating to investigative journalism","titleCN":"调查性报道的","definition":"describing reporting that follows documents and sources over a long period to expose hidden facts","definitionCN":"描述长期追踪文件与消息源、以揭露隐藏事实的报道","example":"The paper's investigative team spent a year on the story.","exampleCN":"该报的调查团队为这篇报道花了一年。","why":"Investigative is investigate + -ive. The Latin source investigare means 'track in', from vestigium 'footprint'. The adjective marks work whose purpose is to follow a trail rather than to report what is already public.","whyCN":"investigative 是 investigate + -ive。拉丁语源 investigare 意为“循迹进入”，来自 vestigium“脚印”。这个形容词标记目的是循迹追查、而非报道已知公开信息的工作。"},{"no":"02","title":"Relating to police investigation","titleCN":"警方侦查的","definition":"describing the work, unit, or method used by authorities to solve a crime","definitionCN":"描述当局为破案而做的工作、部门或方法","example":"The investigative unit reviewed the cold case.","exampleCN":"侦查部门重新审查了这桩旧案。","why":"Police usage makes the trail concrete: scenes, witnesses, and records. The adjective attaches to 'unit', 'work', and 'powers', marking the official function rather than a person's curiosity.","whyCN":"警务用法让痕迹具体化：现场、证人、记录。这个形容词常修饰 unit、work、powers，标记官方职能，而不是个人的好奇。"},{"no":"03","title":"Describing methods or techniques","titleCN":"用于调查的手段","definition":"describing tools or procedures designed to obtain evidence, such as interviews, searches, or forensic tests","definitionCN":"描述为取得证据而设计的工具或程序，如访谈、搜查或法医检验","example":"They used standard investigative techniques to trace the payment.","exampleCN":"他们用标准的侦查手段追踪这笔付款。","why":"Here the adjective modifies the means rather than the ends. A technique is investigative when its purpose is to produce evidence that can be checked by others.","whyCN":"这里的形容词修饰手段而不是目的。当一项技术的目的在于产出可被他人核对的证据时，它就是 investigative 的。"},{"no":"04","title":"Describing a body or committee","titleCN":"具有调查职能的机构","definition":"describing an official group set up to examine a matter and report findings","definitionCN":"描述为审查某一事项并报告结论而设立的官方小组","example":"An investigative committee was formed after the accident.","exampleCN":"事故后成立了一个调查委员会。","why":"Institutions create such bodies when ordinary management cannot be trusted to examine itself. The adjective names a temporary authority with a defined scope.","whyCN":"当普通管理层不足以被信任来审查自身时，机构会设立这类小组。这个形容词命名一个有明确范围的临时权力。"},{"no":"05","title":"Describing legal powers","titleCN":"调查权限的","definition":"describing the authority to compel documents, testimony, or access during an inquiry","definitionCN":"描述调查过程中强制取得文件、证言或进入场所的权力","example":"The regulator has broad investigative powers but limited sanctions.","exampleCN":"监管机构拥有广泛的调查权，但制裁手段有限。","why":"Law separates the power to find facts from the power to punish. The adjective marks the first, which is why 'investigative powers' often appear next to 'limited enforcement'.","whyCN":"法律把查明事实的权力与惩罚的权力分开。这个形容词标记前者，所以 investigative powers 常与 limited enforcement 并提。"},{"no":"06","title":"Describing a research approach","titleCN":"研究上的探究性","definition":"describing a scholarly approach that actively seeks answers rather than only describing","definitionCN":"描述主动寻求答案、而非仅仅描述的学术路径","example":"The course takes an investigative approach to local history.","exampleCN":"这门课以探究方式处理地方史。","why":"Educators use the adjective for learning by inquiry: students pose questions and gather evidence. The word turns the classroom into a place where trails are followed.","whyCN":"教育者用这个形容词指探究式学习：学生提出问题并收集证据。这个词把课堂变成循迹追查的场所。"},{"no":"07","title":"Describing medical procedures","titleCN":"医学检查性的","definition":"describing tests or procedures whose purpose is diagnosis rather than treatment","definitionCN":"描述目的为诊断而非治疗的操作或检查","example":"The procedure is investigative, not therapeutic.","exampleCN":"这项操作是检查性的，不是治疗性的。","why":"Medicine distinguishes what is done to find out from what is done to cure. The adjective keeps the trail image inside the body: each test follows a sign toward its source.","whyCN":"医学区分“为查明而做”与“为治愈而做”。这个形容词把痕迹意象带进体内：每项检查顺着征象追到源头。"},{"no":"08","title":"Describing an investigative mindset","titleCN":"具有追查态度的","definition":"describing a habit of questioning claims and looking for evidence behind them","definitionCN":"描述质疑说法、寻找其背后证据的习惯","example":"Her investigative habit made her distrust press releases.","exampleCN":"她的追查习惯让她不轻信新闻稿。","why":"This sense is about disposition rather than occupation: anyone can read a claim as a trail. The adjective praises scepticism, but also warns that constant suspicion has a cost.","whyCN":"这个义项关乎性情而非职业：任何人都可以把一个说法读成一条痕迹。这个形容词称赞怀疑精神，但也提醒持续怀疑是有代价的。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Investigative is investigate + -ive, formed in English on the Latin verb investigare. The root is vestigium 'footprint', so the adjective describes anything used to follow a trail toward its source.","cn":"investigative 是 investigate + -ive，在英语中由拉丁动词 investigare 构成。词根是 vestigium“脚印”，因此这个形容词描述任何用于循迹追源的东西。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Latin vestigium 'footprint' produced vestigare 'to track' and investigare 'to track into, search out'. The participle investigatus gave English the verb stem.","cn":"拉丁语 vestigium“脚印”产生 vestigare“追踪”与 investigare“追查进去”。分词 investigatus 给英语提供了动词词干。"},{"era":"15C.–16C.","en":"English investigate entered in the fifteenth century; the adjective investigative followed much later, when the -ive pattern was extended to legal and practical contexts.","cn":"英语 investigate 于 15 世纪进入；形容词 investigative 晚得多才出现，当时 -ive 模式被扩展到法律与实践语境。"},{"era":"19C. PRESS","en":"Investigative is generally associated with the rise of professional reporting in the nineteenth century, when newspapers began following documents as police followed footprints.","cn":"investigative 一般与 19 世纪职业报道的兴起相关联，当时报纸开始像警察循脚印那样追查文件。"},{"era":"20C. POLICE AND REFORM","en":"Police reform and muckraking journalism fixed phrases such as 'investigative unit' and 'investigative reporting'. The adjective became a mark of seriousness and public duty.","cn":"警务改革与黑幕揭发报道固定了 investigative unit、investigative reporting 等说法。这个形容词成为严肃性与公共责任的标志。"},{"era":"20C. SCIENCE AND MEDICINE","en":"Research methods and clinical writing adopted 'investigative' to separate finding out from treating. The word now marks purpose, not profession.","cn":"研究方法与临床写作采用 investigative 来区分“查明”与“治疗”。这个词如今标记目的，而不是职业。"},{"era":"PRESENT","en":"Modern usage spans newsrooms, police units, committees, classrooms, and clinics. In every case the adjective says the aim is to discover facts that are not yet established.","cn":"现代用法覆盖编辑部、警队、委员会、课堂与诊所。无论哪种情况，这个形容词都表示目的在于发现尚未确定的事实。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates same-root variants from words built on other roots; the near-meaning group separates investigative, exploratory, and inquisitive.","cn":"形近组区分同根变体与建立在其他词根上的词；近义组区分 investigative、exploratory 与 inquisitive。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"investigatory","ipa":"/ɪnˈvestɪɡətəri/","tag":"same root, -ory variant","definition":"having the nature of an inquiry. It is close to investigative but more formal and more often used of powers and procedures than of reporting.","definitionCN":"具有调查性质的。它接近 investigative，但更正式，且更常用于权力与程序，而非报道。"},{"word":"investment","ipa":"/ɪnˈvestmənt/","tag":"different root: vestis 'garment'","definition":"money or effort put into something for a return. It comes from investire 'to clothe', from vestis 'garment', not from vestigium 'footprint'.","definitionCN":"为获得回报而投入的金钱或精力。它来自 investire“穿衣”，词根是 vestis“衣服”，而非 vestigium“脚印”。"},{"word":"inquisitive","ipa":"/ɪnˈkwɪzətɪv/","tag":"different root: quaerere 'seek'","definition":"eager to learn or ask questions. It comes from quaerere 'seek, ask', and describes curiosity rather than a formal search for evidence.","definitionCN":"渴望了解或提问的。它来自 quaerere“寻求、询问”，描述好奇心，而不是正式的取证。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"exploratory","ipa":"/ɪkˈsplɒrətri/","tag":"open-ended","definition":"done to discover what is there, without a fixed hypothesis. It is more open-ended than investigative, which usually seeks facts about a specific matter.","definitionCN":"为发现那里有什么而做，没有固定假设。它比 investigative 更开放，后者通常查找某件具体事情的事实。"},{"word":"detective","ipa":"/dɪˈtektɪv/","tag":"role","definition":"relating to a person whose job is solving crimes. It names the role, while investigative describes the purpose or method.","definitionCN":"与以破案为业的人有关的。它命名角色，而 investigative 描述目的或方法。"},{"word":"inquisitorial","ipa":"/ɪnˌkwɪzəˈtɔːriəl/","tag":"legal system","definition":"relating to a system where the court itself investigates. It is a technical legal term, much narrower than investigative.","definitionCN":"与由法院自行调查的制度有关的。它是技术法律术语，比 investigative 窄得多。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real associations: vestigium 'footprint', the -ive adjective ending, and the fixed phrases investigative journalism and investigative powers.","cn":"真实联想：vestigium“脚印”、-ive 形容词结尾，以及 investigative journalism、investigative powers 等固定说法。"},"normal":[{"en":"Same root as investigation: this adjective describes anything whose job is to follow the trail.","cn":"与 investigation 同根：这个形容词描述任何以循迹为职责的东西。"},{"en":"Investigative journalism follows documents the way police follow footprints.","cn":"调查报道追文件，正如警察追脚印。"},{"en":"Investigative powers mean you may compel evidence; they do not mean you may punish.","cn":"调查权意味着可以强制取证，并不意味着可以惩罚。"},{"en":"An investigative procedure in hospital is for diagnosis, not for cure.","cn":"医院里的检查性操作是为了诊断，而不是为了治愈。"},{"en":"An investigative habit reads every claim as a possible trail.","cn":"追查习惯把每个说法都读成一条可能的痕迹。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The adjective marks purpose, not profession: a student, a nurse, or a reporter can all work investigatively.","cn":"这个形容词标记目的，而不是职业：学生、护士或记者都可以以调查方式工作。"},{"en":"It assumes facts are hidden but reachable, which is both its optimism and its limit.","cn":"它假定事实虽被隐藏却可抵达，这既是它的乐观，也是它的限度。"},{"en":"Every investigative act asks the same question: what trace would this claim leave if it were true?","cn":"每一次调查性行动都问同一个问题：如果这个说法为真，它会留下什么痕迹？"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Investigative reporting exposed the illegal dumping.","cn":"调查性报道揭露了非法倾倒行为。"},{"en":"The agency has investigative powers but no authority to prosecute.","cn":"该机构有调查权，但没有起诉权。"},{"en":"The scan is investigative only and will not treat the lesion.","cn":"这次扫描仅为检查性质，不会治疗病灶。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因外斯提给提舞”——沿着外面的脚印“提”出证据，还带着追查的架势 → investigative 调查性的、侦查的","word":"investigative"},"root":"in-（进入）+ 拉丁语 vestigium“脚印”、vestigare“追踪”+ -ive；字面义“循迹进入的”，核心是“以查明事实为目的的”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of investigative all describe a purpose: reporting, policing, techniques, committees, legal powers, research teaching, diagnosis, and sceptical habit. The adjective never names a person; it names what the work is for.","cn":"investigative 的八个义项都描述一种目的：报道、警务、手段、委员会、法律权力、研究教学、诊断与怀疑习惯。这个形容词从不命名人，它命名工作的目的。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a searchlight following footprints, leaving no trace unexamined.","cn":"核心意象：一束探照灯沿着脚印照过去，不放过任何痕迹。"},"chain":["PURPOSE","TRACE","SEARCH","EVIDENCE","FINDING","ACCOUNT"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S8","en":"DISPOSITION AND PRESS: reporting and personal scepticism both treat claims as trails.","cn":"态度与新闻：报道与个人怀疑都把说法当作痕迹。"},{"senses":"S2 · S3","en":"POLICE WORK: units and techniques exist to produce evidence that others can check.","cn":"警务：部门与手段的存在，是为了产出可被他人核对的证据。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"AUTHORITY: committees and legal powers are the formal right to inquire, not to punish.","cn":"权威：委员会与法律权力是正式调查权，而不是惩罚权。"},{"senses":"S6","en":"LEARNING: inquiry-based teaching turns students into followers of trails.","cn":"学习：探究式教学把学生变成循迹者。"},{"senses":"S7","en":"MEDICINE: diagnostic procedures follow signs inside the body to their source.","cn":"医学：诊断性操作顺着体内征象追到源头。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Investigative is investigate + -ive, with investigatory as the -ory variant. Both come from Latin investigare and vestigium. The family also contains vestige and vestigial, which preserve the literal footprint.","cn":"investigative 是 investigate + -ive，investigatory 是 -ory 变体。两者都来自拉丁语 investigare 与 vestigium。家族还包含 vestige 与 vestigial，保留字面的“脚印”义。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin vestigium 'footprint' gave vestigare 'track' and investigare 'track into'. The look-alike invest is unrelated: it comes from investire 'clothe', based on vestis 'garment'.","cn":"拉丁语 vestigium“脚印”给出 vestigare“追踪”与 investigare“追进去”。形近的 invest 无关：它来自 investire“穿衣”，词根是 vestis“衣服”。"},"items":[{"word":"investigative","structure":"investigate + -ive","meaning":"serving or relating to investigation","meaningCN":"调查的；调查性的（-ive 构成形容词）","example":"The unit does investigative work.","exampleCN":"这个部门做调查工作。"},{"word":"investigate","structure":"Latin investigare, in- + vestigare 'track'","meaning":"to search out facts","meaningCN":"调查；侦查（字面“循迹进入”）","example":"They investigated the complaint.","exampleCN":"他们调查了这项投诉。"},{"word":"investigation","structure":"investigate + -ion","meaning":"a systematic inquiry","meaningCN":"调查；侦查（-ion 构成名词）","example":"The investigation is still open.","exampleCN":"调查仍在进行。"},{"word":"investigator","structure":"investigate + -or","meaning":"one who carries out an inquiry","meaningCN":"调查员；侦查员（-or 表施动者）","example":"The investigator interviewed ten witnesses.","exampleCN":"调查员访谈了十名证人。"},{"word":"investigatory","structure":"investigate + -ory","meaning":"of the nature of an inquiry","meaningCN":"调查性质的（-ory 构成形容词）","example":"The panel has investigatory authority.","exampleCN":"该小组拥有调查权。"},{"word":"reinvestigate","structure":"re- (again) + investigate","meaning":"to inquire again","meaningCN":"重新调查（re- 表再次）","example":"The archive was reinvestigated.","exampleCN":"这些档案被重新调查。"},{"word":"vestige","structure":"Latin vestigium 'footprint'","meaning":"a remaining trace","meaningCN":"痕迹；遗迹（直接借自拉丁名词）","example":"A vestige of the old road survives.","exampleCN":"旧路的一点残迹仍在。"},{"word":"vestigial","structure":"vestigium + -alis → English -al","meaning":"remaining as a trace, often without function","meaningCN":"残留的；退化的（vestigium + -al）","example":"The tail is vestigial in this species.","exampleCN":"这个物种的尾巴已退化。"},{"word":"invest","structure":"Latin investire 'clothe', from vestis 'garment'","meaning":"to commit money or effort","meaningCN":"投资；投入（同形不同源）","example":"The fund invests in clean energy.","exampleCN":"该基金投资清洁能源。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"vestigium","structure":"second-declension noun","meaning":"footprint, trace","meaningCN":"脚印；痕迹"},{"word":"vestigare","structure":"verb from vestigium","meaning":"to track, follow a trail","meaningCN":"追踪；循迹"},{"word":"investigare","structure":"in- 'into' + vestigare","meaning":"to track down, search out","meaningCN":"追查；查出"},{"word":"investigatus","structure":"past participle of investigare","meaning":"searched out, investigated","meaningCN":"被追查的；被调查的"}]}},{"word":"justification","ipa_uk":"/ˌdʒʌstɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/","ipa_us":"/ˌdʒʌstɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/","definition_zh":"正当理由；辩护；辩解；（神学）称义；（排版）两端对齐","definition_en":"the act of showing that something is right or reasonable; a reason given in defence; (theology) the state of being made righteous; (printing) the alignment of text to both margins","core_image":"天平两端分别放上指控与证据，指针最终停在水平位置","scene":"听证会上，发言人出示三份检测报告。The three reports are the justification for that decision.","sceneCN":"这里 justification 是「正当理由」（第 1 个义项：证明某决定合理的依据）；句意：这三份报告就是该决定的正当理由。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"正当理由；辩护（可数指一条理由，不可数指证明合理的过程）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（神学）称义；（排版）两端对齐（专业义，常带修饰语）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"justification for A","zh":"对 A 的正当理由"},{"phrase":"provide justification","zh":"提供理由"},{"phrase":"without justification","zh":"没有正当理由"},{"phrase":"economic justification","zh":"经济上的合理性"},{"phrase":"justification by faith","zh":"因信称义"},{"phrase":"left justification","zh":"左对齐（排版）"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数（一般／不可数）","form":"justification"},{"label":"复数（多条理由）","form":"justifications"},{"label":"作定语（名词修饰名词）","form":"justification statement"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"justify","pos":"v.","zh":"证明……正当；为……辩护；对齐"},{"word":"justifiable","pos":"adj.","zh":"有正当理由的；可辩护的"},{"word":"justifiably","pos":"adv.","zh":"有理由地"},{"word":"unjustified","pos":"adj.","zh":"没有正当理由的"},{"word":"justificatory","pos":"adj.","zh":"辩护性的"},{"word":"justice","pos":"n.","zh":"正义；公正；司法"},{"word":"just","pos":"adj./adv.","zh":"公正的；恰好"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Showing something to be reasonable","titleCN":"证明某事合理","definition":"the act of demonstrating that a decision, claim, or action is right or reasonable","definitionCN":"证明某个决定、主张或行为正确或合理的行为","example":"The report offers a strong justification for raising the minimum wage.","exampleCN":"这份报告为提高最低工资提供了有力理由。","why":"Justification is justify + -ation. Justify comes from Late Latin justificare, justus 'just' + facere 'to make': to make something just, or to show that it already is. The suffix names the act of making that showing.","whyCN":"justification 是 justify + -ation。justify 源自晚期拉丁语 justificare，即 justus“公正”+ facere“使”：使某事成为公正的，或表明它本就公正。后缀命名的是这一“表明”的行为。"},{"no":"02","title":"A defence offered for conduct","titleCN":"为行为提出的辩解","definition":"a reason put forward to defend an action that others may criticise","definitionCN":"为他人可能批评的行为提出的辩护理由","example":"His justification for leaving early was that the trains had stopped.","exampleCN":"他早退的理由是列车已经停运。","why":"This sense is personal and often defensive: the justification is offered after the act, to answer a challenge. The word assumes a critic exists, which is why it often sounds like an argument rather than a proof.","whyCN":"这个义项是个人化的，常带防御性：理由在行为之后提出，用来回应质疑。这个词预设有一个批评者存在，所以它常听起来像论辩而非证明。"},{"no":"03","title":"Justification in theology","titleCN":"神学上的称义","definition":"the act by which God is said to make a sinner righteous, central to Reformation disputes","definitionCN":"上帝使罪人成为义人的行为，是宗教改革争论的核心","example":"Luther taught justification by faith alone.","exampleCN":"路德教导“唯独因信称义”。","why":"Theology uses the word in its strongest sense: not a claim that someone is just, but a change that makes them so. The Latin facere 'make' is doing real work here, unlike in the everyday sense.","whyCN":"神学用这个词的最强意义：不是声称某人公正，而是使其成为公正的改变。这里拉丁语 facere“使”真正起作用，与日常义不同。"},{"no":"04","title":"Legal or official grounds","titleCN":"法律或官方依据","definition":"the legal grounds that make an action permissible or a claim admissible","definitionCN":"使某行为被允许或某主张可被接受的法律依据","example":"The court found no legal justification for the search.","exampleCN":"法院认定这次搜查没有法律依据。","why":"Law asks not whether an action was reasonable in general but whether it was authorised. Justification here is a formal finding that the required grounds existed.","whyCN":"法律不问行为在一般意义上是否合理，而问它是否被授权。这里的 justification 是对“所需依据确实存在”的正式认定。"},{"no":"05","title":"Text alignment in printing","titleCN":"排版上的对齐","definition":"the adjustment of spacing so that lines of text align evenly at the margin","definitionCN":"调整字距，使各行文字在页边对齐","example":"Full justification stretched the words across the narrow column.","exampleCN":"两端对齐把字距拉宽以填满窄栏。","why":"This sense comes from the same Latin root by a different path: to justify a line is to make its edges 'just' or exact. The printing trade borrowed the moral word and gave it a mechanical meaning.","whyCN":"这个义项来自同一拉丁词根但路径不同：让一行文字的边缘“正”或精确。印刷业借用了这个道德词，赋予它机械含义。"},{"no":"06","title":"Epistemic justification","titleCN":"认识论上的证成","definition":"the reason or warrant that makes a belief reasonable to hold","definitionCN":"使某个信念有理由被持有的依据或保证","example":"Philosophers distinguish justification from mere belief.","exampleCN":"哲学家把证成与单纯的相信区分开来。","why":"Philosophy asks what makes a belief acceptable rather than merely held. Justification here is the warrant, and the debates are about whether it must be internal, external, or both.","whyCN":"哲学追问是什么使一个信念可被接受，而不只是被持有。这里的 justification 是保证，争论在于它必须是内在的、外在的，还是两者兼有。"},{"no":"07","title":"Grounds in an argument","titleCN":"论证中的依据","definition":"the premises or evidence that support a conclusion in reasoning","definitionCN":"推理中支持结论的前提或证据","example":"The justification for the inference lies in the correlation itself.","exampleCN":"这一推断的依据就在相关性本身。","why":"Logic needs a word for the support relation between premises and conclusion. Justification names that relation, not the psychological confidence of the person reasoning.","whyCN":"逻辑学需要一个词来指前提与结论之间的支持关系。justification 命名这一关系，而不是推理者的心理确信。"},{"no":"08","title":"Business case for a request","titleCN":"商业上的理由说明","definition":"a written case showing why a purchase, project, or budget is worth approving","definitionCN":"说明某项采购、项目或预算值得批准的书面论证","example":"The manager attached a two-page justification to the purchase order.","exampleCN":"经理在采购单后附了两页理由说明。","why":"Organizations require justification to make decisions auditable: someone must show that the cost buys a benefit. The word turns a preference into a record.","whyCN":"组织要求理由说明，是为了让决策可被审计：必须有人证明这笔成本换来了收益。这个词把偏好变成记录。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Justification is justify + -ation. Justify comes from Late Latin justificare, from justus 'just, lawful' and facere 'to make'. Justus itself goes back to ius 'law, right', the same root that gives justice, judge, and jury.","cn":"justification 是 justify + -ation。justify 源自晚期拉丁语 justificare，由 justus“公正、合法”与 facere“使”构成。justus 本身上溯 ius“法、权利”，同一词根还给出 justice、judge 与 jury。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Latin ius (genitive iuris) meant 'law, right, justice'. Justus 'lawful, just' came from it, and iudex 'judge' was literally ius + dicere 'say the law'.","cn":"拉丁语 ius（属格 iuris）意为“法、权利、正义”。justus“合法的、公正的”由此而来，而 iudex“法官”字面是 ius + dicere“说出法律”。"},{"era":"LATE LATIN","en":"Justificare combined justus with facere 'to make': to make someone or something just, or to show it as just. The noun justificatio named this making.","cn":"justificare 把 justus 与 facere“使”结合：使某人或某物成为公正的，或表明其为公正。名词 justificatio 命名这一“使之”过程。"},{"era":"14C. ENGLISH","en":"English justification entered through Old French in the fourteenth century. The word carried both the everyday sense 'defence' and the theological sense 'being made righteous'.","cn":"英语 justification 于 14 世纪经古法语进入。这个词同时带有日常义“辩护”与神学义“被称为义”。"},{"era":"16C. REFORMATION","en":"The Reformation made justification a contested technical term: whether it is a change in the sinner or a verdict about them. The word's later legal and philosophical uses inherited this precision.","cn":"宗教改革使 justification 成为有争议的术语：它是罪人身上的改变，还是关于他的判决。这个词后来的法律与哲学用法继承了这种精确性。"},{"era":"17C.–18C. PRINTING","en":"The printing trade used 'justify' for making a line's edges exact, which produced the noun 'justification' in typography. The moral word acquired a mechanical sense.","cn":"印刷业用 justify 指把一行文字的边缘弄“正”，由此产生排版义 justification。这个道德词获得机械含义。"},{"era":"20C. PHILOSOPHY AND MANAGEMENT","en":"Analytic philosophy made justification a central term for the warrant of belief, while organizations made 'justification' a written business case. The word now covers proof, defence, and record.","cn":"分析哲学使 justification 成为信念保证的核心术语，组织则把 justification 变成书面商业论证。这个词如今覆盖证明、辩护与记录。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates words built on ius 'law' or on other roots; the near-meaning group separates reason, defence, and excuse.","cn":"形近组区分建立在 ius“法”或其他词根上的词；近义组区分“理由”“辩护”与“借口”。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"justice","ipa":"/ˈdʒʌstɪs/","tag":"same ius root, noun of rightness","definition":"fairness or the administration of law. It comes from Latin iustitia, from iustus, but names the virtue itself rather than the argument for a decision.","definitionCN":"公平或司法。它来自拉丁语 iustitia，源自 iustus，但命名的是美德本身，而不是为某个决定作论证。"},{"word":"judgment","ipa":"/ˈdʒʌdʒmənt/","tag":"same ius, different root verb","definition":"a decision or opinion. It comes from iudicium, built on ius + dicere 'say', so it names the verdict, not the grounds offered for it.","definitionCN":"裁决或判断。它来自 iudicium，由 ius + dicere“说”构成，因此命名的是判决，而非为其提出的依据。"},{"word":"verification","ipa":"/ˌverɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/","tag":"different root: verus 'true'","definition":"the checking of a fact or claim. It comes from verus 'true', and asks whether something is factually correct rather than whether it is justified.","definitionCN":"对事实或主张的核查。它来自 verus“真”，问的是某事在事实上是否正确，而不是它是否有正当理由。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"reason","ipa":"/ˈriːzn/","tag":"general","definition":"a cause or explanation for something. It can be neutral or trivial, while justification implies that the reason is adequate to defend the act.","definitionCN":"某事的原因或解释。它可以是中性或琐碎的，而 justification 暗示该理由足以为此行为辩护。"},{"word":"defence","ipa":"/dɪˈfens/","tag":"response to attack","definition":"an argument or action that protects against criticism. Justification is the content of such a defence: the grounds that make it work.","definitionCN":"为抵御批评而提出的论证或行动。justification 是这种辩护的内容：使它成立的那些依据。"},{"word":"excuse","ipa":"/ɪkˈskjuːz/","tag":"weak or evasive","definition":"a reason offered to avoid blame, often not accepted by the hearer. It is weaker than justification, which claims genuine adequacy.","definitionCN":"为逃避责备而给的理由，常不被听者接受。它比 justification 弱，后者声称确实充分。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real associations: ius 'law' + facere 'make', the theological phrase justification by faith, and the typographic use of justified text.","cn":"真实联想：ius“法”+ facere“使”、神学说法 justification by faith，以及排版中的 justified text。"},"normal":[{"en":"justus means 'lawful' and facere means 'make': justification is making a case stand as right.","cn":"justus 意为“合法的”，facere 意为“使”：justification 就是让一个说法站得住、显得正当。"},{"en":"justice, judge, jury, and justification all descend from ius, the Latin word for law.","cn":"justice、judge、jury、justification 都源自 ius，即拉丁语“法”。"},{"en":"In theology the word is strongest: it makes a person righteous, not merely calls them so.","cn":"在神学里这个词最强：它使人成为义人，而不只是称他为义人。"},{"en":"In printing, to justify a line is to make its edges exact — 'just' in the geometric sense.","cn":"在印刷中，justify a line 是把行边弄“正”——几何意义上的“正”。"},{"en":"A purchase order needs a justification so that the spending can be audited later.","cn":"采购单需要理由说明，好让这笔支出日后可被审计。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The word always answers a challenge: it exists because someone might say 'no' or 'why'.","cn":"这个词总是在回应质疑：它之所以存在，是因为有人可能说“不行”或“为什么”。"},{"en":"It claims adequacy, not truth — a justification can be sound and the decision still wrong.","cn":"它主张的是充分性，而不是真理性——理由可以成立，决定仍然可能是错的。"},{"en":"From courtroom to column width, the same idea recurs: making edges come out even.","cn":"从法庭到栏宽，同一个想法反复出现：让边缘变得齐整。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"There is no justification for treating one group differently.","cn":"没有正当理由区别对待某个群体。"},{"en":"The theologian wrote about justification by faith alone.","cn":"这位神学家论述了“唯独因信称义”。"},{"en":"The columns look tidy because the text is fully justified.","cn":"因为文字采用了两端对齐，各栏看起来很整齐。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“扎斯提飞开心”——把理由“扎”实、“提”出来，让人飞着也开心地接受 → justification 正当理由、辩护","word":"justification"},"root":"拉丁语 ius/iur-“法、权利”→ iustus“公正的”+ facere“使”+ -ation；字面义“使之公正、使之站得住”，核心是“为某决定提供充分依据”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of justification all answer the question 'why is this acceptable?': a decision, a conduct, a sinner, a search, a line of type, a belief, an inference, and a purchase. The word always offers grounds, and grounds can always be challenged.","cn":"justification 的八个义项都在回答“这为什么可以被接受？”：一个决定、一种行为、一个罪人、一次搜查、一行文字、一个信念、一次推断、一笔采购。这个词总是提供依据，而依据总是可以被质疑。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a balance with accusation on one side and evidence on the other, settling level.","cn":"核心意象：天平一端放指控、一端放证据，最终停在水平。"},"chain":["CHALLENGE","GROUNDS","WEIGHING","ADEQUACY","VERDICT","ACCEPTANCE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"EVERYDAY DEFENCE: a decision or an action is shown to be reasonable, often after criticism.","cn":"日常辩护：决定或行为被表明合理，常在批评之后。"},{"senses":"S3 · S4","en":"AUTHORITY: theology and law decide whether the grounds actually transform or authorise.","cn":"权威：神学与法律判定依据究竟能改变人，还是能授权行为。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"TYPOGRAPHY: the same word makes a line's edges exact.","cn":"排版：同一个词让一行文字的边缘变得精确。"},{"senses":"S6 · S7","en":"REASONING: philosophy and logic ask what warrants a belief or an inference.","cn":"推理：哲学与逻辑追问是什么为信念或推断提供保证。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"MANAGEMENT: a written case turns a preference into an auditable record.","cn":"管理：书面论证把偏好变成可审计的记录。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Justification is justify + -ation, from Late Latin justificare (justus + facere). The family is divided between derivatives of justify and the ius 'law' relatives justice, just, judge, and jury.","cn":"justification 是 justify + -ation，源自晚期拉丁语 justificare（justus + facere）。家族分为 justify 的派生词与 ius“法”的亲属词 justice、just、judge、jury。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin ius (genitive iuris) 'law, right' produced iustus 'just', iustitia 'justice', iudex 'judge' (ius + dicere 'say'), and iudicium 'judgement'. Justificare is a Late Latin compound of iustus with facere 'make'.","cn":"拉丁语 ius（属格 iuris）“法、权利”产生 iustus“公正的”、iustitia“正义”、iudex“法官”（ius + dicere“说”）、iudicium“判断”。justificare 是晚期拉丁语中 iustus 与 facere“使”的复合词。"},"items":[{"word":"justification","structure":"justify + -ation","meaning":"grounds that show something is right; alignment","meaningCN":"正当理由；辩护；对齐（-ation 构成名词）","example":"No justification was given for the delay.","exampleCN":"对这次延误没有给出理由。"},{"word":"justify","structure":"Late Latin justificare (justus + facere)","meaning":"to show to be right; to align text","meaningCN":"证明正当；为……辩护；对齐（源自晚期拉丁语）","example":"How can you justify the expense?","exampleCN":"你如何证明这笔开支合理？"},{"word":"justifiable","structure":"justify + -able","meaning":"able to be defended as right","meaningCN":"有正当理由的（-able 表可能）","example":"The delay was justifiable in the circumstances.","exampleCN":"在当时情况下，延误是有理由的。"},{"word":"justifiably","structure":"justifiable + -ly","meaning":"with good grounds","meaningCN":"有理由地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"She was justifiably angry.","exampleCN":"她生气是有道理的。"},{"word":"unjustified","structure":"un- (not) + justified","meaning":"without adequate grounds","meaningCN":"没有正当理由的（un- 表否定）","example":"The criticism was unjustified.","exampleCN":"这项批评没有道理。"},{"word":"justificatory","structure":"justification + -ory","meaning":"serving to justify","meaningCN":"辩护性的（-ory 构成形容词）","example":"He added a justificatory footnote.","exampleCN":"他加了一条辩解性脚注。"},{"word":"justice","structure":"Latin iustitia, from iustus","meaning":"fairness; the law in operation","meaningCN":"正义；司法（iustitia）","example":"The victims demanded justice.","exampleCN":"受害者要求正义。"},{"word":"just","structure":"Latin iustus 'lawful, fair'","meaning":"fair and lawful","meaningCN":"公正的；合法的（iustus）","example":"It was a just decision.","exampleCN":"这是一个公正的决定。"},{"word":"judge","structure":"Latin iudex, from ius + dicere 'say the law'","meaning":"one who decides cases","meaningCN":"法官；评判者（ius + dicere）","example":"The judge heard both sides.","exampleCN":"法官听取了双方陈述。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"ius","structure":"ius, iuris (third declension)","meaning":"law, right, justice","meaningCN":"法；权利；正义"},{"word":"iustus","structure":"adjective from ius","meaning":"lawful, just","meaningCN":"合法的；公正的"},{"word":"iustificare","structure":"iustus + facere 'make' (Late Latin)","meaning":"to make just, justify","meaningCN":"使成为义；证明正当"},{"word":"iustificatio","structure":"iustificare + -tio (action noun)","meaning":"a making just, justification","meaningCN":"称义；证明正当"}]}},{"word":"laboratory","ipa_uk":"/ləˈbɒrətri/","ipa_us":"/ˈlæbərətɔːri/","definition_zh":"实验室；实验大楼；（大学的）实验课教室；（口语）实验室、检验室","definition_en":"a room or building equipped for scientific experiments, research, teaching, or the testing of materials and samples","core_image":"一间摆满仪器、贴着标签的房间：每个瓶子里都装着一个待验证的问题","scene":"化学课上，老师说这些样品要送去做元素分析。These samples go to the laboratory for elemental analysis.","sceneCN":"这里 laboratory 是「实验室」（第 1 个义项：进行科学实验的场所）；句意：这些样品要送到实验室做元素分析。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"实验室；实验大楼（可数，指场所）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（作定语）实验室的；实验条件下的（如 laboratory test）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"research laboratory","zh":"研究实验室"},{"phrase":"laboratory test","zh":"实验室检验"},{"phrase":"laboratory equipment","zh":"实验设备"},{"phrase":"language laboratory","zh":"语言实验室"},{"phrase":"laboratory conditions","zh":"实验条件"},{"phrase":"laboratory assistant","zh":"实验助理"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"laboratory"},{"label":"复数","form":"laboratories"},{"label":"口语缩略形式","form":"lab"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"lab","pos":"n.","zh":"实验室（口语缩略）"},{"word":"labor","pos":"n./v.","zh":"劳动；工作（美式拼写）"},{"word":"laborious","pos":"adj.","zh":"费力的；辛苦的"},{"word":"laboriously","pos":"adv.","zh":"费力地"},{"word":"elaborate","pos":"v./adj.","zh":"精心制作；详尽的"},{"word":"collaborate","pos":"v.","zh":"合作；协作"},{"word":"collaboration","pos":"n.","zh":"合作；协作"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Room for scientific experiments","titleCN":"进行科学实验的房间","definition":"a room fitted with instruments and benches where scientific work is carried out","definitionCN":"配备仪器与工作台、用于开展科学工作的房间","example":"The samples were analysed in a clean laboratory.","exampleCN":"样品在洁净实验室中分析。","why":"Laboratory is Latin laboratorium, 'a place for labour', from laborare 'to work' and labor 'work'. The word says nothing about science; it names a place set aside for work, and science later made that place its home.","whyCN":"laboratory 是拉丁语 laboratorium“劳作之处”，来自 laborare“工作”与 labor“劳动”。这个词本身与科学无关；它命名一个专门用于工作的地方，后来科学才把这个地方变成自己的家。"},{"no":"02","title":"A research institution","titleCN":"研究机构","definition":"an organization or large facility devoted to research, often named after its field or sponsor","definitionCN":"专门从事研究的机构或大型设施，常以领域或资助方命名","example":"The national laboratory runs the particle accelerator.","exampleCN":"国家实验室运行这台粒子加速器。","why":"As research grew expensive, the word scaled from a room to an institution. A laboratory can now be a campus with thousands of staff, while the singular article still suggests a shared place of work.","whyCN":"当研究变得昂贵，这个词从一间屋子扩展到一个机构。实验室现在可以是有数千员工的园区，而单数冠词仍暗示一个共同的工作场所。"},{"no":"03","title":"Teaching laboratory","titleCN":"教学实验室","definition":"a room where students perform set experiments as part of a course","definitionCN":"学生作为课程的一部分进行规定实验的房间","example":"The laboratory session lasts three hours every Thursday.","exampleCN":"实验课每周四持续三小时。","why":"In education the word names a scheduled activity as well as a place: 'laboratory' on a timetable means practical work. The emphasis moves from discovery to training.","whyCN":"在教育中，这个词既命名场所，也命名一项排定的活动：课表上的 laboratory 意为实践课。重点从发现转向训练。"},{"no":"04","title":"Medical testing laboratory","titleCN":"医学检验室","definition":"a facility where blood, tissue, or other samples are tested to support diagnosis","definitionCN":"对血液、组织或其他样本进行检验以支持诊断的场所","example":"The laboratory reported the results within an hour.","exampleCN":"检验室在一小时内报告了结果。","why":"Hospitals use the word for the back room where evidence is produced. The laboratory does not treat the patient; it supplies the numbers on which treatment depends.","whyCN":"医院用这个词指产出证据的后场。检验室不治疗病人，它提供治疗所依赖的数字。"},{"no":"05","title":"Language laboratory","titleCN":"语言实验室","definition":"a room with audio equipment where students practise listening and speaking","definitionCN":"配备音频设备、供学生练习听说能力的房间","example":"The language laboratory has booths for individual practice.","exampleCN":"语言实验室有供个人练习的隔间。","why":"This mid-twentieth-century sense applied the word to language teaching, borrowed from the idea of controlled practice. The equipment has changed, but the name survives in universities.","whyCN":"这一 20 世纪中的义项把该词用于语言教学，借自“受控练习”的观念。设备已变，但名称在大学里保留下来。"},{"no":"06","title":"Photographic darkroom","titleCN":"摄影暗房","definition":"a darkened room used for developing film and making prints, historically called a photographic laboratory","definitionCN":"用于冲洗胶片与制作照片的暗室，旧称 photographic laboratory","example":"He spent the night in the photographic laboratory.","exampleCN":"他在摄影暗房里待了一夜。","why":"Photography adopted the word because the darkroom is a place of controlled chemical work. The sense is now archaic but survives in the phrase 'photo lab'.","whyCN":"摄影采用这个词，因为暗房是受控化学工作的场所。这个义项现已陈旧，但保存在 photo lab 这一说法中。"},{"no":"07","title":"Production or post-production studio","titleCN":"制作室；后期工作室","definition":"a studio where animation, film, or sound work is produced, often called a lab in informal use","definitionCN":"制作动画、影片或声音的工作室，口语中常称 lab","example":"The animation laboratory finished the sequence in a week.","exampleCN":"动画工作室一周内完成了这个段落。","why":"Creative industries borrowed 'lab' for workshops that experiment with technique. The word suggests trial and iteration rather than manufacturing on a fixed line.","whyCN":"创意产业借用 lab 指试验技术的作坊。这个词暗示反复试做与迭代，而不是在固定流水线上制造。"},{"no":"08","title":"Laboratory as an adjective","titleCN":"作定语的实验室","definition":"used before another noun to mean 'done under controlled experimental conditions'","definitionCN":"置于名词前，表示“在受控实验条件下完成的”","example":"The laboratory results were promising but not yet tested in the field.","exampleCN":"实验室结果令人鼓舞，但尚未在实地检验。","why":"As a modifier, the word draws a boundary between controlled and real conditions. 'Laboratory conditions' means the world has been simplified so that one variable can be watched.","whyCN":"作修饰语时，这个词在受控条件与真实条件之间划界。laboratory conditions 意为世界被简化，以便观察单一变量。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Laboratory comes from Latin laboratorium 'a place for labour', from laborare 'to work', from labor 'work, toil'. English borrowed it in the seventeenth century; the scientific sense was fixed later, and the clipped form lab is a nineteenth-century convenience.","cn":"laboratory 来自拉丁语 laboratorium“劳作之处”，源自 laborare“工作”，而 laborare 又来自 labor“劳动、辛苦”。英语于 17 世纪借入；科学义后来才固定，缩略形式 lab 则是 19 世纪的便利说法。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Latin labor meant 'work, toil, hardship'. The verb laborare meant 'to work, toil', and laboratorium named a place where work is done. Nothing in the root points to science.","cn":"拉丁语 labor 意为“工作、辛劳、艰难”。动词 laborare 意为“工作、劳作”，laboratorium 命名做事的地方。词根中没有任何成分指向科学。"},{"era":"16C.–17C. ENGLISH","en":"English laboratory appears in the seventeenth century, first for places of chemical and alchemical work. The word inherited the Latin sense of a room reserved for a particular kind of labour.","cn":"英语 laboratory 于 17 世纪出现，最早指化学与炼金术工作的场所。这个词继承了拉丁语“为某类劳动保留的房间”之义。"},{"era":"18C.–19C. SCIENCE","en":"As experimental science professionalised, the laboratory became the standard site of discovery, and the word spread to universities, hospitals, and industry.","cn":"随着实验科学专业化，实验室成为发现的标准场所，这个词扩展到大学、医院与工业界。"},{"era":"19C. CLIPPING","en":"The shortened form lab is recorded in the late nineteenth century, first in university and medical slang before becoming standard informal English.","cn":"缩略形式 lab 于 19 世纪晚期被记录，先在大学与医学俚语中使用，后成为标准口语。"},{"era":"20C. INSTITUTIONS","en":"Big science turned laboratories into named institutions, and education turned them into scheduled classes. The word now covers a room, a campus, and a timetabled activity.","cn":"大科学把实验室变成有名字的机构，教育把它变成排定的课程。这个词如今同时指一间屋子、一个园区和一项课表活动。"},{"era":"PRESENT","en":"Modern usage ranges from hospital testing rooms to animation studios. The common element remains the Latin one: a place set apart for a particular kind of work.","cn":"现代用法从医院检验室延伸到动画工作室。共同成分仍是拉丁语那个：为某类工作专门划出的地方。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates words that resemble laboratory but come from lavare or observare; the near-meaning group separates lab, workshop, and facility.","cn":"形近组区分外形相似但来自 lavare 或 observare 的词；近义组区分 lab、workshop 与 facility。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"lavatory","ipa":"/ˈlævətri/","tag":"different root: lavare 'wash'","definition":"a toilet or washroom. It comes from lavare 'to wash', not from labor 'work'; the resemblance is accidental.","definitionCN":"厕所或盥洗室。它来自 lavare“洗”，而非 labor“劳动”；相似纯属偶然。"},{"word":"observatory","ipa":"/əbˈzɜːvətəri/","tag":"different root: observare 'watch'","definition":"a building for watching the sky. Latin observare 'watch' supplies the root; the suffix -ory is shared, the stem is not.","definitionCN":"观测天空的建筑。拉丁语 observare“观察”提供词根；后缀 -ory 相同，词干不同。"},{"word":"laborious","ipa":"/ləˈbɔːriəs/","tag":"same labor, adjective","definition":"requiring much effort. It shares the Latin labor root but describes the effort of work, not the place where work happens.","definitionCN":"需要很多努力的。它共享拉丁 labor 词根，但描述工作的费力程度，而非工作发生的地点。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"lab","ipa":"/læb/","tag":"informal","definition":"the clipped, everyday word for a laboratory. It is the same place, used in speech and in compound names such as lab coat.","definitionCN":"laboratory 的缩略日常说法。是同一个地方，用于口语以及 lab coat 这类复合词。"},{"word":"workshop","ipa":"/ˈwɜːkʃɒp/","tag":"making","definition":"a room where things are made or repaired. It stresses craft and production, while laboratory stresses testing and experiment.","definitionCN":"制作或修理物品的房间。它强调手艺与生产，而 laboratory 强调检验与实验。"},{"word":"facility","ipa":"/fəˈsɪləti/","tag":"general","definition":"a building or service provided for a purpose. It is the broad term; laboratory is one kind of facility with a specific function.","definitionCN":"为某目的提供的建筑或服务。它是宽泛用词；laboratory 是其中具有特定功能的一类设施。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real associations: Latin labor 'work', the seventeenth-century borrowing, and the everyday clipping lab.","cn":"真实联想：拉丁语 labor“劳动”、17 世纪借入，以及日常缩略形式 lab。"},"normal":[{"en":"labor means 'work': a laboratory is literally a place for work, not a place for science as such.","cn":"labor 意为“劳动”：laboratory 字面就是做事的地方，本身并不专指科学。"},{"en":"The same labor root gives laborious, elaborate, and collaborate — all about effort.","cn":"同一 labor 词根给出 laborious（费力的）、elaborate（精心制作）、collaborate（合作）——都与付出努力有关。"},{"en":"laboratory and lavatory look alike but lavatory comes from 'wash' — a classic trap.","cn":"laboratory 与 lavatory 外形相似，但 lavatory 来自“洗”——这是经典陷阱。"},{"en":"On a timetable, 'laboratory' means a practical class, not just a room.","cn":"在课表上，laboratory 意为实践课，而不只是一间房子。"},{"en":"Big science made the laboratory a named institution with thousands of staff.","cn":"大科学使实验室成为有数千员工的具名机构。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The word is about separation: a place cut off from ordinary life so that one kind of work can go on undisturbed.","cn":"这个词讲的是分隔：一块从日常生活中划出的地方，好让某类工作不被打扰地进行。"},{"en":"Science did not create the word; it moved into a room that already meant 'work'.","cn":"科学没有创造这个词；它搬进了一间本就意为“工作”的屋子。"},{"en":"When people say 'under laboratory conditions', they admit the world has been simplified.","cn":"当人们说 under laboratory conditions 时，他们承认世界已被简化。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The laboratory tested the water for heavy metals.","cn":"实验室检测了水中的重金属。"},{"en":"Students spend Friday afternoon in the teaching laboratory.","cn":"学生周五下午在教学实验室上课。"},{"en":"The drug worked in laboratory conditions but failed in trials.","cn":"这种药在实验条件下有效，却在试验中失败。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“来包了托瑞”——来了一包样品，托付给瑞那里的房间去检验 → laboratory 实验室","word":"laboratory"},"root":"拉丁语 labor“劳动”+ -atorium（场所后缀），经 laborare“工作”构成；字面义“劳作之处”，核心是“为某类工作专门划出的场所”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of laboratory all name a place set apart for a particular kind of work: experiment, research, teaching, diagnosis, language practice, photography, animation, or controlled testing. The word never specifies science; context does.","cn":"laboratory 的八个义项都命名一块为某类工作专门划出的地方：实验、研究、教学、诊断、语言练习、摄影、动画或受控检验。这个词从不明确指科学；是语境在指。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a room full of instruments and labelled bottles, each holding a question to be tested.","cn":"核心意象：一间摆满仪器与标签瓶子的房间，每个瓶子里装着一个待检验的问题。"},"chain":["PLACE APART","WORK","INSTRUMENTS","TEST","RESULT","KNOWLEDGE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"RESEARCH: a room and then an institution devoted to producing new knowledge.","cn":"研究：先是一间屋子，后来是专门生产新知识的机构。"},{"senses":"S3 · S5","en":"TEACHING: scheduled practical classes and language booths turn the place into a method.","cn":"教学：排定的实践课与语言隔间把场所变成一种方法。"},{"senses":"S4","en":"DIAGNOSIS: the medical laboratory supplies numbers on which treatment depends.","cn":"诊断：医学检验室提供治疗所依赖的数字。"},{"senses":"S6 · S7","en":"CRAFT: darkrooms and animation studios use 'lab' for controlled creative work.","cn":"技艺：暗房与动画工作室用 lab 指受控的创造性工作。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"BOUNDARY: as a modifier, the word marks the difference between simplified and real conditions.","cn":"边界：作修饰语时，这个词标记简化条件与真实条件之间的差别。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Laboratory is Latin laboratorium from labor 'work'. The family splits between place words (laboratory, lab) and effort words (laborious, elaborate, collaborate), all sharing the same labor root.","cn":"laboratory 是拉丁语 laboratorium，源自 labor“劳动”。家族分为场所词（laboratory、lab）与努力词（laborious、elaborate、collaborate），都共享 labor 词根。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin labor 'toil' and laborare 'to work' produced laboratorium 'place of work', laboriosus 'full of toil', and the compound elaborare 'work out'. Collaborare is a modern Latin-derived compound meaning 'work together'.","cn":"拉丁语 labor“辛劳”与 laborare“工作”产生 laboratorium“工作之处”、laboriosus“充满辛劳的”，以及复合词 elaborare“做出来”。collaborare 是源自拉丁语的现代复合词，意为“一起工作”。"},"items":[{"word":"laboratory","structure":"Latin laboratorium, from laborare 'work'","meaning":"a place equipped for scientific or technical work","meaningCN":"实验室（源自“工作之处”）","example":"The laboratory is on the second floor.","exampleCN":"实验室在二楼。"},{"word":"lab","structure":"clipping of laboratory","meaning":"informal word for a laboratory","meaningCN":"实验室（口语缩略）","example":"Meet me in the lab at nine.","exampleCN":"九点在实验室见。"},{"word":"labor","structure":"Latin labor 'work, toil'","meaning":"work, especially physical effort","meaningCN":"劳动；工作（labor）","example":"The work required manual labor.","exampleCN":"这项工作需要体力劳动。"},{"word":"laborious","structure":"Latin laboriosus, from labor","meaning":"requiring much effort","meaningCN":"费力的；辛苦的（-ious 构成形容词）","example":"The copying was laborious.","exampleCN":"抄写工作很费力。"},{"word":"laboriously","structure":"laborious + -ly","meaning":"with great effort","meaningCN":"费力地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"He climbed laboriously up the slope.","exampleCN":"他费力地爬上山坡。"},{"word":"elaborate","structure":"e- (out) + laborare 'work'","meaning":"to work out in detail; detailed","meaningCN":"精心制作；详尽的（e- + laborare）","example":"They elaborated the plan.","exampleCN":"他们细化了方案。"},{"word":"collaborate","structure":"com- (together) + laborare 'work'","meaning":"to work together","meaningCN":"合作；协作（com- + laborare）","example":"Two teams collaborated on the study.","exampleCN":"两个团队合作完成这项研究。"},{"word":"collaboration","structure":"collaborate + -ion","meaning":"joint work","meaningCN":"合作；协作（-ion 构成名词）","example":"The paper was a close collaboration.","exampleCN":"这篇论文是密切合作的成果。"},{"word":"belabor","structure":"be- (about) + labor 'work'","meaning":"to discuss something far too long","meaningCN":"反复赘述（be- + labor）","example":"Do not belabor the point.","exampleCN":"不要反复啰嗦这一点。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"labor","structure":"labor, laboris (third declension)","meaning":"work, toil, hardship","meaningCN":"劳动；辛劳；艰难"},{"word":"laborare","structure":"first-conjugation verb from labor","meaning":"to work, toil","meaningCN":"工作；劳作"},{"word":"laboratorium","structure":"laborare + -torium (place suffix)","meaning":"a place for work","meaningCN":"工作之处；实验室"},{"word":"laboriosus","structure":"labor + -iosus (full of)","meaning":"full of toil, laborious","meaningCN":"充满辛劳的；费力的"}]}},{"word":"landscape","ipa_uk":"/ˈlændskeɪp/","ipa_us":"/ˈlændskeɪp/","definition_zh":"风景；景观；地貌；（某一领域的）局面；（印刷、摄影）横向版式","definition_en":"the visible features of an area of land; a picture representing such scenery; the overall pattern of a field of activity; (printing) a page format wider than it is tall","core_image":"从高处望下去，田野、河流与道路拼成一整幅画","scene":"地理课上，老师把投影切成一幅航拍图。The valley landscape was left behind by a retreating glacier.","sceneCN":"这里 landscape 是「地貌景观」（第 1 个义项：一片土地的可见形态）；句意：这条河谷景观是冰川退却后留下的。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"风景；景观；地貌（可数指一片景观，不可数指景观类型）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（某领域的）局面；横向版式（常带修饰语，如 political landscape）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"natural landscape","zh":"自然景观"},{"phrase":"political landscape","zh":"政治格局"},{"phrase":"landscape painting","zh":"风景画"},{"phrase":"landscape architecture","zh":"景观设计"},{"phrase":"in landscape format","zh":"以横向版式"},{"phrase":"a changing landscape","zh":"不断变化的格局"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"landscape"},{"label":"复数","form":"landscapes"},{"label":"作定语（名词修饰名词）","form":"landscape design"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"landscaped","pos":"adj.","zh":"经景观设计的"},{"word":"landscaping","pos":"n.","zh":"景观布置；造景"},{"word":"landscaper","pos":"n.","zh":"景观设计师；园林工"},{"word":"landscape","pos":"v.","zh":"对……进行景观设计"},{"word":"seascape","pos":"n.","zh":"海景；海景画"},{"word":"cityscape","pos":"n.","zh":"城市景观"},{"word":"moonscape","pos":"n.","zh":"月球表面景观"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Visible features of land","titleCN":"一片土地的可见形态","definition":"the shape, texture, and features of an area of land, including hills, rivers, fields, and vegetation","definitionCN":"一片土地的形状、质地与特征，包括山丘、河流、田野与植被","example":"Glaciers shaped the landscape of this valley.","exampleCN":"冰川塑造了这条河谷的地貌。","why":"Landscape is borrowed from Dutch landschap, land plus -schap, a suffix of state or condition cognate with English -ship. The word began as 'the condition of the land', which is why it can name both a region and how that region looks.","whyCN":"landscape 借自荷兰语 landschap，由 land 加 -schap 构成，后者是表示状态或状况的后缀，与英语 -ship 同源。这个词最初意为“土地的状况”，所以它既能命名一片区域，也能命名这片区域的样子。"},{"no":"02","title":"A landscape painting","titleCN":"风景画","definition":"a painting or photograph whose main subject is natural scenery","definitionCN":"以自然景色为主要题材的绘画或摄影","example":"The museum bought a seventeenth-century Dutch landscape.","exampleCN":"博物馆买下一幅 17 世纪荷兰风景画。","why":"The word entered English in the sixteenth century as an art term: a picture of a land. Dutch painters made the genre famous, and the word travelled with the paintings.","whyCN":"这个词在 16 世纪作为艺术术语进入英语：一幅关于土地的画。荷兰画家使这一画种闻名，词随画一起传来。"},{"no":"03","title":"Landscape in geography and ecology","titleCN":"地理与生态学中的景观","definition":"an area considered as a system of interacting physical, biological, and human features","definitionCN":"被视作物理、生物与人文特征交互系统的区域","example":"Landscape ecology studies how patches of habitat connect.","exampleCN":"景观生态学研究栖息地斑块如何连接。","why":"Geography turned the word into a technical unit: a landscape is not just a view but a system with boundaries and flows. The visual sense survives inside the scientific one.","whyCN":"地理学把这个词变成技术单位：景观不只是视野，而是有边界与流动的系统。视觉义在科学义内部存活下来。"},{"no":"04","title":"The pattern of a field of activity","titleCN":"某一领域的格局","definition":"the overall arrangement of forces, players, or conditions in a particular area of activity","definitionCN":"某一活动领域中力量、参与者或条件的总体布局","example":"The merger changed the competitive landscape of the industry.","exampleCN":"这次合并改变了该行业的竞争格局。","why":"Twentieth-century business and political writing borrowed the word for a field of play: competitors occupy positions the way hills occupy a view. The metaphor is spatial, and it treats the situation as something seen from above.","whyCN":"20 世纪的商业与政治写作把这个词借来指一个竞技场：竞争者占据位置，就像山丘占据视野。这个比喻是空间性的，把局势当作从高处看到的东西。"},{"no":"05","title":"Landscape page format","titleCN":"横向版式","definition":"a page or image orientation in which the width is greater than the height","definitionCN":"宽度大于高度的页面或图像方向","example":"Print the map in landscape format so the whole route fits.","exampleCN":"把地图打成横向版式，好让整条路线容纳进来。","why":"Printing and photography borrowed the word because a wide page resembles a landscape view: the eye moves sideways across it. The term now means orientation alone, with no scenery involved.","whyCN":"印刷与摄影借用这个词，因为宽页面像一幅风景视野：视线横向扫过。这个术语如今只指方向，与景色无关。"},{"no":"06","title":"Landscape design","titleCN":"景观设计","definition":"the planned shaping of gardens, parks, and grounds for use and appearance","definitionCN":"为使用与外观而对花园、公园与场地进行的规划性塑造","example":"The landscape of the campus was redesigned last year.","exampleCN":"校园的景观去年被重新设计。","why":"Gardening adopted the word in the eighteenth century, when improvers began shaping views rather than merely planting. Landscape became both the object seen and the act of arranging it.","whyCN":"园艺在 18 世纪采用这个词，当时造园者开始塑造视野，而不只是种植。landscape 由此既指被看见的对象，也指安排它的行为。"},{"no":"07","title":"Cultural landscape","titleCN":"文化景观","definition":"a landscape shaped by human activity and carrying the marks of a community's history","definitionCN":"由人类活动塑造、带有群体历史印记的景观","example":"Rice terraces are a cultural landscape maintained for centuries.","exampleCN":"梯田是维护了数百年的文化景观。","why":"Heritage studies use the term to reject the split between nature and culture: a landscape is co-produced by people and place. The word then carries a claim about who made what we see.","whyCN":"遗产研究用这个术语来否定自然与文化的截然二分：景观由人与地方共同生产。这个词由此承载一个主张：我们所见的景象是谁造成的。"},{"no":"08","title":"The current overall situation","titleCN":"当前总体形势","definition":"the general state of affairs that someone surveys before acting","definitionCN":"某人在行动前所审视的总体状况","example":"Before launching the product, they studied the regulatory landscape.","exampleCN":"在推出产品之前，他们研究了监管形势。","why":"This sense generalises the spatial metaphor to any field: the landscape is what you see when you step back. It implies a survey before a decision, not a detailed analysis of one part.","whyCN":"这个义项把空间比喻推广到任何领域：景观是你退后一步看到的东西。它暗示决策前的总体巡视，而不是对某一局部的细致分析。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Landscape is a sixteenth-century borrowing from Dutch landschap, land plus -schap (state, condition), cognate with English -ship. It entered English first as a painting term and later spread to geography, gardening, and figurative usage.","cn":"landscape 是 16 世纪从荷兰语 landschap 借来的词，由 land 加 -schap（状态、状况）构成，与英语 -ship 同源。它先作为绘画术语进入英语，后来扩展到地理、园艺与比喻用法。"},"items":[{"era":"DUTCH / GERMANIC","en":"Dutch landschap combined land with -schap, a suffix of condition or collection, related to English -ship. The word meant 'the condition of the land' or 'a region', not yet a picture.","cn":"荷兰语 landschap 把 land 与表示状况或集合的后缀 -schap 结合，后者与英语 -ship 相关。该词意为“土地的状况”或“一片地区”，当时还不是画。"},{"era":"16C. ENGLISH","en":"English borrowed landscape in the sixteenth century as a term for a painting of scenery, alongside the older variant landskip. The artistic sense came first in English usage.","cn":"英语在 16 世纪借入 landscape，作为描绘景色的绘画术语，同时还有较早的变体 landskip。在英语用法中，艺术义最先出现。"},{"era":"17C.–18C. GARDENING","en":"Landscape gardening made the word active: to landscape a park was to arrange its views. The noun and the verb then grew together.","cn":"景观造园使这个词变为主动：landscape a park 意为安排它的视野。名词与动词由此一起生长。"},{"era":"19C. GEOGRAPHY","en":"Geography adopted landscape as a technical term for the visible form of a region, studied through maps and fieldwork. Physical and cultural landscapes were distinguished.","cn":"地理学采用 landscape 作为区域可见形态的技术术语，通过地图与野外工作研究。自然景观与文化景观被区分开来。"},{"era":"20C. FIGURATIVE USE","en":"Business, politics, and journalism extended the word to any field of activity, producing phrases such as 'the competitive landscape'. The spatial metaphor became a standard way to describe strategy.","cn":"商业、政治与新闻把这个词扩展到任何活动领域，产生 the competitive landscape 等说法。空间比喻成为描述战略的标准方式。"},{"era":"20C. PRINTING","en":"Printing and photography borrowed landscape for a page wider than it is tall, because such a page resembles a wide view. The term now names orientation alone.","cn":"印刷与摄影借用 landscape 指宽大于高的页面，因为这样的页面像一幅宽视野。这个术语如今只命名方向。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates words sharing the -scape suffix or the land element but built on different bases; the near-meaning group separates scenery, terrain, and view.","cn":"形近组区分共享 -scape 后缀或 land 成分但基词不同的词；近义组区分 scenery、terrain 与 view。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"seascape","ipa":"/ˈsiːskeɪp/","tag":"same -scape, different base","definition":"a view or picture of the sea. It is a modern formation on the model of landscape, replacing land with sea.","definitionCN":"海景或海景画。它是仿 landscape 构成的现代词，把 land 换成 sea。"},{"word":"scapegoat","ipa":"/ˈskeɪpɡəʊt/","tag":"different root: escape + goat","definition":"someone blamed for others' faults. The scape here comes from escape, not from landscape's -schap; the resemblance is accidental.","definitionCN":"替他人受责的人。这里的 scape 来自 escape，而非 landscape 的 -schap；相似纯属偶然。"},{"word":"landslide","ipa":"/ˈlændslaɪd/","tag":"same land, different second element","definition":"the sliding down of earth or rock, or an overwhelming election victory. It joins land with slide, with no sense of scenery.","definitionCN":"土石滑落，或压倒性的选举胜利。它把 land 与 slide 结合，与景色无关。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"scenery","ipa":"/ˈsiːnəri/","tag":"visual pleasure","definition":"the general appearance of a place, especially when attractive. It is uncountable and evaluative; landscape can be neutral and countable.","definitionCN":"一个地方的整体外观，尤指宜人时。它不可数且带评价；landscape 可中性、可数。"},{"word":"terrain","ipa":"/təˈreɪn/","tag":"physical ground","definition":"the physical surface of land, especially as it affects movement. It stresses ground conditions, while landscape includes what is seen.","definitionCN":"土地的物理表面，尤指影响行进时。它强调地面条件，而 landscape 包含所见之物。"},{"word":"view","ipa":"/vjuː/","tag":"from a point","definition":"what can be seen from a particular place. It depends on the observer's position; a landscape exists as a region, whether or not anyone is looking.","definitionCN":"从某一地点能看到的东西。它取决于观察者的位置；landscape 作为区域存在，无论是否有人在看。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real associations: Dutch landschap, the -ship suffix, the painting term of the sixteenth century, and the modern phrase political landscape.","cn":"真实联想：荷兰语 landschap、-ship 后缀、16 世纪的绘画术语，以及现代说法 political landscape。"},"normal":[{"en":"land + -schap (the same suffix as -ship): landscape is 'the condition of the land'.","cn":"land + -schap（与 -ship 同源的后缀）：landscape 就是“土地的状况”。"},{"en":"It entered English as a painting word, which is why a landscape can be a picture as well as a place.","cn":"它作为绘画词进入英语，所以 landscape 既可是地方，也可是画。"},{"en":"A wide page is printed in landscape because it looks like a wide view.","cn":"宽页面以横向打印，因为它看起来像一幅宽视野。"},{"en":"'Political landscape' treats parties as hills occupying positions in a view.","cn":"political landscape 把政党当作占据视野中位置的山丘。"},{"en":"seascape and cityscape are modern copies of the same pattern.","cn":"seascape 与 cityscape 是同一模式的现代仿造词。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The suffix means condition, not picture: the word is about how land stands, and the picture is a later use.","cn":"后缀意为状况，而非图画：这个词关乎土地处于何种状态，图画是后来的用法。"},{"en":"Every figurative landscape invites you to step back — the word always implies a viewing distance.","cn":"每一个比喻性的 landscape 都邀请你退后一步——这个词总暗示一段观看距离。"},{"en":"A cultural landscape denies the split between nature and human history: what you see was co-produced.","cn":"文化景观否定自然与人类历史的二分：你所见的是共同生产的。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The volcanic landscape attracts hikers from around the world.","cn":"这片火山地貌吸引着世界各地的徒步者。"},{"en":"The election reshaped the political landscape of the country.","cn":"这次选举重塑了该国的政治格局。"},{"en":"The map is printed in landscape so that the coastline fits on one page.","cn":"地图以横向版式印制，好让海岸线容纳在一页内。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“兰德斯给普”——荷兰的兰德斯（Land）把土地的样子“给”了出来 → landscape 风景、景观","word":"landscape"},"root":"荷兰语 landschap = land（土地）+ -schap（状态、状况，与英语 -ship 同源）；字面义“土地的状况”，核心是“从远处看到的一片土地的形态与格局”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of landscape all describe a wide arrangement seen as a whole: terrain, a painting, an ecological system, a field of competition, a page, a designed garden, a human-shaped heritage, and the current situation. The word always implies a viewing distance.","cn":"landscape 的八个义项都描述被当作整体看待的宽广布局：地貌、绘画、生态系统、竞争场域、页面、设计的园林、人塑造的遗产，以及当前形势。这个词总暗示一段观看距离。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a high vantage point where fields, a river, and roads compose one picture.","cn":"核心意象：一处高处的视点，田野、河流与道路组成一幅画。"},"chain":["LAND","SURFACE","WIDE VIEW","COMPOSITION","PATTERN","SITUATION"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S3","en":"NATURE: terrain and ecological systems are landscapes as regions, not merely as views.","cn":"自然：地貌与生态系统作为区域性的景观，而不只是视野。"},{"senses":"S2 · S6","en":"ART AND DESIGN: painting and garden-making both arrange what will be seen.","cn":"艺术与设计：绘画与造园都在安排将被看到的东西。"},{"senses":"S4 · S8","en":"SITUATION: fields of activity are surveyed from above and described as layouts.","cn":"形势：活动领域被从高处巡视，并被描述为布局。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"FORMAT: a wide page borrows the shape of a wide view.","cn":"版式：宽页面借用了宽视野的形状。"},{"senses":"S7","en":"HERITAGE: a cultural landscape denies the split between nature and human history.","cn":"遗产：文化景观否定自然与人类历史的二分。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Landscape is Dutch landschap, land + -schap, cognate with English -ship. The suffix has become productive in English: seascape, cityscape, and moonscape are modern coinages on the same pattern.","cn":"landscape 是荷兰语 landschap，由 land + -schap 构成，与英语 -ship 同源。这个后缀在英语中变得能产：seascape、cityscape、moonscape 都是按同一模式造的现代词。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Landscape has no Latin root: it is a Germanic compound of land and -schap. The nearest Latin relatives in English vocabulary are terra 'land' and campus 'field', which supply terrain and campus, but they are not etymological relatives.","cn":"landscape 没有拉丁词根：它是 land 与 -schap 的日耳曼语复合词。英语词汇中最近的拉丁亲属是 terra“土地”与 campus“田野”，它们提供 terrain 与 campus，但并非词源亲属。"},"items":[{"word":"landscape","structure":"Dutch landschap = land + -schap","meaning":"the visible form of a region; a picture of it","meaningCN":"景观；风景；风景画（land + -schap）","example":"The landscape changed after the flood.","exampleCN":"洪水之后地貌改变了。"},{"word":"landscaped","structure":"landscape + -ed","meaning":"arranged for appearance","meaningCN":"经景观设计的（-ed 构成形容词）","example":"The hotel has landscaped gardens.","exampleCN":"酒店有经过设计的园林。"},{"word":"landscaping","structure":"landscape + -ing","meaning":"the work of shaping grounds","meaningCN":"景观布置；造景（-ing 构成名词）","example":"Landscaping raised the property's value.","exampleCN":"景观布置提升了房产价值。"},{"word":"landscaper","structure":"landscape + -er","meaning":"one who designs grounds","meaningCN":"景观设计师；园林工（-er 表施动者）","example":"The landscaper planted native grasses.","exampleCN":"景观设计师种下本地草类。"},{"word":"seascape","structure":"sea + -scape (by analogy with landscape)","meaning":"a view or picture of the sea","meaningCN":"海景；海景画（sea + -scape）","example":"The gallery hangs mostly seascapes.","exampleCN":"画廊主要挂海景画。"},{"word":"cityscape","structure":"city + -scape","meaning":"the visual character of a city","meaningCN":"城市景观（city + -scape）","example":"The cityscape is dominated by glass towers.","exampleCN":"城市景观以玻璃塔楼为主。"},{"word":"moonscape","structure":"moon + -scape","meaning":"a barren, cratered landscape","meaningCN":"月球表面景观；荒凉地貌（moon + -scape）","example":"The mining site resembled a moonscape.","exampleCN":"矿区看起来像月球表面。"},{"word":"land","structure":"Old English land","meaning":"the solid surface of the earth","meaningCN":"土地；陆地（古英语本族词）","example":"The land rises toward the hills.","exampleCN":"土地向山丘方向升高。"},{"word":"landskip","structure":"older English variant of landscape","meaning":"a landscape painting (archaic)","meaningCN":"风景画（古旧变体，今已罕用）","example":"The inventory lists two landskips.","exampleCN":"清单上列有两幅风景画。"}],"latinEntries":[]}}]);
